ABILITY_ICE_STORM_NAME|Ice Storm
ABILITY_ICE_STORM_SUMMARY|Drops a storm of ice over a radius 2 area. Combatants take 1d10 bludgeoning damage and 2d8 cold damage. There is no saving throw. Wet ground and water freeze.
ABILITY_ICE_STORM_SHORT_SUMMARY|Radius 2 ice; no save.
CLASS_ACTION_PRIMORDIAL_BEAM_SUMMARY|Channel a pure arcane beam, spending HP and MP each pulse.
CLASS_ACTION_PRIMORDIAL_BEAM_SHORT_SUMMARY|Channel a pure arcane beam.
ITEM_LANTERN_DESC|A hooded travel lantern with a shuttered face and soot-blackened vents. Equip and light it to illuminate dark areas; refill it with oil flasks.
ITEM_OIL_FLASK_DESC|A stoppered flask of lamp oil. Use it to refill an equipped lantern, or throw it to splash flammable oil across a tile.
ITEM_BLACKGLASS_HEAVY_CROSSBOW_NAME|blackglass heavy crossbow
ITEM_BLACKGLASS_HEAVY_CROSSBOW_DESC|A heavy blackglass crossbow with a reinforced steel winch and a narrow dark channel. Pierce: critical hits deal 50% more damage.
ITEM_BLACKGLASS_FOCUS_RING_NAME|blackglass focus ring
ITEM_BLACKGLASS_FOCUS_RING_DESC|A narrow blackglass ring with a flat lens set over the knuckle. It grants +2 DEF, +1 ARM, +1 arcane spell attack, and is indestructible.
ITEM_BLACKGLASS_FOCUS_RING_UNIDENTIFIED_NAME|ring
ITEM_BLACKGLASS_FOCUS_RING_UNIDENTIFIED_DESC|Unidentified jewelry can hide blessings, curses, or other magic beneath plain metalwork.
ITEM_TORN_HIDE_NAME|torn hide
ITEM_TORN_HIDE_DESC|A ragged strip of hide cut loose from a carcass. It is only fit for salvage.
ITEM_CHIPPED_FANG_NAME|chipped fang
ITEM_CHIPPED_FANG_DESC|A broken fang with the root still rough. Buyers count it as creature salvage.
ITEM_SPLIT_CLAW_NAME|split claw
ITEM_SPLIT_CLAW_DESC|A cracked claw too damaged for any careful work, but still worth a little.
ITEM_CRACKED_TUSK_NAME|cracked tusk
ITEM_CRACKED_TUSK_DESC|A tusk split along one side. It has value as raw bone and nothing more.
ITEM_MATTED_PELT_NAME|matted pelt
ITEM_MATTED_PELT_DESC|A dirty pelt with patches still workable for a patient tanner.
ITEM_LONG_FANG_NAME|long fang
ITEM_LONG_FANG_DESC|A long predator fang, dulled at the tip but still worth saving.
ITEM_HEAVY_CLAW_NAME|heavy claw
ITEM_HEAVY_CLAW_DESC|A thick claw from a large beast, chipped but still valuable as hard scrap.
ITEM_BROKEN_HORN_NAME|broken horn
ITEM_BROKEN_HORN_DESC|A snapped horn with a jagged base. It is salvage, not a trophy.
ITEM_THICK_HIDE_NAME|thick hide
ITEM_THICK_HIDE_DESC|A heavy patch of hide too scarred for fine leather but worth trade.
ITEM_GREAT_FANG_NAME|great fang
ITEM_GREAT_FANG_DESC|A large fang with old cracks along the enamel.
ITEM_HEAVY_TUSK_NAME|heavy tusk
ITEM_HEAVY_TUSK_DESC|A heavy tusk too damaged for display, but valuable as dense bone.
ITEM_BLACK_CLAW_NAME|black claw
ITEM_BLACK_CLAW_DESC|A dark, hard claw broken from a dangerous creature.
ITEM_RAT_TAIL_NAME|rat tail
ITEM_RAT_TAIL_DESC|A stringy vermin tail tied off for bounty or salvage buyers.
ITEM_BAT_WING_NAME|bat wing
ITEM_BAT_WING_DESC|A torn leathery wing, light enough to bundle for trade.
ITEM_BRITTLE_SHELL_NAME|brittle shell
ITEM_BRITTLE_SHELL_DESC|A cracked shell plate that flakes at the edges.
ITEM_TORN_WING_NAME|torn wing
ITEM_TORN_WING_DESC|A torn insect wing, dried stiff and useful only as odd salvage.
ITEM_VENOM_GLAND_NAME|venom gland
ITEM_VENOM_GLAND_DESC|A drained venom gland wrapped so it does not leak.
ITEM_CHITIN_PLATE_NAME|chitin plate
ITEM_CHITIN_PLATE_DESC|A scratched plate of chitin from a large vermin shell.
ITEM_TANGLED_SILK_NAME|tangled silk
ITEM_TANGLED_SILK_DESC|A knotted wad of strong silk too fouled for clean work.
ITEM_BARBED_LEG_NAME|barbed leg
ITEM_BARBED_LEG_DESC|A stiff, barbed insect leg clipped down for salvage.
ITEM_TORN_SCALE_NAME|torn scale
ITEM_TORN_SCALE_DESC|A torn scale plate with ragged hide still attached.
ITEM_CLOUDED_EYE_NAME|clouded eye
ITEM_CLOUDED_EYE_DESC|A cloudy preserved eye sealed before it can spoil.
ITEM_CHIPPED_TOOTH_NAME|chipped tooth
ITEM_CHIPPED_TOOTH_DESC|A chipped reptile tooth with a cracked root.
ITEM_SPLIT_HIDE_NAME|split hide
ITEM_SPLIT_HIDE_DESC|A split strip of hide, rough but still tradeable.
ITEM_HARD_SCALE_NAME|hard scale
ITEM_HARD_SCALE_DESC|A tough scale plate, scratched but not useless.
ITEM_LONG_TOOTH_NAME|long tooth
ITEM_LONG_TOOTH_DESC|A long reptile tooth, dulled from use.
ITEM_TOUGH_HIDE_NAME|tough hide
ITEM_TOUGH_HIDE_DESC|A thick hide strip that still has some value to tanners.
ITEM_YELLOWED_EYE_NAME|yellowed eye
ITEM_YELLOWED_EYE_DESC|A preserved yellow eye sealed in waxed cloth.
ITEM_CRACKED_DRAKE_SCALE_NAME|cracked drake scale
ITEM_CRACKED_DRAKE_SCALE_DESC|A hard drake scale split through the center.
ITEM_DRAKE_TOOTH_NAME|drake tooth
ITEM_DRAKE_TOOTH_DESC|A drake tooth with a rough, damaged edge.
ITEM_HEAVY_DRAKE_SCALE_NAME|heavy drake scale
ITEM_HEAVY_DRAKE_SCALE_DESC|A heavy scale plate from a powerful drake, scarred but valuable.
ITEM_LONG_DRAKE_TOOTH_NAME|long drake tooth
ITEM_LONG_DRAKE_TOOTH_DESC|A long drake tooth with old cracks near the base.
ITEM_SPLINTERED_DRAGONBONE_NAME|splintered dragonbone
ITEM_SPLINTERED_DRAGONBONE_DESC|A dense splinter of dragonbone, broken but still prized.
ITEM_BENT_BUCKLE_NAME|bent buckle
ITEM_BENT_BUCKLE_DESC|A bent buckle that can no longer hold a strap.
ITEM_CRACKED_PIPE_NAME|cracked pipe
ITEM_CRACKED_PIPE_DESC|A clay pipe cracked through the bowl.
ITEM_TORN_POUCH_NAME|torn pouch
ITEM_TORN_POUCH_DESC|A little pouch split open at the seam.
ITEM_BENT_BUTTON_NAME|bent button
ITEM_BENT_BUTTON_DESC|A cheap metal button bent out of shape.
ITEM_BURNT_SPOON_NAME|burnt spoon
ITEM_BURNT_SPOON_DESC|A smoke-blackened spoon too warped for table use.
ITEM_CRACKED_BOWL_NAME|cracked bowl
ITEM_CRACKED_BOWL_DESC|A cracked bowl held together by grime and luck.
ITEM_TORN_STRAP_NAME|torn strap
ITEM_TORN_STRAP_DESC|A torn leather strap with a ragged buckle hole.
ITEM_BENT_TIN_CUP_NAME|bent tin cup
ITEM_BENT_TIN_CUP_DESC|A dented tin cup that will not sit flat.
ITEM_RUSTED_SPUR_NAME|rusted spur
ITEM_RUSTED_SPUR_DESC|A single rusted spur torn from an old boot.
ITEM_DENTED_BADGE_NAME|dented badge
ITEM_DENTED_BADGE_DESC|A dented badge with its mark scraped almost clean.
ITEM_SPLIT_COIN_PURSE_NAME|split coin purse
ITEM_SPLIT_COIN_PURSE_DESC|A coin purse split at the bottom, empty and useless except as scrap.
ITEM_BROKEN_COMB_NAME|broken comb
ITEM_BROKEN_COMB_DESC|A comb with half its teeth snapped away.
ITEM_DENTED_SNUFF_TIN_NAME|dented snuff tin
ITEM_DENTED_SNUFF_TIN_DESC|A dented tin with a lid that no longer shuts.
ITEM_BROKEN_KNIFE_SHEATH_NAME|broken knife sheath
ITEM_BROKEN_KNIFE_SHEATH_DESC|A split sheath that would drop any blade put inside it.
ITEM_BENT_IRON_BUCKLE_NAME|bent iron buckle
ITEM_BENT_IRON_BUCKLE_DESC|A heavy iron buckle bent past use.
ITEM_BONE_SPLINTER_NAME|bone splinter
ITEM_BONE_SPLINTER_DESC|A sharp splinter of old bone, too small for any use but salvage.
ITEM_TWISTED_WIRE_NAME|twisted wire
ITEM_TWISTED_WIRE_DESC|A short twist of wire bent out of shape.
ITEM_FRAYED_CORD_NAME|frayed cord
ITEM_FRAYED_CORD_DESC|A length of cord frayed too badly to trust.
ITEM_BENT_NAIL_NAME|bent nail
ITEM_BENT_NAIL_DESC|A bent nail pulled from broken wood.
ITEM_SPLIT_HORN_NAME|split horn
ITEM_SPLIT_HORN_DESC|A split horn with a jagged break through the middle.
ITEM_RUSTED_CHAIN_LINK_NAME|rusted chain link
ITEM_RUSTED_CHAIN_LINK_DESC|A rusted chain link broken from a larger length.
ITEM_CHIPPED_AXE_HEAD_NAME|chipped axe head
ITEM_CHIPPED_AXE_HEAD_DESC|An axe head chipped badly enough to be scrap.
ITEM_BLACKENED_BUCKLE_NAME|blackened buckle
ITEM_BLACKENED_BUCKLE_DESC|A fire-blackened buckle warped by heat.
ITEM_RUSTED_HINGE_NAME|rusted hinge
ITEM_RUSTED_HINGE_DESC|A rusted hinge that still has some salvage value.
ITEM_BROKEN_HANDLE_NAME|broken handle
ITEM_BROKEN_HANDLE_DESC|A broken handle from a tool, door, or old box.
ITEM_TORN_SACK_NAME|torn sack
ITEM_TORN_SACK_DESC|A coarse sack torn open along one side.
ITEM_ANCIENT_RIVET_NAME|ancient rivet
ITEM_ANCIENT_RIVET_DESC|A heavy old rivet pulled from ruined machinery or forgotten gates.
ITEM_BROKEN_LAMP_FRAME_NAME|broken lamp frame
ITEM_BROKEN_LAMP_FRAME_DESC|A bent lamp frame with the glass and burner missing.
ITEM_BENT_GOBLET_NAME|bent goblet
ITEM_BENT_GOBLET_DESC|A metal goblet crushed badly enough that it cannot hold drink.
ITEM_DENTED_PAN_NAME|dented pan
ITEM_DENTED_PAN_DESC|A pan dented through the base and useless for cooking.
ITEM_SPLIT_SILVER_SPOON_NAME|split silver spoon
ITEM_SPLIT_SILVER_SPOON_DESC|A silver spoon split down the bowl, valuable only as metal.
ITEM_CRACKED_MIRROR_SHARD_NAME|cracked mirror shard
ITEM_CRACKED_MIRROR_SHARD_DESC|A mirror shard with cracks through the silvering.
ITEM_TARNISHED_CUP_NAME|tarnished cup
ITEM_TARNISHED_CUP_DESC|A tarnished cup with a split lip and a dented base.
ITEM_BENT_BRASS_PLATE_NAME|bent brass plate
ITEM_BENT_BRASS_PLATE_DESC|A brass plate bent out of shape and scratched across the face.
ITEM_BROKEN_COMPASS_NAME|broken compass
ITEM_BROKEN_COMPASS_DESC|A sea compass with a cracked glass face and a loose, useless needle.
ITEM_CRACKED_BONE_NAME|cracked bone
ITEM_CRACKED_BONE_DESC|A cracked bone with no mark or power to it.
ITEM_SPLIT_COFFIN_NAIL_NAME|split coffin nail
ITEM_SPLIT_COFFIN_NAIL_DESC|A split coffin nail, rusted from damp wood.
ITEM_BROKEN_CANDLE_STUB_NAME|broken candle stub
ITEM_BROKEN_CANDLE_STUB_DESC|A snapped candle stub too dirty to burn cleanly.
ITEM_BRITTLE_BONE_SHARD_NAME|brittle bone shard
ITEM_BRITTLE_BONE_SHARD_DESC|A brittle shard of bone that crumbles at the edges.
ITEM_BENT_COFFIN_HANDLE_NAME|bent coffin handle
ITEM_BENT_COFFIN_HANDLE_DESC|A coffin handle bent away from its mounting plate.
ITEM_CRACKED_BURIAL_PLATE_NAME|cracked burial plate
ITEM_CRACKED_BURIAL_PLATE_DESC|A burial plate cracked through the name and date.
ITEM_VETHRIN_S_SEALED_NOTE_NAME|vethrin's sealed note
ITEM_VETHRIN_S_SEALED_NOTE_DESC|A folded note sealed with cheap wax and marked for a Reedwater fisherman.
ITEM_ASH_TOWER_DRAKE_SCALE_NAME|ash tower drake scale
ITEM_ASH_TOWER_DRAKE_SCALE_DESC|A scorched drake scale kept as proof for Velra's Ash Tower work.
UI_ACTION_EXAMINE_ALL|examine all
ITEM_VENDOR_EXAMINE_ALL_CONFIRM|Examine all {0} items for {1}g?
ITEM_VENDOR_EXAMINE_ALL_NONE|There are no items here that this specialist can examine.
