FRONTEND_INTRO_STORY_01||opening story paragraph shown after character creation|You came east because of the blackglass star amulet.
FRONTEND_INTRO_STORY_02||opening story paragraph shown after character creation|Your family kept it as an old heirloom. Months ago it started warming against your skin and ruining your sleep. No one at home knew why.
FRONTEND_INTRO_STORY_03||opening story paragraph shown after character creation|At the ports, the same rumors kept coming up: the Sundering Scar, blackglass in old ruins, missing caravans, and dragons seen far inland.
FRONTEND_INTRO_STORY_04||opening story paragraph shown after character creation|You paid for passage to Reedwater Docks. From there, the road north leads to Havenford and the first people who might know more.
FRONTEND_INTRO_STORY_05||opening story paragraph shown after character creation|The crossing nearly killed you. A storm hit before dawn, tore rigging loose, and drove water over the deck.
FRONTEND_INTRO_STORY_06||opening story paragraph shown after character creation|Captain Thauld and his crew kept the boat afloat with wet rope, cracked hands, and shouted orders.
FRONTEND_INTRO_STORY_07||opening story paragraph shown after character creation|You came ashore at Reedwater Docks half frozen, salt-sick, and still wearing the amulet under your shirt.
FRONTEND_INTRO_STORY_08||opening story paragraph shown after character creation|Time to give thanks to the captain, take a rest at the inn, and then take the road out to Havenford.
FRONTEND_INTRO_STORY_09||opening story paragraph shown after character creation|Someone there may know what the amulet is, and why dragon sightings are being reported inland.
FRONTEND_STORMWRECK_STORY_01||tutorial departure story beat|The storm hit before dawn. Wind tore the rigging loose and drove black water over the deck.
FRONTEND_STORMWRECK_STORY_02||tutorial departure story beat|Thauld kept the boat afloat until it struck a reef. You came to on a narrow island with wreckage washing in behind you.
FRONTEND_STORMWRECK_STORY_03||tutorial departure story beat|The captain is signaling from a sheltered cove across the island. Reach him before the storm turns again.
CREATION_MODE_ADVENTURE_NAME|20|new-game mode option name|Adventure
CREATION_MODE_ADVENTURE_SUMMARY_A|72|new-game mode option summary|A standard adventure-style play through where you can save the game
CREATION_MODE_ADVENTURE_SUMMARY_B|88|new-game mode option summary|by sleeping at an inn or camping, and reload from there if you die.
CREATION_MODE_ADVENTURE_SUMMARY_C|40|new-game mode option summary|Recommended for new players.
CREATION_MODE_ADVENTUREPARTY_NAME|24|new-game mode option name|Party Mode
CREATION_MODE_ADVENTUREPARTY_SUMMARY_A|80|new-game mode option summary|Adventure rules with a party of up to three independent adventurers.
CREATION_MODE_ADVENTUREPARTY_SUMMARY_B|80|new-game mode option summary|Switch between them while the others follow and fight on their own.
CREATION_MODE_ADVENTUREPARTY_SUMMARY_C|64|new-game mode option summary|Experimental and deliberately unbalanced; intended for fun.
CREATION_MODE_ROGUELIKE_NAME|20|new-game mode option name|Roguelike
CREATION_MODE_ROGUELIKE_SUMMARY_A|112|new-game mode option summary|A traditional roguelike playthrough, with no reloading upon death. Beating the game is a monumental achievement.
CREATION_MODE_ROGUELIKE_SUMMARY_B|64|new-game mode option summary|Saves resume the same run only. Death is permanent.
CREATION_MODE_ROGUELIKE_SUMMARY_C|40|new-game mode option summary|Not recommended for new players.
CREATION_DIFFICULTY_RELAXED_NAME|20|new-game difficulty option name|Relaxed
CREATION_DIFFICULTY_RELAXED_SUMMARY_A|104|new-game difficulty option summary|The difficulty is reduced slightly across the board, making the run a bit less punishing overall.
CREATION_DIFFICULTY_RELAXED_SUMMARY_B|40|new-game difficulty option summary|Recommended for new players.
CREATION_DIFFICULTY_RELAXED_SUMMARY_C|40|new-game difficulty option summary|A gentler introduction to the systems.
CREATION_DIFFICULTY_STANDARD_NAME|20|new-game difficulty option name|Standard
CREATION_DIFFICULTY_STANDARD_SUMMARY_A|80|new-game difficulty option summary|The standard difficulty setting with no special modifiers. It is difficult.
CREATION_DIFFICULTY_STANDARD_SUMMARY_B|48|new-game difficulty option summary|No special modifiers or adjustments.
CREATION_DIFFICULTY_STANDARD_SUMMARY_C|40|new-game difficulty option summary|The default experience.
CREATION_DIFFICULTY_BRUTAL_NAME|20|new-game difficulty option name|Brutal
CREATION_DIFFICULTY_BRUTAL_SUMMARY_A|112|new-game difficulty option summary|The standard difficulty rules but with stronger enemies appearing earlier. Better loot if you can survive it.
CREATION_DIFFICULTY_BRUTAL_SUMMARY_B|48|new-game difficulty option summary|Stronger enemies appear earlier than usual.
CREATION_DIFFICULTY_BRUTAL_SUMMARY_C|40|new-game difficulty option summary|For veterans seeking a challenge.
CREATION_START_PLAY_TUTORIAL_NAME|24|new-game tutorial option name|Play Tutorial
CREATION_START_PLAY_TUTORIAL_SUMMARY_A|88|new-game tutorial option summary|Start your adventure on the way to the dockside town to take the boat to Valoria.
CREATION_START_PLAY_TUTORIAL_SUMMARY_B|72|new-game tutorial option summary|Good for learning the essentials, and recommended for new players.
CREATION_START_PLAY_TUTORIAL_SUMMARY_C|48|new-game tutorial option summary|Introduces core mechanics and controls.
CREATION_START_SKIP_TUTORIAL_NAME|24|new-game tutorial option name|Skip Tutorial
CREATION_START_SKIP_TUTORIAL_SUMMARY_A|72|new-game tutorial option summary|Start as the boat arrives and jump straight into the open world.
CREATION_START_SKIP_TUTORIAL_SUMMARY_B|48|new-game tutorial option summary|Assumes familiarity with the interface.
CREATION_START_SKIP_TUTORIAL_SUMMARY_C|40|new-game tutorial option summary|No guidance or tutorial steps.
CREATION_SEX_MALE_NAME|16|new-game sex option name|Male
CREATION_SEX_MALE_SUMMARY_A|64|new-game sex option summary|Improved starting Strength rolls.
CREATION_SEX_MALE_SUMMARY_B|64|new-game sex option summary|Reduced starting Dexterity rolls.
CREATION_SEX_MALE_SUMMARY_C|48|new-game sex option summary|Armor burden thresholds are 10% higher.
CREATION_SEX_FEMALE_NAME|16|new-game sex option name|Female
CREATION_SEX_FEMALE_SUMMARY_A|64|new-game sex option summary|Improved starting Dexterity rolls.
CREATION_SEX_FEMALE_SUMMARY_B|64|new-game sex option summary|Reduced starting Strength rolls.
CREATION_SEX_FEMALE_SUMMARY_C|80|new-game sex option summary|Sickness duration and final fever damage are reduced by 20%.
RACE_HUMAN_SUMMARY_A|104|new-game race summary for Human|A common and adaptable people found across towns, roads, farms, armies, and frontier settlements.
RACE_HUMAN_SUMMARY_B|128|new-game race summary for Human|Starting skill: Presence. Bonuses: Spear training and +1 proficiency, 3 starting skill points, and extra points while leveling.
RACE_HUMAN_SUMMARY_C|72|new-game race summary for Human|Extra kit: 2 rations, a waterskin, and 2 random trail items.
RACE_DWARF_SUMMARY_A|112|new-game race summary for Dwarf|A sturdy people from old stoneholds and forge towns, known for endurance, craft, and deep-road tradition.
RACE_DWARF_SUMMARY_B|144|new-game race summary for Dwarf|Starting skill: Handiwork. Bonuses: +2 CON, -2 DEX, axe/crossbow/shield training and +1 proficiency, +1 Axe rank, secrets, faster healing.
RACE_DWARF_SUMMARY_C|64|new-game race summary for Dwarf|Extra kit: torches and rope for dark stone work.
RACE_ELF_SUMMARY_A|104|new-game race summary for Elf|A long-lived people from guarded woodland realms, skilled in archery, swordplay, and wilderness travel.
RACE_ELF_SUMMARY_B|144|new-game race summary for Elf|Starting skill: Survival. Bonuses: +2 DEX, -1 STR/CON, +1 vision, sleep/charm resist, bow/sword +1 proficiency and +2 ranks, +25% mana regen.
RACE_ELF_SUMMARY_C|72|new-game race summary for Elf|Extra kit: travel cloak, more arrows, and crossbow kits swap to bows.
RACE_HALF_ELF_SUMMARY_A|120|new-game race summary for Half-Elf|Half-elves share human and elven heritage, often living at the edge of both peoples rather than fully within either.
RACE_HALF_ELF_SUMMARY_B|144|new-game race summary for Half-Elf|Starting skill: Survival. Bonuses: faster skill points, sleep/charm resist, bow/sword +1 proficiency and +1 rank, +10% mana regen.
RACE_HALF_ELF_SUMMARY_C|72|new-game race summary for Half-Elf|Extra kit: a cloak and waterskin fit for mixed roads and long days.
RACE_HALFLING_SUMMARY_A|96|new-game race summary for Halfling|A small, quick-footed people known for stealth, sharp senses, slings, and practical survival.
RACE_HALFLING_SUMMARY_B|128|new-game race summary for Halfling|Starting skill: Stealth. Bonuses: +2 DEX, -2 STR, +1 DEF, Sling +1 proficiency and +2 ranks, +1 Luck, fear immunity, eats more.
RACE_HALFLING_SUMMARY_C|56|new-game race summary for Halfling|Extra kit: a sling pouch and extra trail food.
RACE_GNOME_SUMMARY_A|96|new-game race summary for Gnome|A clever and curious people skilled with tools, locks, devices, appraisal, and arcane study.
RACE_GNOME_SUMMARY_B|128|new-game race summary for Gnome|Starting skill: Appraisal. Bonuses: +1 DEX, +1 INT, -2 STR, cheaper spells, appraisal talent, +2 traps/locks/spellbooks.
RACE_GNOME_SUMMARY_C|64|new-game race summary for Gnome|Extra kit: lockpicks and lamp oil for fiddly work.
RACE_HALF_ORC_SUMMARY_A|88|new-game race summary for Half-Orc|Shunned in society for their orcish blood, half-orcs are tough and dangerous fighters.
RACE_HALF_ORC_SUMMARY_B|144|new-game race summary for Half-Orc|Starting skill: Athletics. Bonuses: +2 STR, +1 CON, -1 INT, -2 CHA, Polearm training and +1 proficiency, darkvision, corpse/ailment tolerance.
RACE_HALF_ORC_SUMMARY_C|64|new-game race summary for Half-Orc|Extra kit: a torch, bandage, and ration.
CLASS_FIGHTER_SUMMARY_A|96|new-game class summary for Fighter|A skilled warrior comfortable with all manner of weapons and armor, excelling in close combat.
CLASS_FIGHTER_SUMMARY_B|144|new-game class summary for Fighter|Class skill: Athletics. Trained: knives, axes, maces, flails, spears, staves, swords, polearms, bows, crossbows, slings, throwing, shields.
