CATALOG_LOCATION_DOCKS_SUMMARY|128|catalog location summary for Docks|Reedwater Docks is a storm-damaged landing at the eastern road's end.
CATALOG_LOCATION_DOCKS_DETAIL|224|catalog location detail for Docks|The area has timber piers, fish sheds, wet plank walks, boat traffic, and basic services for new travelers.
CATALOG_LOCATION_DOCKS_ENEMIES|128|catalog location commonly seen enemies for Docks|dockhands, fishers, smugglers
CATALOG_LOCATION_TIDEHOOK_DOCKS_SUMMARY|128|catalog location summary for TidehookDocks|Tidehook Docks is a small south-shore town built around skiffs, net sheds, and marsh traffic.
CATALOG_LOCATION_TIDEHOOK_DOCKS_DETAIL|224|catalog location detail for TidehookDocks|It has merchants, fishing gear, boat passage, and a spear rack for travelers crossing wet roads.
CATALOG_LOCATION_TIDEHOOK_DOCKS_ENEMIES|128|catalog location commonly seen enemies for TidehookDocks|fishers, traders, shorefolk
CATALOG_LOCATION_TRAVELLERS_REST_SUMMARY|128|catalog location summary for TravellersRest|Traveller's Rest is a remote road inn and waystation for tired travelers.
CATALOG_LOCATION_TRAVELLERS_REST_DETAIL|224|catalog location detail for TravellersRest|It has guest rooms, an outdoor drinking yard, a mixed-goods counter, and loose road gossip from people passing through.
CATALOG_LOCATION_TRAVELLERS_REST_ENEMIES|128|catalog location commonly seen enemies for TravellersRest|travellers, merchants
CATALOG_LOCATION_HAVENFORD_SUMMARY|128|catalog location summary for Havenford|Havenford is a frontier village with farms, a shrine, a forge, and a small elder's hall.
CATALOG_LOCATION_HAVENFORD_DETAIL|224|catalog location detail for Havenford|The village has raids and road trouble nearby, but it remains an early supply stop.
CATALOG_LOCATION_HAVENFORD_ENEMIES|128|catalog location commonly seen enemies for Havenford|villagers, drifters, elder's guards
CATALOG_LOCATION_RAT_CELLAR_SUMMARY|128|catalog location summary for RatCellar|Rat Cellar is a cramped dockside storage cellar below Reedwater.
CATALOG_LOCATION_RAT_CELLAR_DETAIL|224|catalog location detail for RatCellar|The rooms contain chewed grain sacks, broken planks, tight corners, and a large rat nest.
CATALOG_LOCATION_RAT_CELLAR_ENEMIES|128|catalog location commonly seen enemies for RatCellar|giant rats
CATALOG_LOCATION_BANDIT_CAMP_SUMMARY|128|catalog location summary for BanditCamp|Ragged Camp is a small bandit camp near the western tracks.
CATALOG_LOCATION_BANDIT_CAMP_DETAIL|224|catalog location detail for BanditCamp|It has bedrolls, cookfires, stolen supplies, rough barricades, and poorly organized guards.
CATALOG_LOCATION_BANDIT_CAMP_ENEMIES|128|catalog location commonly seen enemies for BanditCamp|bandits, cutthroats, enforcers
CATALOG_LOCATION_ROADSIDE_SHRINE_SUMMARY|128|catalog location summary for RoadsideShrine|Roadside Shrine is a cracked roadside chapel with a small undercroft beneath it.
CATALOG_LOCATION_ROADSIDE_SHRINE_DETAIL|224|catalog location detail for RoadsideShrine|The lower rooms are tight, partly ruined, and occupied by undead and cult intruders.
CATALOG_LOCATION_ROADSIDE_SHRINE_ENEMIES|128|catalog location commonly seen enemies for RoadsideShrine|skeletons, cultists, green slime, a ghost
CATALOG_LOCATION_GOBLIN_CAVE_SUMMARY|128|catalog location summary for GoblinCave|Goblin Cave is a cave hold in the eastern ridge.
CATALOG_LOCATION_GOBLIN_CAVE_DETAIL|224|catalog location detail for GoblinCave|The tunnels are narrow, cluttered with stolen scrap, and guarded by goblins with a few kobold allies.
CATALOG_LOCATION_GOBLIN_CAVE_ENEMIES|128|catalog location commonly seen enemies for GoblinCave|goblins, slingers, kobold archers
CATALOG_LOCATION_HAVENFORD_MINES_SUMMARY|128|catalog location summary for HavenfordMines|Havenford Mines is a small worked mine in the mountains east of Havenford.
CATALOG_LOCATION_HAVENFORD_MINES_DETAIL|224|catalog location detail for HavenfordMines|Its timbered rooms and stone corridors are blocked by boulders and occupied by kobolds, rats, and cave vermin.
CATALOG_LOCATION_HAVENFORD_MINES_ENEMIES|128|catalog location commonly seen enemies for HavenfordMines|kobolds, giant rats, cave spiders
CATALOG_LOCATION_ASH_TOWER_SUMMARY|128|catalog location summary for AshTower|Ash Tower is a burned tower ruin with collapsed floors and heat-damaged stone.
CATALOG_LOCATION_ASH_TOWER_DETAIL|224|catalog location detail for AshTower|Old fire wards and animated guardians patrol the rooms, making it a dangerous mid-road side tower.
CATALOG_LOCATION_ASH_TOWER_ENEMIES|128|catalog location commonly seen enemies for AshTower|lesser fire elementals, animated armor, flying swords
CATALOG_LOCATION_SUNKEN_CRYPT_SUMMARY|128|catalog location summary for SunkenCrypt|Sunken Crypt is a set of burial chambers that have settled into wet stone.
CATALOG_LOCATION_SUNKEN_CRYPT_DETAIL|224|catalog location detail for SunkenCrypt|Expect damp corridors, sealed tomb rooms, stagnant water, hidden side chambers, and undead around the deeper burials.
CATALOG_LOCATION_SUNKEN_CRYPT_ENEMIES|128|catalog location commonly seen enemies for SunkenCrypt|skeletons, slime, leeches, ghouls
CATALOG_LOCATION_STARFALL_BURROW_SUMMARY|128|catalog location summary for StarfallBurrow|Starfall Burrow is a cracked ridge breach with blackglass growth inside the stone.
CATALOG_LOCATION_STARFALL_BURROW_DETAIL|224|catalog location detail for StarfallBurrow|The route mixes natural breaks, root-choked passages, ruined chambers, and early blackglass creatures.
CATALOG_LOCATION_STARFALL_BURROW_ENEMIES|128|catalog location commonly seen enemies for StarfallBurrow|blackglass hounds, blackglass rats, young drakes
CATALOG_LOCATION_SOUTH_GATE_SUMMARY|128|catalog location summary for SouthGate|South Gate is the dwarven roadhead built into the mountain approach.
CATALOG_LOCATION_SOUTH_GATE_DETAIL|224|catalog location detail for SouthGate|It contains guarded supply rooms, bunks, a small forge, and the controlled entrance to the South Gate Tunnels.
CATALOG_LOCATION_SOUTH_GATE_ENEMIES|128|catalog location commonly seen enemies for SouthGate|dwarven guards, suppliers, road wardens
CATALOG_LOCATION_UNDERWAY_SUMMARY|128|catalog location summary for Underway|The Underway is the old dwarven road north from Stonecleft.
CATALOG_LOCATION_UNDERWAY_DETAIL|224|catalog location detail for Underway|South Gate Tunnels lead to Stonecleft; beyond the town, The Underway climbs through broad cut-stone roadways toward North Gate.
CATALOG_LOCATION_UNDERWAY_ENEMIES|128|catalog location commonly seen enemies for Underway|kobold warriors, spiders, rust monsters, drakes
CATALOG_LOCATION_HIGHMARK_SUMMARY|128|catalog location summary for Highmark|Highmark is a large human city with markets, gates, noble houses, and White Seal offices.
CATALOG_LOCATION_HIGHMARK_DETAIL|224|catalog location detail for Highmark|It serves as the main northern city hub for faction work, supplies, and later story progress.
CATALOG_LOCATION_HIGHMARK_ENEMIES|128|catalog location commonly seen enemies for Highmark|guards, canons, market folk
CATALOG_LOCATION_WHITE_SEAL_TOWER_SUMMARY|128|catalog location summary for WhiteSealTower|Tower of the White Seal is a beacon tower on the road above Highmark.
CATALOG_LOCATION_WHITE_SEAL_TOWER_DETAIL|224|catalog location detail for WhiteSealTower|The tower has ritual rooms, upper stairs, cult chaplains, animated guardians, and cold warding magic near the beacon site.
CATALOG_LOCATION_WHITE_SEAL_TOWER_ENEMIES|128|catalog location commonly seen enemies for WhiteSealTower|cult chaplains, helmed horrors, frost elementals
CATALOG_LOCATION_CAMP_KESTREL_SUMMARY|128|catalog location summary for CampKestrel|Camp Kestrel is a forward Silver Lance camp near the Great Scar.
CATALOG_LOCATION_CAMP_KESTREL_DETAIL|224|catalog location detail for CampKestrel|The camp has tents, engineers, guards, supply stores, and access to the first deeper Scar operations.
CATALOG_LOCATION_CAMP_KESTREL_ENEMIES|128|catalog location commonly seen enemies for CampKestrel|lancers, engineers, camp guards
CATALOG_LOCATION_WHITE_VAULT_SUMMARY|128|catalog location summary for WhiteVault|White Vault is an old sealed complex beneath Highmark.
CATALOG_LOCATION_WHITE_VAULT_DETAIL|224|catalog location detail for WhiteVault|It descends through formal south-to-north seal halls, side reliquaries, locked vault rooms, undead defenders, and a guarded inner chamber.
CATALOG_LOCATION_WHITE_VAULT_ENEMIES|128|catalog location commonly seen enemies for WhiteVault|skeleton knights, wights, greater drake
CATALOG_LOCATION_GLASSROOT_HOLLOW_SUMMARY|128|catalog location summary for GlassrootHollow|Glassroot Hollow is a hidden elven hollow damaged by blackglass roots.
CATALOG_LOCATION_GLASSROOT_HOLLOW_DETAIL|224|catalog location detail for GlassrootHollow|The hollow opens as an outdoor grove, then descends into organic stone/root chambers where blackglass growth thickens by floor.
CATALOG_LOCATION_GLASSROOT_HOLLOW_ENEMIES|128|catalog location commonly seen enemies for GlassrootHollow|wolf spiders, ettercaps, owlbears, treants, drakes
CATALOG_LOCATION_TELWYND_SUMMARY|128|catalog location summary for Telwynd|Telwynd is a hidden elven archive and protected waystation.
CATALOG_LOCATION_TELWYND_DETAIL|224|catalog location detail for Telwynd|It has lamplit ward-roads, garden pools, outdoor work clearings, and a northern gate circle for later hidden travel.
CATALOG_LOCATION_TELWYND_ENEMIES|128|catalog location commonly seen enemies for Telwynd|veilwardens, archivists, envoys
CATALOG_LOCATION_ISTARIAN_TUNNELS_SUMMARY|128|catalog location summary for IstarianTunnels|Istarian Tunnels are the old imperial access works below Camp Kestrel.
CATALOG_LOCATION_ISTARIAN_TUNNELS_DETAIL|224|catalog location detail for IstarianTunnels|The route mixes stone service tunnels, buried roadwork, cave breaks, and light blackglass traces before the Ancient Dwarven Gate.
CATALOG_LOCATION_ISTARIAN_TUNNELS_ENEMIES|128|catalog location commonly seen enemies for IstarianTunnels|deep rats, gray dwarves, blackglass hounds, young drakes
CATALOG_LOCATION_ELVEN_PASSAGEWAYS_SUMMARY|128|catalog location summary for ElvenPassageways|Elven Passageways are hidden root roads that bypass the worst ruined route.
CATALOG_LOCATION_ELVEN_PASSAGEWAYS_DETAIL|224|catalog location detail for ElvenPassageways|They are winding organic passages with grove clusters, living roots, poison hazards, and old elven wardwork.
CATALOG_LOCATION_ELVEN_PASSAGEWAYS_ENEMIES|128|catalog location commonly seen enemies for ElvenPassageways|treants, ettercaps, slimes, puddings, ghouls
CATALOG_LOCATION_ISTARIAN_SANCTUM_SUMMARY|128|catalog location summary for IstarianSanctum|Istarian Sanctum is a hard ruined temple route below the Ancient Dwarven Gate.
CATALOG_LOCATION_ISTARIAN_SANCTUM_DETAIL|224|catalog location detail for IstarianSanctum|The sanctum is compact, trap-heavy, and full of imperial stonework, constructs, elemental wards, and rare old horrors.
CATALOG_LOCATION_ISTARIAN_SANCTUM_ENEMIES|128|catalog location commonly seen enemies for IstarianSanctum|gargoyles, golems, elementals, medusas
CATALOG_LOCATION_SUNDERING_DEPTHS_SUMMARY|128|catalog location summary for SunderingDepths|Sundering Depths is the deep blackglass descent beyond the branch routes.
CATALOG_LOCATION_SUNDERING_DEPTHS_DETAIL|224|catalog location detail for SunderingDepths|The route leaves the old access works behind and becomes broken stone, heavy blackglass pressure, sealed thresholds, and corrupted beasts.
CATALOG_LOCATION_SUNDERING_DEPTHS_ENEMIES|128|catalog location commonly seen enemies for SunderingDepths|blackglass hounds, blackglass brutes, deep blackglass drakes
CATALOG_LOCATION_STARFALL_CORE_SUMMARY|128|catalog location summary for StarfallCore|Starfall Core is the deepest central section of the Scar route.
CATALOG_LOCATION_STARFALL_CORE_DETAIL|224|catalog location detail for StarfallCore|The area contains broken blackglass chambers, final rift spaces, elite corrupted monsters, and the primordial dragon encounter.
CATALOG_LOCATION_STARFALL_CORE_ENEMIES|128|catalog location commonly seen enemies for StarfallCore|primordial dragon, deep blackglass drakes, elite blackglass beasts
CATALOG_LOCATION_BURNED_COTTAGE_SUMMARY|128|catalog location summary for BurnedCottage|Burned Cottage is a destroyed roadside home with a hidden cellar below the ash.
CATALOG_LOCATION_BURNED_COTTAGE_DETAIL|224|catalog location detail for BurnedCottage|The surface is burned out, but the cellar descends into wet stone, cult remains, water-glyph markings, and a wolf den.
CATALOG_LOCATION_BURNED_COTTAGE_ENEMIES|128|catalog location commonly seen enemies for BurnedCottage|wolves, dire wolf, giant rats, cave spiders, slimes
CATALOG_LOCATION_STANDING_COTTAGE_SUMMARY|128|catalog location summary for StandingCottage|A small cottage stands intact beside the road.
CATALOG_LOCATION_STANDING_COTTAGE_DETAIL|224|catalog location detail for StandingCottage|A novice wizard keeps a quiet home here and sells copies of simple spellbooks.
CATALOG_LOCATION_STANDING_COTTAGE_ENEMIES|128|catalog location commonly seen enemies for StandingCottage|none
CATALOG_LOCATION_MOSSVALE_CLEARING_SUMMARY|128|catalog location summary for MossvaleClearing|Hunter's Clearing is an old forest glade around a clear spring and a moss-eyed statue.
CATALOG_LOCATION_MOSSVALE_CLEARING_DETAIL|224|catalog location detail for MossvaleClearing|Old snares and animal paths cross the glade. Marble stairs behind the statue descend into the Infinite Dungeon.
CATALOG_LOCATION_MOSSVALE_CLEARING_ENEMIES|128|catalog location commonly seen enemies for MossvaleClearing|wolves, boars, bears, spiders
CATALOG_LOCATION_INFINITE_DUNGEON_SUMMARY|160|catalog location summary for InfiniteDungeon|An unending dungeon whose rooms and inhabitants change whenever its stairs are crossed.
CATALOG_LOCATION_INFINITE_DUNGEON_DETAIL|256|catalog location detail for InfiniteDungeon|Danger and treasure rise with depth. Every tenth floor opens into a shifting marble waystation kept by will-o'-wisps, with beds, supplies, enchantment, and martial goods.
CATALOG_LOCATION_INFINITE_DUNGEON_ENEMIES|128|catalog location commonly seen enemies for InfiniteDungeon|changing dungeon denizens
CATALOG_LOCATION_INFINITE_DUNGEON_LEVEL|128|catalog level description for InfiniteDungeon|Level: 1-20 (scales with depth)
CATALOG_LOCATION_SMUGGLER_GROTTO_SUMMARY|128|catalog location summary for SmugglerGrotto|Smuggler Grotto is a set of wet shore caves used for hidden storage.
CATALOG_LOCATION_SMUGGLER_GROTTO_DETAIL|224|catalog location detail for SmugglerGrotto|The caves contain smugglers' goods, tide pools, narrow passages, and animals from the surrounding water and rocks.
CATALOG_LOCATION_SMUGGLER_GROTTO_ENEMIES|128|catalog location commonly seen enemies for SmugglerGrotto|bandits, snakes, giant rats, slime
CATALOG_LOCATION_BROKEN_WATCHTOWER_SUMMARY|128|catalog location summary for BrokenWatchtower|Ruined Watchtower is an old border tower with broken upper rooms and exposed stairs.
CATALOG_LOCATION_BROKEN_WATCHTOWER_DETAIL|224|catalog location detail for BrokenWatchtower|The site gives raiders a lookout over the road and contains enough intact stone for a defended camp.
CATALOG_LOCATION_BROKEN_WATCHTOWER_ENEMIES|128|catalog location commonly seen enemies for BrokenWatchtower|orcs, hobgoblins, archers, giant bats
CATALOG_LOCATION_BLACKGLASS_CAVERN_SUMMARY|128|catalog location summary for BlackglassCavern|Blackglass Cavern is a cavern system lined with blackglass shards and scarred stone.
CATALOG_LOCATION_BLACKGLASS_CAVERN_DETAIL|224|catalog location detail for BlackglassCavern|Its rooms contain corrupted animals, blackglass hazards, tight side routes, and stronger threats deeper in.
CATALOG_LOCATION_BLACKGLASS_CAVERN_ENEMIES|128|catalog location commonly seen enemies for BlackglassCavern|blackglass vermin, shardmouth hounds, vein weavers
CATALOG_LOCATION_KINGS_BARROW_SUMMARY|128|catalog location summary for KingsBarrow|King's Barrow is a royal burial mound from the old Marches.
CATALOG_LOCATION_KINGS_BARROW_DETAIL|224|catalog location detail for KingsBarrow|The barrow has sealed tomb halls, guard chambers, grave goods, and undead soldiers around the deeper rooms.
CATALOG_LOCATION_KINGS_BARROW_ENEMIES|128|catalog location commonly seen enemies for KingsBarrow|skeletons, ghouls, fallen lance knights
CATALOG_LOCATION_OLD_CAVE_SUMMARY|128|catalog location summary for OldCave|Old Cave is a plain cave entrance that leads into worked stone rooms.
CATALOG_LOCATION_OLD_CAVE_DETAIL|224|catalog location detail for OldCave|The lower area includes catacombs, storage pockets, insects, snakes, undead, and scattered slime.
CATALOG_LOCATION_OLD_CAVE_ENEMIES|128|catalog location commonly seen enemies for OldCave|ants, snakes, skeletons, slime
CATALOG_LOCATION_DUSTY_DUNGEON_SUMMARY|128|catalog location summary for DustyDungeon|Dusty Dungeon is a small cut-stone ruin with simple rooms and old storage areas.
CATALOG_LOCATION_DUSTY_DUNGEON_DETAIL|224|catalog location detail for DustyDungeon|It is an early low-risk dungeon with basic vermin, a few hazards, and modest supplies.
CATALOG_LOCATION_DUSTY_DUNGEON_ENEMIES|128|catalog location commonly seen enemies for DustyDungeon|rats, bats, snakes, slime
CATALOG_LOCATION_ABANDONED_MINE_SUMMARY|128|catalog location summary for AbandonedMine|Abandoned Mine is a worked mine with old equipment and side shafts.
CATALOG_LOCATION_ABANDONED_MINE_DETAIL|224|catalog location detail for AbandonedMine|Kobolds have moved into parts of it, while insects and rust monsters occupy the rougher lower sections.
CATALOG_LOCATION_ABANDONED_MINE_ENEMIES|128|catalog location commonly seen enemies for AbandonedMine|kobold archers, ants, rust monsters
CATALOG_LOCATION_FLOODGATE_CISTERN_SUMMARY|128|catalog location summary for FloodgateCistern|Floodgate Cistern is an old imperial reservoir and sluice complex.
CATALOG_LOCATION_FLOODGATE_CISTERN_DETAIL|224|catalog location detail for FloodgateCistern|It has flooded rooms, raised service walks, drain channels, fungus growth, drowned corpses, and a water drake in the lower sluice.
CATALOG_LOCATION_FLOODGATE_CISTERN_ENEMIES|128|catalog location commonly seen enemies for FloodgateCistern|leeches, slime, crocodiles, ghouls, water drake
CATALOG_LOCATION_BANDIT_TOLL_CAMP_SUMMARY|128|catalog location summary for BanditTollCamp|Bandit Toll Camp is a fortified bridge checkpoint with a wooden fort behind the river crossing.
CATALOG_LOCATION_BANDIT_TOLL_CAMP_DETAIL|224|catalog location detail for BanditTollCamp|The camp has palisades, a toll bridge, shacks, camp yards, store piles, barracks, and a boss room on the upper fort floor.
CATALOG_LOCATION_BANDIT_TOLL_CAMP_ENEMIES|128|catalog location commonly seen enemies for BanditTollCamp|bandits, enforcers, cutthroats
CATALOG_LOCATION_OLD_MINEWORKS_SUMMARY|128|catalog location summary for OldMineworks|Deadrock Mineworks is a sealed dwarven mineworks below the hills.
CATALOG_LOCATION_OLD_MINEWORKS_DETAIL|224|catalog location detail for OldMineworks|Old service rooms and cut-stone shafts lead into deeper blackglass scoring, duergar barracks, and Vargrom's guarded salvage chamber.
CATALOG_LOCATION_OLD_MINEWORKS_ENEMIES|128|catalog location commonly seen enemies for OldMineworks|duergar veterans, duergar priests, blackglass duergar, skeleton knights
CATALOG_LOCATION_CHALKHILL_BURROWS_SUMMARY|128|catalog location summary for ChalkhillBurrows|Chalk Warren is a pale hill tunnel system cut through soft chalk.
CATALOG_LOCATION_CHALKHILL_BURROWS_DETAIL|224|catalog location detail for ChalkhillBurrows|It connects smugglers' passages, animal burrows, narrow chambers, and a small underground lake.
CATALOG_LOCATION_CHALKHILL_BURROWS_ENEMIES|128|catalog location commonly seen enemies for ChalkhillBurrows|medusas, manticores, umber hulks
CATALOG_LOCATION_ORC_BASE_SUMMARY|128|catalog location summary for OrcBase|Orc Fortress is a compact hill fort with palisades and dug-in rooms.
CATALOG_LOCATION_ORC_BASE_DETAIL|224|catalog location detail for OrcBase|It is denser than a normal cave, with guard rooms, stores, chests, orc groups, occasional ogres, and a warboss room.
CATALOG_LOCATION_ORC_BASE_ENEMIES|128|catalog location commonly seen enemies for OrcBase|orcs, ogres, ravagers, a warboss
CATALOG_LOCATION_ORC_WAR_SITE_SUMMARY|128|catalog summary shared by the selected Orc finale site|The surviving orc warband gathers in either cramped hill warrens or a broad palisade camp.
CATALOG_LOCATION_ORC_WAR_SITE_DETAIL|224|catalog detail shared by the selected Orc finale site|The Warrens route is longer, dark, and confined. The War Camp route begins in an open fortified camp and descends into shorter dugouts.
CATALOG_LOCATION_ORC_WAR_SITE_ENEMIES|128|catalog enemies shared by the selected Orc finale site|orc champions, throwers, berserkers, warlocks, ogres
CATALOG_LOCATION_REEDMIRE_SHRINE_SUMMARY|128|catalog location summary for ReedmireShrine|Reedmire Shrine is a flooded shrine in marshland.
CATALOG_LOCATION_REEDMIRE_SHRINE_DETAIL|224|catalog location detail for ReedmireShrine|The route passes through cold water, reed beds, broken stone rooms, and marsh creatures using the ruins for cover.
CATALOG_LOCATION_REEDMIRE_SHRINE_ENEMIES|128|catalog location commonly seen enemies for ReedmireShrine|leeches, vipers, cultists, will-o-wisps
CATALOG_LOCATION_DESERTED_CAMP_SUMMARY|128|catalog location summary for DesertedCamp|Deserted Camp is an abandoned military stopover with rough clearings and cold campfires.
CATALOG_LOCATION_DESERTED_CAMP_DETAIL|224|catalog location detail for DesertedCamp|Bedrolls, weapon racks, crates, sacks, and cut stumps mark where expedition groups made camp before undead and scavengers moved in.
CATALOG_LOCATION_DESERTED_CAMP_ENEMIES|128|catalog location commonly seen enemies for DesertedCamp|fallen lance knights, grave hounds, skeleton knights
CATALOG_LOCATION_MOONWELL_OBSERVATORY_SUMMARY|128|catalog location summary for MoonwellObservatory|Moonwell Observatory is a hilltop observatory with lens galleries and lower ritual rooms.
CATALOG_LOCATION_MOONWELL_OBSERVATORY_DETAIL|224|catalog location detail for MoonwellObservatory|The upper floors are built for moon and star work, while the hidden chamber below holds stronger enemies.
CATALOG_LOCATION_MOONWELL_OBSERVATORY_ENEMIES|128|catalog location commonly seen enemies for MoonwellObservatory|evil mages, ghosts, necromancer lords
CATALOG_LOCATION_HIGHWIND_MONASTERY_SUMMARY|128|catalog location summary for HighwindMonastery|Highwind Monastery is a burned monastery with cloisters, cells, and heat-damaged halls.
CATALOG_LOCATION_HIGHWIND_MONASTERY_DETAIL|224|catalog location detail for HighwindMonastery|Fire elementals, greater fire elementals, and animated armor occupy the complex, especially around sealed inner rooms.
CATALOG_LOCATION_HIGHWIND_MONASTERY_ENEMIES|128|catalog location commonly seen enemies for HighwindMonastery|fire elementals, greater fire elementals, animated armor
CATALOG_LOCATION_HIGHWIND_CATACOMBS_SUMMARY|128|catalog location summary for HighwindCatacombs|Highwind Catacombs is the undercrypt below the monastery.
CATALOG_LOCATION_HIGHWIND_CATACOMBS_DETAIL|224|catalog location detail for HighwindCatacombs|The descent passes through ossuaries, crypt halls, tomb rooms, burned lower chapels, and a final crypt.
CATALOG_LOCATION_HIGHWIND_CATACOMBS_ENEMIES|128|catalog location commonly seen enemies for HighwindCatacombs|mummies, wraiths, bone golems, death knights, fire elementals
CATALOG_LOCATION_BRIAR_SAINT_GROVE_SUMMARY|128|catalog location summary for BriarSaintGrove|Briar Saint Grove is an overgrown shrine grove with thorn roots and quiet pools.
CATALOG_LOCATION_BRIAR_SAINT_GROVE_DETAIL|224|catalog location detail for BriarSaintGrove|The paths are broken by brush, water, old shrine stones, spiders, and aggressive forest beasts.
CATALOG_LOCATION_BRIAR_SAINT_GROVE_ENEMIES|128|catalog location commonly seen enemies for BriarSaintGrove|dire wolves, ettercaps, wolf spiders, owlbears, treants
CATALOG_LOCATION_GLASSNEEDLE_RAVINE_SUMMARY|128|catalog location summary for GlassneedleRavine|Narrow Ravine is a steep ravine with ledges and splintered blackglass in the stone.
CATALOG_LOCATION_GLASSNEEDLE_RAVINE_DETAIL|224|catalog location detail for GlassneedleRavine|The upper descent uses tight winding ravine caves, then opens into lower worked rooms beneath the ravine floor.
CATALOG_LOCATION_GLASSNEEDLE_RAVINE_ENEMIES|128|catalog location commonly seen enemies for GlassneedleRavine|harpies, gargoyles, cave fishers, ropers, umber hulks
CATALOG_LOCATION_SERPENTWATER_OASIS_SUMMARY|128|catalog location summary for SerpentwaterOasis|Stillwater Oasis is a desert spring fed by mountain water.
CATALOG_LOCATION_SERPENTWATER_OASIS_DETAIL|224|catalog location detail for SerpentwaterOasis|The site has deep pools, sahuagin champions, sea hags, water elementals, and hydras around the central water.
CATALOG_LOCATION_SERPENTWATER_OASIS_ENEMIES|128|catalog location commonly seen enemies for SerpentwaterOasis|sahuagin champions, sea hags, water elementals, hydras
CATALOG_LOCATION_TROLLKING_CAVE_SUMMARY|128|catalog location summary for TrollkingCave|Bloodied Cave is a mountain cave controlled by trolls.
CATALOG_LOCATION_TROLLKING_CAVE_DETAIL|224|catalog location detail for TrollkingCave|The tunnels are large enough for ogres and giants, with bones, refuse piles, and close-quarters fights throughout.
CATALOG_LOCATION_TROLLKING_CAVE_ENEMIES|128|catalog location commonly seen enemies for TrollkingCave|trolls, ogres, hill giants
CATALOG_LOCATION_LESSER_SCAR_BREACH_SUMMARY|128|catalog location summary for LesserScarBreach|Lesser Scar Breach is a long blackglass dungeon below a lesser scar break.
CATALOG_LOCATION_LESSER_SCAR_BREACH_DETAIL|224|catalog location detail for LesserScarBreach|The first half is cracked stone and blackglass growth, then a sealed midpoint leads to deeper scar pressure below.
CATALOG_LOCATION_LESSER_SCAR_BREACH_ENEMIES|128|catalog location commonly seen enemies for LesserScarBreach|blackglass beasts, earth elementals, stone golems, black dragons
CATALOG_LOCATION_ROCKMAW_KEEP_SUMMARY|128|catalog location summary for RockmawKeep|Rockmaw Keep is a plains stronghold held by ogres and giants.
CATALOG_LOCATION_ROCKMAW_KEEP_DETAIL|224|catalog location detail for RockmawKeep|It has an approach yard, breached gates, barracks, stores, pens, upper halls, and a final arena.
CATALOG_LOCATION_ROCKMAW_KEEP_ENEMIES|128|catalog location commonly seen enemies for RockmawKeep|ogres, ogre champions, ettins, hill giants, stone giants
CATALOG_LOCATION_SALTMERE_CAVERNS_SUMMARY|128|catalog location summary for SaltmereCaverns|Saltmere Caverns is a coastal salt cave system with wet lower chambers.
CATALOG_LOCATION_SALTMERE_CAVERNS_DETAIL|224|catalog location detail for SaltmereCaverns|Dry salt caves give way to tidal passages, flooded chambers, sahuagin pockets, heat pockets, and a storm water lair.
CATALOG_LOCATION_SALTMERE_CAVERNS_ENEMIES|128|catalog location commonly seen enemies for SaltmereCaverns|sahuagin, sea hags, giant eels, water elementals, salamanders
CATALOG_LOCATION_OLD_IMPERIAL_LIGHTHOUSE_SUMMARY|128|catalog location summary for OldImperialLighthouse|Old Imperial Lighthouse is a drowned imperial watchtower on the far eastern peninsula.
CATALOG_LOCATION_OLD_IMPERIAL_LIGHTHOUSE_DETAIL|224|catalog location detail for OldImperialLighthouse|Its basement is flooded and occupied by water creatures, while the narrowing tower shifts from sahuagin patrols to wisps, specters, wraiths, and a sea hag at the dead beacon.
CATALOG_LOCATION_OLD_IMPERIAL_LIGHTHOUSE_ENEMIES|128|catalog location commonly seen enemies for OldImperialLighthouse|sahuagin, giant eels, water weirds, will-o-wisps, wraiths, sea hag
CATALOG_LOCATION_MOUNTAIN_PASS_SUMMARY|128|catalog location summary for MountainPass|Mountain Pass is a northern ascent into a white dragon lair.
CATALOG_LOCATION_MOUNTAIN_PASS_DETAIL|224|catalog location detail for MountainPass|The lower floor is a long winding climb, and the upper cavern is an open frozen lair with no natural spawns.
CATALOG_LOCATION_MOUNTAIN_PASS_ENEMIES|128|catalog location commonly seen enemies for MountainPass|ancient white dragon
CATALOG_LOCATION_ELDERWYRM_GROVE_SUMMARY|128|catalog location summary for ElderwyrmGrove|Elderwyrm Grove is a remote forest lair around an elder forest dragon.
CATALOG_LOCATION_ELDERWYRM_GROVE_DETAIL|224|catalog location detail for ElderwyrmGrove|The grove is dense, maze-like, and filled with large predators before the final dragon area.
CATALOG_LOCATION_ELDERWYRM_GROVE_ENEMIES|128|catalog location commonly seen enemies for ElderwyrmGrove|dire bears, owlbears, treants, wyverns, forest dragons
CATALOG_LOCATION_GREAT_SCAR_CREVASSE_SUMMARY|128|catalog location summary for GreatScarCrevasse|Great Scar Crevasse is a hard western branch of the Scar.
CATALOG_LOCATION_GREAT_SCAR_CREVASSE_DETAIL|224|catalog location detail for GreatScarCrevasse|It descends through broken blackglass, angular stone rooms, branch paths, miniboss areas, and two artifact-guarding lairs.
CATALOG_LOCATION_GREAT_SCAR_CREVASSE_ENEMIES|128|catalog location commonly seen enemies for GreatScarCrevasse|shardmouth hounds, scar stalkers, gargoyles, drakes
CATALOG_LOCATION_HIGHMARK_AQUEDUCT_SUMMARY|128|catalog location summary for HighmarkAqueduct|Highmark Aqueduct is an old waterworks northwest of Highmark.
CATALOG_LOCATION_HIGHMARK_AQUEDUCT_DETAIL|224|catalog location detail for HighmarkAqueduct|It contains shallow center-channel corridors, sluice walks, flooded pockets, side service rooms, maintenance halls, and water hazards.
CATALOG_LOCATION_HIGHMARK_AQUEDUCT_ENEMIES|128|catalog location commonly seen enemies for HighmarkAqueduct|leeches, slime, drowned dead, water weirds
CATALOG_LOCATION_GHOSTWOOD_SUMMARY|128|catalog location summary for Ghostwood|Ghostwood is a dense undead-infested forest maze leading to an old stone tower.
CATALOG_LOCATION_GHOSTWOOD_DETAIL|224|catalog location detail for Ghostwood|The forest section uses dense trees and limited sight lines, while the tower contains stronger undead and vampires.
CATALOG_LOCATION_GHOSTWOOD_ENEMIES|128|catalog location commonly seen enemies for Ghostwood|grave hounds, wights, vampires
CATALOG_LOCATION_GREYCLIFF_QUARRY_SUMMARY|128|catalog location summary for GreycliffQuarry|Greycliff Quarry is an old quarry now held by bandits and mountain creatures.
CATALOG_LOCATION_GREYCLIFF_QUARRY_DETAIL|224|catalog location detail for GreycliffQuarry|It has open quarry yards, ramps, cut passages, broken cliff ledges, and upper areas used by flying threats.
CATALOG_LOCATION_GREYCLIFF_QUARRY_ENEMIES|128|catalog location commonly seen enemies for GreycliffQuarry|bandits, gargoyles, harpies, wyverns
CATALOG_LOCATION_OLDROOT_TEMPLE_SUMMARY|128|catalog location summary for OldrootTemple|Oldroot Temple is a pre-Starfall nature temple partly reclaimed by roots and animals.
CATALOG_LOCATION_OLDROOT_TEMPLE_DETAIL|224|catalog location detail for OldrootTemple|The floors mix temple rooms, wall-biting root growth, blocking vines, brush, trees, spiders, and large forest beasts.
CATALOG_LOCATION_OLDROOT_TEMPLE_ENEMIES|128|catalog location commonly seen enemies for OldrootTemple|dire wolves, ettercaps, owlbears, treants
CATALOG_LOCATION_WIDOWRUN_CAVE_SUMMARY|128|catalog location summary for WidowrunCave|Widowrun Cave is a narrow cave system dominated by webs and poison threats.
CATALOG_LOCATION_WIDOWRUN_CAVE_DETAIL|224|catalog location detail for WidowrunCave|The layout has choke points, webbed chambers, small pools, light blackglass corruption, and spiders or ettercaps guarding the deeper rooms.
CATALOG_LOCATION_WIDOWRUN_CAVE_ENEMIES|128|catalog location commonly seen enemies for WidowrunCave|wolf spiders, blackglass spiders, ettercaps, pit vipers
CATALOG_LOCATION_MOONWELL_TUNNELS_SUMMARY|128|catalog location summary for MoonwellTunnels|Moonwell Tunnels is an old dwarven shortcut below the Moonwell hills.
CATALOG_LOCATION_MOONWELL_TUNNELS_DETAIL|224|catalog location detail for MoonwellTunnels|The route includes two small end sections and a long tunnel floor overrun by deep stone creatures.
CATALOG_LOCATION_MOONWELL_TUNNELS_ENEMIES|128|catalog location commonly seen enemies for MoonwellTunnels|troglodytes, rust monsters, ropers, xorn
CATALOG_LOCATION_DESOLATE_DOCKS_SUMMARY|128|catalog location summary for DesolateDocks|Desolate Docks is a ruined dock settlement on the peninsula northeast of Traveller's Rest.
CATALOG_LOCATION_DESOLATE_DOCKS_DETAIL|224|catalog location detail for DesolateDocks|It has a rough sand-edged shore, damaged piers, broken-open houses, clustered dock supplies, and a small occupied cellar.
CATALOG_LOCATION_DESOLATE_DOCKS_ENEMIES|128|catalog location commonly seen enemies for DesolateDocks|orcs, hobgoblins, bugbears, dock scavengers
CATALOG_LOCATION_INCONSPICUOUS_CAVE_SUMMARY|128|catalog location summary for InconspicuousCave|Inconspicuous Cave starts as an ordinary cave mouth in the hills.
CATALOG_LOCATION_INCONSPICUOUS_CAVE_DETAIL|224|catalog location detail for InconspicuousCave|Lower floors become more organized and end in clean stone rooms controlled by werewolves and their king.
CATALOG_LOCATION_INCONSPICUOUS_CAVE_ENEMIES|128|catalog location commonly seen enemies for InconspicuousCave|wargs, werewolves, cave bears, the werewolf king
