BOSS_INTRO_JORREN_THE_BANDIT_VETERAN|160|named monster intro message for Jorren, the Bandit Veteran|"Drop the pack and maybe I leave you breathing. Reach for steel and I make an example for the next wagon."
BOSS_INTRO_SKRIT_THE_KOBOLD_PACKLEADER|160|named monster intro message for Skrit, the Kobold Packleader|"No tallfolk in Skrit's tunnels! The shiny vein feeds my pack, not your soft pockets."
BOSS_INTRO_EDRAN_THE_GHOST|160|named monster intro message for Edran, the Ghost|"She kept the lamp lit for me. The road shut, the dark rose, and I never reached the door."
BOSS_INTRO_NHALOR_THE_WATER_WEIRD|160|named monster intro message for Nhalor, the Water Weird|The reeds hid the old water until foolish hands stirred it. Now the deep takes back its gift.
BOSS_INTRO_OLD_SNAPJAW_THE_CROCODILE|160|named monster intro message for Old Snapjaw, the Crocodile|The black water breaks around old teeth. Snapjaw lunges for the hand that stole his cove.
BOSS_INTRO_SER_CALDUS_THE_WIGHT|160|named monster intro message for Ser Caldus, the Wight|"I swore the crossing shut with lance and bone. Living feet pass only over my ruin."
BOSS_INTRO_HALRIC_THE_GREATER_GHOUL|160|named monster intro message for Halric, the Greater Ghoul|"The ranks are hungry, and your warm heart drums too loudly. Come join the old line."
BOSS_INTRO_OLD_BRIARBACK_THE_OWLBEAR|160|named monster intro message for Old Briarback, the Owlbear|Branches snap, feathers bristle, and the old hunter charges from the brush.
BOSS_INTRO_MAVRESSA_THE_SPIDER_QUEEN|160|named monster intro message for Mavressa, the Spider Queen|"Step lightly, warm thing. Every thread you break tells my children where to bite."
BOSS_INTRO_HIGHLEDGE_THE_WYVERN|160|named monster intro message for Deathtail, the Wyvern|A shadow drops from the cliff. Deathtail screams once, and the rocks answer with wings.
BOSS_INTRO_VAERITH_THE_FOREST_DRAGON|160|named monster intro message for Vaerith, the Forest Dragon|The dragon's voice sinks into the roots: "Your blood smells of old keys and broken bargains. This line ends here."
BOSS_INTRO_VEYR_THE_VAMPIRE_LORD|160|named monster intro message for Veyr, the Vampire Lord|"You climbed all this way with a heart still beating. How generous of you."
BOSS_INTRO_RUSKARN_THE_GREATER_GARGOYLE|160|named monster intro message for Ruskarn, the Greater Gargoyle|The carved thing unfolds from the wall, stone claws scraping for warm trespass.
BOSS_INTRO_GARRUN_THE_UMBER_HULK|160|named monster intro message for Garrun, the Umber Hulk|The floor bursts open. Garrun's many eyes roll toward the sound of your breath.
BOSS_INTRO_VORRAK_THE_UMBER_HULK|160|named monster intro message for Vorrak, the Umber Hulk|Stone dust pours from the ceiling as Vorrak claws up through the dark beneath you.
BOSS_INTRO_OLD_UMBER_HULK|160|named monster intro message for Old Umber Hulk|Something huge moves under the tunnel floor. Then the old digger comes up hungry.
BOSS_INTRO_VARROTH_THE_WEREWOLF_KING|160|named monster intro message for Varroth, the Werewolf King|"You smell of iron, fear, and camp smoke. Run if you like; the pack loves a chase."
BOSS_INTRO_BROTHER_ORATH_THE_MASTER_NECROMANCER|160|named monster intro message for Brother Orath, the Master Necromancer|"Stay still. A useful skeleton is worth more than another brave fool with opinions."
BOSS_INTRO_PRIOR_ARVEN_THE_GREATER_SHADOW|160|named monster intro message for Prior Arven, the Greater Shadow|"I kept the sins below the floor for years. You opened the door. Now carry them."
BOSS_INTRO_RHAZVEK_THE_YOUNG_RED_DRAGON|160|named monster intro message for Rhazvek, the Young Red Dragon|Rhazvek's voice snaps through the heat: "Your little star burns black under my flame. Let us see which fire owns you."
BOSS_INTRO_MAEROTH_THE_RED_DRAGON|160|named monster intro message for Maeroth, the Red Dragon|Maeroth's voice rolls through the ash: "Highwind's prayers are ash. Kneel in the soot, or burn with them."
BOSS_INTRO_MAEROTH_THE_ELDER_RED_DRAGON|160|named monster intro message for Maeroth, the Elder Red Dragon|Maeroth's voice rolls through the ash: "I have slept under hotter ruins than your courage. Come, little spark."
BOSS_INTRO_ORRIC_VANE_THE_MASTER_NECROMANCER|160|named monster intro message for Orric Vane, the Master Necromancer|"Do you know what a body is worth when it stops arguing? Step closer and I will appraise yours."
BOSS_INTRO_ORREN_THE_BLACK_DRAGON|160|named monster intro message for Orren, the Black Dragon|Orren's voice crawls through the breach: "You brought Lightglass here. Good. I wanted it warm in your hand when it failed."
BOSS_INTRO_KRAVOSS_THE_DEEP_BLACKGLASS_DRAKE|160|named monster intro message for Kravoss, the Deep Blackglass Drake|A voice grinds inside your skull: "The Scar roots deep. You found the mouth; now it closes."
BOSS_INTRO_VYRNAX_THE_DEEP_BLACKGLASS_DRAKE|160|named monster intro message for Vyrnax, the Deep Blackglass Drake|A voice drips through the blackglass: "Old blood, bright glass, small courage. The deep eats them all."
BOSS_INTRO_BROND_THE_OGRE_CHAMPION|160|named monster intro message for Brond, the Ogre Champion|"Maug shouts. Brond breaks gates. You look easier than a gate."
BOSS_INTRO_VEYRA_THE_MUMMY_LORD|160|named monster intro message for Veyra, the Mummy Lord|"No guest crosses this crypt. Kneel as an offering, or be wrapped as one."
BOSS_INTRO_AZRAN_THE_ELDER_BLUE_DRAGON|160|named monster intro message for Azran, the Elder Blue Dragon|Azran's voice gathers like thunder: "Stormwater carried your scent into my hall. Kneel before thunder learns your name."
BOSS_INTRO_ISSHARA_THE_HYDRA|160|named monster intro message for Isshara, the Hydra|One head tastes the air. The others hiss, hungry to decide which part of you is first.
BOSS_INTRO_GRUMMOK_THE_TROLL_KING|160|named monster intro message for Grummok, the Troll King|"Little bones, big pot, fresh screams. Grummok likes visitors who fit in the stew."
BOSS_INTRO_MULGREN_THE_TROLL|160|named monster intro message for Mulgren, the Troll|The bottom dust stirs. Mulgren drags a spiked morning star from the dark. "Soft bones came all the way down."
BOSS_INTRO_BLOODCOIL_THE_GIANT_LEECH|160|named monster intro message for Bloodcoil, the Giant Leech|Black water ripples. Bloodcoil unfastens from the lakebed and stretches toward the warmth in the room.
BOSS_INTRO_NEEDLELEGS_THE_WOLF_SPIDER|160|named monster intro message for Needlelegs, the Wolf Spider|Webs tremble across the chamber. Needlelegs unfolds from the stone and darts forward on pale, sharpened limbs.
BOSS_INTRO_OBITUARY_GHOST|160|one-use obituary ghost intro message|A dead adventurer steps through the stone, pale gear hanging from a body that no longer remembers its wounds.
BOSS_INTRO_CINDERMAW_THE_DIRE_WOLF|160|named monster intro message for Cindermaw, the Dire Wolf|Cindermaw raises its ash-black muzzle and barks once. The shallow water trembles around the dead cultists.
BOSS_INTRO_CAERWYN_THE_ANCIENT_FOREST_DRAGON|160|named monster intro message for Caerwyn, the Ancient Forest Dragon|The dragon's voice rustles through the canopy: "Root, crown, and old wound remember your bloodline. I will bury it."
BOSS_INTRO_ARVAELOS_THE_ANCIENT_WHITE_DRAGON|160|named monster intro message for Arvaelos, the Ancient White Dragon|Arvaelos's voice is cold in your teeth: "So far from warm doors. So close to becoming another shape beneath the ice."
BOSS_INTRO_AURALITH_THE_YOUNG_BLUE_DRAGON|160|named monster intro message for Auralith, the Young Blue Dragon|A voice crackles inside your skull: "The Beacon Prism still rings with my storm. Listen while it breaks you."
BOSS_INTRO_KAELVORN_THE_GREATER_DRAKE|160|named monster intro message for Kaelvorn, the Greater Drake|A voice presses into your head: "Old oaths locked this vault. Warm blood opened it. I will drink the mistake."
BOSS_INTRO_MORDRAXIS_THE_BLACKGLASS_DRAKE|160|named monster intro message for Mordraxis, the Blackglass Drake|A voice scrapes behind your eyes: "There it is, old blood under your skin. Come closer. The blackglass wants you screaming."
BOSS_INTRO_MOONWELL_ECHO_THE_LIGHTGLASS_GHOST|160|named monster intro message for Moonwell Echo, the Lightglass Ghost|A pale dragon-shape rises inside the ghost. It opens a mouth of cold light, and the Moonwell water trembles.
BOSS_INTRO_VHAROX_THE_BLACKGLASS_DRAKE|160|named monster intro message for Vharox, the Blackglass Drake|A voice pulses through the blackglass: "I know your line. I have waited longer than you have been alive."
BOSS_INTRO_KROSH_THE_ORC_WARRIOR|160|named monster intro message for Krosh, the Orc Warrior|"These docks burn when I say they burn. You can go in the fire first."
BOSS_INTRO_VARGROM_THE_DUERGAR_GUARD|160|named monster intro message for Vargrom, the Blackglass Duergar Captain|"My works kept your road breathing. Come deeper, and Deadrock takes the rest."
BOSS_INTRO_KHORVUL_THE_DRAKE|160|named monster intro message for Khorvul, the Drake|A voice hammers inside your skull: "The north gate fed me well, softblood. Your bones will hold the hinge shut."
BOSS_INTRO_RAKTO_THE_GOBLIN_CHIEF|160|named monster intro message for Rakto, the Goblin Chief|"My cave, my teeth, my take! Come closer and Rakto wears your ears!"
BOSS_INTRO_VRASK_THE_YOUNG_DRAKE|160|named monster intro message for Vrask, the Young Drake|A voice echoes inside your head: "That black star sings in your blood. Burn, little heir, and wake it louder."
BOSS_INTRO_GORVUK_THE_ORC_WARBOSS|160|named monster intro message for Gorvuk, the Orc Warboss|"Stonecleft road, Stonecleft iron, Stonecleft throats. Gorvuk takes all three."
BOSS_INTRO_MORGHAT_THE_ORC_WARLOCK|160|named monster intro message for Morghat, the Orc Warlock|"You followed us underground. Good. The stone will keep your bones."
BOSS_INTRO_VARKAN_THE_ORC_CHAMPION|160|named monster intro message for Varkan, the Orc Champion|"Krosh failed. Gorvuk failed. Varkan will build the warband from your corpse."
BOSS_INTRO_BRAM_THE_STONE_GOLEM|160|named monster intro message for Bram, the Stone Golem|Bram's carved eyes flare. The old floor shifts under his first step.
BOSS_INTRO_MAUG_THE_ETTIN|160|named monster intro message for Maug, the Ettin|"Maug says smash. Maug says bite. For once, both heads agree."
BOSS_INTRO_KING_HALRIC_THE_BARROW_WIGHT|160|named monster intro message for King Halric, the Barrow Wight|"Halric holds the road. Halric holds the ring. No living hand takes either."
BOSS_INTRO_RHAZUN_THE_WATER_DRAKE|160|named monster intro message for Rhazun, the Water Drake|A voice gurgles under the water: "What sinks here stays here. Come down, warm blood."
BOSS_INTRO_DORUN_VARR_THE_TOLL_BOSS|160|named monster intro message for Dorun Varr, the Toll Boss|"Bridge toll is blood today. Pay up, or Dorun throws the rest of you over."
BOSS_INTRO_THYRAXX_THE_ANCIENT_BLUE_DRAGON|160|named monster intro message for Thyraxx, the Ancient Blue Dragon|Thyraxx's voice splits the air: "I taught this height to fear thunder. Now I will teach you."
BOSS_INTRO_VERRIK_ASHVOW|160|named monster intro message for Verrik Ashvow|"The drowned dead kept my vow better than the living ever did. Kneel with them."
STORY_VOICE_UNDERWAY_OPEN||delayed fullscreen voice after The Underway opens|A distant voice says: "The lower road is open. Come down."
STORY_VOICE_WHITE_SEAL||delayed fullscreen voice after the White Seal rite is complete|A distant voice says: "Blood of the seal, carry the star made clean. The old lock waits below."
STORY_VOICE_STONEWARD||delayed fullscreen voice after the Stoneward Gate opens|A distant voice says: "The stone road has heard you. Deeper, child of the seal." Thunder rolls once above you.
STORY_VOICE_FINAL_SEAL||delayed fullscreen voice after seeing the final blood seal|A low voice says: "Blood alone is not the word. Bring the lost phrase and the Lightglass star to the seal."
