# Random NPC flavor dialogue
NPC_LINE_EDRIN_1||random NPC flavor dialogue line 1 from kEdrinLines|Mind the inkstones. River order, then age, then whether they hum when the lamp is near.
NPC_LINE_EDRIN_2||random NPC flavor dialogue line 2 from kEdrinLines|Trace the carving first. The stone lies less when it has not been dragged across a table.
NPC_LINE_EDRIN_3||random NPC flavor dialogue line 3 from kEdrinLines|Wrap blackglass in cloth, not leather. Leather sweats, and blackglass remembers pressure.
NPC_LINE_EDRIN_CAVE_COMPLETE_1||random NPC flavor dialogue line 1 from kEdrinCaveCompleteLines|Goblins gone, yes, but the cave marks are older and more patient. That worries me more.
NPC_LINE_EDRIN_CAVE_COMPLETE_2||random NPC flavor dialogue line 2 from kEdrinCaveCompleteLines|The tally cuts under the soot predate the goblins. Crude hands built over careful ones.
NPC_LINE_EDRIN_CAVE_COMPLETE_3||random NPC flavor dialogue line 3 from kEdrinCaveCompleteLines|Chief's dead. Good. Now the wall grooves can speak without goblin trash piled in their mouths.
NPC_LINE_THERYN_1||random NPC flavor dialogue line 1 from kTherynLines|Do not dust old pages with your sleeve. That is how fools awaken the margin notes.
NPC_LINE_THERYN_2||random NPC flavor dialogue line 2 from kTherynLines|A book written in dragon blood is not a treasure. It is an argument waiting for a reader.
NPC_LINE_THERYN_3||random NPC flavor dialogue line 3 from kTherynLines|If it was never written down, it is rumor. If it was written down badly, it is worse.
NPC_LINE_FARMER_1||random NPC flavor dialogue line 1 from kFarmerLines|East fence leans like a drunk uncle. One more rain and the goats will vote it down.
NPC_LINE_FARMER_2||random NPC flavor dialogue line 2 from kFarmerLines|Seed bins are thin. We plant careful now and pray careless later.
NPC_LINE_FARMER_3||random NPC flavor dialogue line 3 from kFarmerLines|Crows have grown bold enough to argue. I keep a stone pile by the rows.
NPC_LINE_FARMER_4||random NPC flavor dialogue line 4 from kFarmerLines|No wagons since yesterday. Even the dogs know quiet road is wrong.
NPC_LINE_FARMER_CAVE_STARTED_1||random NPC flavor dialogue line 1 from kFarmerCaveStartedLines|Goblins pulled the high fence down and left laughing cuts in the rails.
NPC_LINE_FARMER_CAVE_STARTED_2||random NPC flavor dialogue line 2 from kFarmerCaveStartedLines|Half the seed grain went into goblin sacks. Spring does not care who stole it.
NPC_LINE_FARMER_CAVE_STARTED_3||random NPC flavor dialogue line 3 from kFarmerCaveStartedLines|They left the gate open after dark. The missing ewe had more sense than the latch.
NPC_LINE_FARMER_CAVE_COMPLETE_1||random NPC flavor dialogue line 1 from kFarmerCaveCompleteLines|Goblins gone. Now the fence can be ordinary trouble again.
NPC_LINE_FARMER_CAVE_COMPLETE_2||random NPC flavor dialogue line 2 from kFarmerCaveCompleteLines|Chief's dead, they say. Good. The sheep still stare at the cave like it owes them money.
NPC_LINE_FARMER_CAVE_COMPLETE_3||random NPC flavor dialogue line 3 from kFarmerCaveCompleteLines|If wagons come back, maybe seed prices stop climbing like ivy.
NPC_LINE_BEGGAR_1||random NPC flavor dialogue line 1 from kBeggarLines|Spare a copper? I can make one coin argue with hunger till dusk.
NPC_LINE_BEGGAR_2||random NPC flavor dialogue line 2 from kBeggarLines|New faces pass. The kind ones look ashamed before they say no.
NPC_LINE_BEGGAR_3||random NPC flavor dialogue line 3 from kBeggarLines|Hunger teaches the village map. I know which doors smell of bread.
NPC_LINE_BEGGAR_4||random NPC flavor dialogue line 4 from kBeggarLines|Cold ground does not care for dignity. A spare blanket does.
NPC_LINE_BEGGAR_CAVE_COMPLETE_1||random NPC flavor dialogue line 1 from kBeggarCaveCompleteLines|Goblins gone, and the road remembers coin. Even pity spends better now.
NPC_LINE_BEGGAR_CAVE_COMPLETE_2||random NPC flavor dialogue line 2 from kBeggarCaveCompleteLines|Fewer empty hands on the east track. That means more soup for the ones left.
NPC_LINE_BEGGAR_CAVE_COMPLETE_3||random NPC flavor dialogue line 3 from kBeggarCaveCompleteLines|Chief's dead. The village looks at the road like it might forgive us.
NPC_LINE_DRIFTER_1||random NPC flavor dialogue line 1 from kDrifterLines|East-road ditches turn up buckles, arrows, and lies every dawn.
NPC_LINE_DRIFTER_2||random NPC flavor dialogue line 2 from kDrifterLines|Drivers pass the ridge quiet. A man can hear fear through cart wheels.
NPC_LINE_DRIFTER_3||random NPC flavor dialogue line 3 from kDrifterLines|The cave took packs, tack, and one red mule mean enough to be missed.
NPC_LINE_DRIFTER_4||random NPC flavor dialogue line 4 from kDrifterLines|Wind from the east brings voices some nights. I sleep where it cannot find both ears.
NPC_LINE_DRIFTER_5||random NPC flavor dialogue line 5 from kDrifterLines|Low path after dark? No. The brush there watches back.
NPC_LINE_DRIFTER_CAVE_COMPLETE_1||random NPC flavor dialogue line 1 from kDrifterCaveCompleteLines|Goblins gone. The ditches hold rainwater instead of boots now.
NPC_LINE_DRIFTER_CAVE_COMPLETE_2||random NPC flavor dialogue line 2 from kDrifterCaveCompleteLines|Chief's dead. I still watch the brush, but now it feels like habit.
NPC_LINE_DRIFTER_CAVE_COMPLETE_3||random NPC flavor dialogue line 3 from kDrifterCaveCompleteLines|Wagoners linger by the ridge again. One even laughed before checking over his shoulder.
NPC_LINE_PEDDLER_1||random NPC flavor dialogue line 1 from kPeddlerLines|You probably wonder how I keep turning up first. Mostly I just walk a lot.
NPC_LINE_PEDDLER_2||random NPC flavor dialogue line 2 from kPeddlerLines|I get around. Somebody has to carry the odd bits between towns.
NPC_LINE_PEDDLER_3||random NPC flavor dialogue line 3 from kPeddlerLines|Funny thing about the road: leave early enough and you look quick.
NPC_LINE_HALF_ORC_HUMAN_1||random NPC flavor dialogue line 1 from kHumanHalfOrcLines|State your business and keep your hands where folk can see them.
NPC_LINE_HALF_ORC_HUMAN_2||random NPC flavor dialogue line 2 from kHumanHalfOrcLines|If you are passing through, pass. The road is wide enough without talk.
NPC_LINE_HALF_ORC_HUMAN_3||random NPC flavor dialogue line 3 from kHumanHalfOrcLines|I have nothing for orc blood today. Try someone braver or poorer.
NPC_LINE_HALF_ORC_HUMAN_4||random NPC flavor dialogue line 4 from kHumanHalfOrcLines|People remember raids longer than they remember names. Do not stand so close.
NPC_LINE_HALF_ORC_HUMAN_5||random NPC flavor dialogue line 5 from kHumanHalfOrcLines|You may have done good work. My door still has children behind it.
NPC_LINE_HALF_ORC_HUMAN_RELIGIOUS_1||random NPC flavor dialogue line 1 from kHumanReligiousHalfOrcLines|The Seal weighs deeds, but men at gates weigh faces first. Walk carefully.
NPC_LINE_HALF_ORC_HUMAN_RELIGIOUS_2||random NPC flavor dialogue line 2 from kHumanReligiousHalfOrcLines|The White Seal does not ask easy blood. It asks whether the hand holds.
NPC_LINE_HALF_ORC_HUMAN_RELIGIOUS_3||random NPC flavor dialogue line 3 from kHumanReligiousHalfOrcLines|If the altar has room for old sins, it has room for hard lineage. Earn your place there.
NPC_LINE_HALF_ORC_PRAGMATIC_1||random NPC flavor dialogue line 1 from kPragmaticHalfOrcLines|Coin first, blood after. That rule keeps the stall standing.
NPC_LINE_HALF_ORC_PRAGMATIC_2||random NPC flavor dialogue line 2 from kPragmaticHalfOrcLines|Your look scares fools away. For some trades, that is almost a discount.
NPC_LINE_HALF_ORC_PRAGMATIC_3||random NPC flavor dialogue line 3 from kPragmaticHalfOrcLines|Road mud covers every blood the same. Town walls are fussier.
NPC_LINE_HALF_ORC_PRAGMATIC_4||random NPC flavor dialogue line 4 from kPragmaticHalfOrcLines|I sell to hands that pay and keep steel sheathed. You manage both, we have no quarrel.
NPC_LINE_HALF_ORC_CHILD_1||random NPC flavor dialogue line 1 from kChildHalfOrcLines|Ma says not to stare at tusks. I was not staring. Much.
NPC_LINE_HALF_ORC_CHILD_2||random NPC flavor dialogue line 2 from kChildHalfOrcLines|Pa says orc blood runs hot. Is that why the dogs bark first?
NPC_LINE_HALF_ORC_DWARF_1||random NPC flavor dialogue line 1 from kDwarfHalfOrcLines|Orc blood in my hall? Keep walking.
NPC_LINE_HALF_ORC_DWARF_2||random NPC flavor dialogue line 2 from kDwarfHalfOrcLines|The range keeps its scars under names and dates. Yours wakes an old column.
NPC_LINE_HALF_ORC_DWARF_3||random NPC flavor dialogue line 3 from kDwarfHalfOrcLines|Deep stairs are not barred for poetry. Too many tusks came up them with axes once.
NPC_LINE_HALF_ORC_DWARF_4||random NPC flavor dialogue line 4 from kDwarfHalfOrcLines|Iron will take your grip. Clan trust is a harder metal and slower to heat.
NPC_LINE_HALF_ORC_DWARF_5||random NPC flavor dialogue line 5 from kDwarfHalfOrcLines|Do good work and the foreman may nod. Do not expect the wall-carvings to forgive you.
NPC_LINE_HALF_ORC_ELF_1||random NPC flavor dialogue line 1 from kElfHalfOrcLines|The wards hear two inheritances in one tread. They will not be hurried into trust.
NPC_LINE_HALF_ORC_ELF_2||random NPC flavor dialogue line 2 from kElfHalfOrcLines|The path permits you. The grove has not mistaken permission for welcome.
NPC_LINE_HALF_ORC_ELF_3||random NPC flavor dialogue line 3 from kElfHalfOrcLines|Old boundaries were written after old griefs. Your step reads loudly against them.
NPC_LINE_HALF_ORC_ELF_4||random NPC flavor dialogue line 4 from kElfHalfOrcLines|Speak softly near the hidden ways. Suspicion needs very little help here.
NPC_LINE_HALF_ORC_SOLDIER_1||random NPC flavor dialogue line 1 from kSoldierHalfOrcLines|Clear the line. Shields need room.
NPC_LINE_HALF_ORC_SOLDIER_2||random NPC flavor dialogue line 2 from kSoldierHalfOrcLines|If the horn sounds, you move where I point. Blood can argue after the line holds.
NPC_LINE_HALF_ORC_SOLDIER_3||random NPC flavor dialogue line 3 from kSoldierHalfOrcLines|The Scar takes any hand that holds steel. The gate takes notes all the same.
NPC_LINE_HALF_ORC_SOLDIER_4||random NPC flavor dialogue line 4 from kSoldierHalfOrcLines|Fight clean and report clean. That buys more trust here than ancestry ever will.
NPC_LINE_STONECLEFT_FILLER_1||random NPC flavor dialogue line 1 from kStonecleftFillerLines|The mess line starts after shift change. If you smell barley, you are heading the right way.
NPC_LINE_STONECLEFT_FILLER_2||random NPC flavor dialogue line 2 from kStonecleftFillerLines|Commons crew is short two haulers. Watch for carts cutting across the road.
NPC_LINE_STONECLEFT_FILLER_3||random NPC flavor dialogue line 3 from kStonecleftFillerLines|Dorran has the armory locked again. If you need enchanted steel, ask him, not the counter clerk.
NPC_LINE_STONECLEFT_FILLER_4||random NPC flavor dialogue line 4 from kStonecleftFillerLines|Keep your lamp hooded by the lower gate. The guards count faces, not glare.
NPC_LINE_STONECLEFT_FILLER_5||random NPC flavor dialogue line 5 from kStonecleftFillerLines|Fresh chalk means open work. Red chalk means do not touch the stone.
NPC_LINE_STONECLEFT_FILLER_6||random NPC flavor dialogue line 6 from kStonecleftFillerLines|The cistern crews came up wet and angry. Nobody likes water in a forge hold.
NPC_LINE_STONECLEFT_FILLER_7||random NPC flavor dialogue line 7 from kStonecleftFillerLines|If Bera shouts your name, you forgot a tab or left mud on her floor.
NPC_LINE_STONECLEFT_FILLER_8||random NPC flavor dialogue line 8 from kStonecleftFillerLines|Underway carts are backed up below. Every crate has a mark and every mark has a clerk.
NPC_LINE_STONECLEFT_FILLER_9||random NPC flavor dialogue line 9 from kStonecleftFillerLines|Stonecleft eats boot nails. Buy spares before the road buys them for you.
NPC_LINE_STONECLEFT_FILLER_10||random NPC flavor dialogue line 10 from kStonecleftFillerLines|North road talk goes through Throkk first. He knows which gate is lying.
NPC_LINE_STONECLEFT_MASON_1||random NPC flavor dialogue line 1 from kStonecleftMasonLines|Durn says the west wall is sound. The east wall is sound enough if no one drills new holes in it.
NPC_LINE_STONECLEFT_MASON_2||random NPC flavor dialogue line 2 from kStonecleftMasonLines|Need Durn? Follow the chalk and the plumb line. Need a wider door? Bring wedges and four sober backs.
NPC_LINE_STONECLEFT_MASON_3||random NPC flavor dialogue line 3 from kStonecleftMasonLines|That arch is old imperial work under dwarf repair. Look at the left spring stone; our cut is cleaner.
NPC_LINE_STONECLEFT_MINER_1||random NPC flavor dialogue line 1 from kStonecleftMinerLines|Lift crew is late again. Ask the lower gate guard, not me.
NPC_LINE_STONECLEFT_MINER_2||random NPC flavor dialogue line 2 from kStonecleftMinerLines|Ore carts get right of way. People heal faster than axles.
NPC_LINE_STONECLEFT_MINER_3||random NPC flavor dialogue line 3 from kStonecleftMinerLines|If you hear three taps from below, stand clear of the chain run.
NPC_LINE_STONECLEFT_MINER_4||random NPC flavor dialogue line 4 from kStonecleftMinerLines|Vark has crews counting props, not stories. If he sends you somewhere, take a helmet.
NPC_LINE_STONECLEFT_GUARD_FLAVOR_1||random NPC flavor dialogue line 1 from kStonecleftGuardFlavorLines|Keep to the main hall. The side doors are work rooms, not shortcuts.
NPC_LINE_STONECLEFT_GUARD_FLAVOR_2||random NPC flavor dialogue line 2 from kStonecleftGuardFlavorLines|Keep moving near the lower gate. The watch is counting loads and faces.
NPC_LINE_STONECLEFT_GUARD_FLAVOR_3||random NPC flavor dialogue line 3 from kStonecleftGuardFlavorLines|No loose packs by the stair. If it is yours, carry it; if it is not, leave it.
NPC_LINE_STONECLEFT_GUARD_FLAVOR_4||random NPC flavor dialogue line 4 from kStonecleftGuardFlavorLines|If the cart crew shouts twice, clear the middle track.
NPC_LINE_TELWYND_WARDWORK_1||random NPC flavor dialogue line 1 from kTelwyndWardworkLines|The outer wards accepted dawn poorly. Something crossed near the glassroot and left no scent.
NPC_LINE_TELWYND_WARDWORK_2||random NPC flavor dialogue line 2 from kTelwyndWardworkLines|Do not step over silver twine. It is not decoration, and it dislikes apology.
NPC_LINE_TELWYND_WARDWORK_3||random NPC flavor dialogue line 3 from kTelwyndWardworkLines|Old wards wake for old names. New feet must wait until the grove decides how much to hear.
NPC_LINE_TELWYND_WARDWORK_4||random NPC flavor dialogue line 4 from kTelwyndWardworkLines|The hidden ways remember intrusion more clearly than welcome. We tend that memory with care.
NPC_LINE_TELWYND_PATH_1||random NPC flavor dialogue line 1 from kTelwyndPathLines|The path through the Veiled Wood is quiet. Quiet is not peace; it is the wood listening before it answers.
NPC_LINE_TELWYND_PATH_2||random NPC flavor dialogue line 2 from kTelwyndPathLines|The forest path rewards patience. Hurry, and you find the wrong clearing.
NPC_LINE_TELWYND_PATH_3||random NPC flavor dialogue line 3 from kTelwyndPathLines|Rain loosens more than mud. We walk the side trails after storms and close what opened.
NPC_LINE_TELWYND_PATH_4||random NPC flavor dialogue line 4 from kTelwyndPathLines|Straight lines through these trees usually mean someone is lost. Telwynd owes strangers no rescue.
NPC_LINE_TELWYND_WORKER_1||random NPC flavor dialogue line 1 from kTelwyndWorkerLines|Leaf fall hides the old footway. We clear only enough for guests who are expected.
NPC_LINE_TELWYND_WORKER_2||random NPC flavor dialogue line 2 from kTelwyndWorkerLines|Pool silt drinks moonlight if it lies too long. Patient hands remove it before the ward dulls.
NPC_LINE_TELWYND_WORKER_3||random NPC flavor dialogue line 3 from kTelwyndWorkerLines|Green shoots cross every line they can. Growth is not innocence; we prune it all the same.
NPC_LINE_TELWYND_WORKER_4||random NPC flavor dialogue line 4 from kTelwyndWorkerLines|Resin, twine, and old songs hold the low boughs. Axes are for people with short memories.
NPC_LINE_TELWYND_CHILD_1||random NPC flavor dialogue line 1 from kTelwyndChildLines|The gate wardens know where visitors may walk. I know because I tried every shortcut.
NPC_LINE_TELWYND_CHILD_2||random NPC flavor dialogue line 2 from kTelwyndChildLines|Dark roots sleep under the benches. They twitch when grown folk lie about being calm.
NPC_LINE_STONECLEFT_LOWER_PASSAGE_1||random NPC flavor dialogue line 1 from kStonecleftLowerPassageLines|The lower pass is open, but not friendly. Keep lamps fed and hands clear of side cuts.
NPC_LINE_STONECLEFT_LOWER_PASSAGE_2||random NPC flavor dialogue line 2 from kStonecleftLowerPassageLines|Blackglass shows in the lower work. Step around it and report any fresh growth.
NPC_LINE_STONECLEFT_LOWER_PASSAGE_3||random NPC flavor dialogue line 3 from kStonecleftLowerPassageLines|If you are bound for Highmark, keep north through the Underway and ignore the old cart ruts.
NPC_LINE_KESTREL_FIELD_SUPPLIER_1||random NPC flavor dialogue line 1 from kKestrelFieldSupplierLines|Spearheads, boot nails, lamp oil. If a patrol forgets it, the Scar teaches the lesson.
NPC_LINE_KESTREL_FIELD_SUPPLIER_2||random NPC flavor dialogue line 2 from kKestrelFieldSupplierLines|Rations go out by weight. Stories come back heavier and do not feed anyone.
NPC_LINE_KESTREL_FIELD_SUPPLIER_3||random NPC flavor dialogue line 3 from kKestrelFieldSupplierLines|Patched mail still turns small teeth. I save the sound pieces for people who listen.
NPC_LINE_KESTREL_GUARD_1||random NPC flavor dialogue line 1 from kKestrelGuardLines|Hold the road edge. Wagons and wounded get right of way through this gate.
NPC_LINE_KESTREL_GUARD_2||random NPC flavor dialogue line 2 from kKestrelGuardLines|If blackglass starts cracking under your boots, step back and call the line.
NPC_LINE_KESTREL_GUARD_3||random NPC flavor dialogue line 3 from kKestrelGuardLines|One horn closes the camp. Two horns put every Lancer on the wall.
NPC_LINE_KESTREL_GUARD_4||random NPC flavor dialogue line 4 from kKestrelGuardLines|Captain Vaust wants reports short: what you saw, where, and whether it moves.
NPC_LINE_KESTREL_GUARD_5||random NPC flavor dialogue line 5 from kKestrelGuardLines|No one walks the west road alone after dusk. That rule cost enough to keep.
NPC_LINE_KESTREL_SCOUT_1||random NPC flavor dialogue line 1 from kKestrelScoutLines|The west patrol line shifts after the Scar breathes. Watch which way the grass refuses.
NPC_LINE_KESTREL_SCOUT_2||random NPC flavor dialogue line 2 from kKestrelScoutLines|Fog cuts sight before it cuts sound. Trust boots, not eyes.
NPC_LINE_KESTREL_SCOUT_3||random NPC flavor dialogue line 3 from kKestrelScoutLines|Tracks vanish near the black grit. That does not mean the patrol flew away.
NPC_LINE_KESTREL_SCOUT_4||random NPC flavor dialogue line 4 from kKestrelScoutLines|Fog west of the Scar moves against the wind. Report that calmly and captains stop smiling.
NPC_LINE_KESTREL_SCOUT_5||random NPC flavor dialogue line 5 from kKestrelScoutLines|Old paths sink under ash after noon. Test with the spear butt before you trust a boot.
NPC_LINE_KESTREL_SCOUT_6||random NPC flavor dialogue line 6 from kKestrelScoutLines|The wood keeps old campfire smoke under its bark. If you smell it, turn back.
NPC_LINE_KESTREL_SAPPER_1||random NPC flavor dialogue line 1 from kKestrelSapperLines|Charges make doors. Braces decide whether those doors become graves.
NPC_LINE_KESTREL_SAPPER_2||random NPC flavor dialogue line 2 from kKestrelSapperLines|Dust on a pick is honest. Dust falling from a silent ceiling is not.
NPC_LINE_KESTREL_SAPPER_3||random NPC flavor dialogue line 3 from kKestrelSapperLines|When a brace starts talking, you leave. Stone gives warnings only once.
NPC_LINE_KESTREL_SAPPER_4||random NPC flavor dialogue line 4 from kKestrelSapperLines|Old fire cracked the walls before we got here. We just find the places still angry.
NPC_LINE_KESTREL_SAPPER_5||random NPC flavor dialogue line 5 from kKestrelSapperLines|If the prop bows inward, do not pray over it. Wedge, shout, and move.
NPC_LINE_KESTREL_WORKER_1||random NPC flavor dialogue line 1 from kKestrelWorkerLines|Rope, water, spear shafts: half the camp is dull work, so the sharp work can happen.
NPC_LINE_KESTREL_WORKER_2||random NPC flavor dialogue line 2 from kKestrelWorkerLines|Ash piles on crates, pots, boots, and teeth. We sweep so we can see what changed.
NPC_LINE_KESTREL_WORKER_3||random NPC flavor dialogue line 3 from kKestrelWorkerLines|Returns come back short of hands. The line still needs carrying.
NPC_LINE_KESTREL_WORKER_4||random NPC flavor dialogue line 4 from kKestrelWorkerLines|Tunnel spoil blocks every path twice: once when it falls, once when officers argue about it.
NPC_LINE_KESTREL_SMITH_1||random NPC flavor dialogue line 1 from kKestrelSmithLines|The anvil stays hot because the line keeps breaking teeth on iron.
NPC_LINE_KESTREL_SMITH_2||random NPC flavor dialogue line 2 from kKestrelSmithLines|Torn mail gets patched if it saved skin. If it failed, it goes in the scrap bin without ceremony.
NPC_LINE_KESTREL_SMITH_3||random NPC flavor dialogue line 3 from kKestrelSmithLines|Wagons lag, coal thins, and captains still want miracles before dawn.
NPC_LINE_KESTREL_SMITH_4||random NPC flavor dialogue line 4 from kKestrelSmithLines|Old tunnel iron rings wrong under the hammer. Too eager, like it remembers a worse forge.
NPC_LINE_KESTREL_MEDICAL_1||random NPC flavor dialogue line 1 from kKestrelMedicalLines|Stretchers come in after quiet calls. Loud calls give people warning.
NPC_LINE_KESTREL_MEDICAL_2||random NPC flavor dialogue line 2 from kKestrelMedicalLines|Tunnel wounds rot slowly and lie politely until midnight.
NPC_LINE_KESTREL_MEDICAL_3||random NPC flavor dialogue line 3 from kKestrelMedicalLines|Fog cases are the worst. No bite, no fever, just men shaking like something followed them home.
NPC_LINE_KESTREL_MEDICAL_4||random NPC flavor dialogue line 4 from kKestrelMedicalLines|If you can joke, you can wait. If you stop joking, I find a surgeon.
NPC_LINE_KESTREL_ORDERLY_1||random NPC flavor dialogue line 1 from kKestrelOrderlyLines|The aid-station cots are clean enough. That is the highest compliment they get.
NPC_LINE_KESTREL_ORDERLY_2||random NPC flavor dialogue line 2 from kKestrelOrderlyLines|If you are bleeding, sit down before a surgeon has to tell you twice.
NPC_LINE_KESTREL_ORDERLY_3||random NPC flavor dialogue line 3 from kKestrelOrderlyLines|Fresh straw under a cot can make a wounded Lancer believe in civilization again.
NPC_LINE_KESTREL_ORDERLY_4||random NPC flavor dialogue line 4 from kKestrelOrderlyLines|Mud from the breach road dries black on the planks. We scrub until it looks ordinary.
NPC_LINE_GENERIC_NPC_1||random NPC flavor dialogue line 1 from kGenericNpcLines|Wagons roll through lighter every season. Folks still wave like that fools the road.
NPC_LINE_GENERIC_NPC_2||random NPC flavor dialogue line 2 from kGenericNpcLines|Strangers with maps stop in the square. The dogs remember more names than we do.
NPC_LINE_CHILD_1||random NPC flavor dialogue line 1 from kChildLines|Pa says the cave took three sheep. I named one, so I count it twice.
NPC_LINE_CHILD_2||random NPC flavor dialogue line 2 from kChildLines|The east path ate the goats. I saw prints like little knives before the rain.
NPC_LINE_CHILD_3||random NPC flavor dialogue line 3 from kChildLines|Pa says the cave chief marks names on the wall. I only whisper mine indoors.
NPC_LINE_CHILD_CAVE_STARTED_1||random NPC flavor dialogue line 1 from kChildCaveStartedLines|The gate man took rope and blade east. Ma put bread by the door for luck.
NPC_LINE_CHILD_CAVE_STARTED_2||random NPC flavor dialogue line 2 from kChildCaveStartedLines|A stranger hunts the cave chief now. I saw the lamp go small between the trees.
NPC_LINE_CHILD_CAVE_COMPLETE_1||random NPC flavor dialogue line 1 from kChildCaveCompleteLines|Pa says the chief is dead. I told the sheep, but they already knew.
NPC_LINE_CHILD_CAVE_COMPLETE_2||random NPC flavor dialogue line 2 from kChildCaveCompleteLines|Chief's dead. I still keep the stick, but now it is for practice.
NPC_LINE_DOG_1||random NPC flavor dialogue line 1 from kDogLines|The dog sniffs once, sneezes, and faces the east fence.
NPC_LINE_DOG_2||random NPC flavor dialogue line 2 from kDogLines|The dog circles your boots, decides you are complicated, and sits by the post.
NPC_LINE_GOAT_1||random NPC flavor dialogue line 1 from kGoatLines|The goat butts the post like it has a legal grievance.
NPC_LINE_GOAT_2||random NPC flavor dialogue line 2 from kGoatLines|The goat tugs its tether and studies your pack with criminal hope.
NPC_LINE_CHICKEN_1||random NPC flavor dialogue line 1 from kChickenLines|The chicken pecks once, judges the dust, and flutters onto the rail.
NPC_LINE_CHICKEN_2||random NPC flavor dialogue line 2 from kChickenLines|The chicken hops the rail, steals a grain, and denies everything.
NPC_LINE_MULE_1||random NPC flavor dialogue line 1 from kMuleLines|The mule stamps once and gives the load a look usually saved for tax collectors.
NPC_LINE_MULE_2||random NPC flavor dialogue line 2 from kMuleLines|The mule snorts toward the open path, then remembers it dislikes paths too.
NPC_LINE_DOCK_RUMOR_1||random NPC flavor dialogue line 1 from kDockRumorLines|Nets come up thin. The shoals feel like something counted the fish first.
NPC_LINE_DOCK_RUMOR_2||random NPC flavor dialogue line 2 from kDockRumorLines|Boats from the south run late. Captains blame Scar winds when they do not want questions.
NPC_LINE_DOCK_RUMOR_3||random NPC flavor dialogue line 3 from kDockRumorLines|Havenford wagons come back short of hands. The road charges more than toll.
NPC_LINE_DOCK_RUMOR_4||random NPC flavor dialogue line 4 from kDockRumorLines|The cellar moves crates after last watch. Anyone who hears it suddenly remembers chores.
NPC_LINE_DOCK_RUMOR_5||random NPC flavor dialogue line 5 from kDockRumorLines|Blackglass tugs wet lines. Old netmen feel it in the wrist before the mesh tears.
NPC_LINE_DOCK_RUMOR_6||random NPC flavor dialogue line 6 from kDockRumorLines|Dragons or no dragons, inland roads eat caravans. Water at least spits wreckage back.
NPC_LINE_PEASANT_STORE_1||random NPC flavor dialogue line 1 from kPeasantStoreLines|The boat takes the handsome barrels. We buy the ugly ones and hope ugly means full.
NPC_LINE_PEASANT_STORE_2||random NPC flavor dialogue line 2 from kPeasantStoreLines|Sealed casks go to captains. Stained grain goes to people with pots and no pride.
NPC_LINE_PEASANT_STORE_3||random NPC flavor dialogue line 3 from kPeasantStoreLines|Axes sell before noon. After that, a hammer learns new duties.
NPC_LINE_PEASANT_ROAD_1||random NPC flavor dialogue line 1 from kPeasantRoadLines|Wheels sink in washouts. Everyone pushes except the merchant who owns the wheels.
NPC_LINE_PEASANT_ROAD_2||random NPC flavor dialogue line 2 from kPeasantRoadLines|Dogs will not cross the ridge at dusk. Sensible beasts, dogs.
NPC_LINE_PEASANT_ROAD_3||random NPC flavor dialogue line 3 from kPeasantRoadLines|When wagons turn back before fog, nobody calls the driver coward until he is out of earshot.
NPC_LINE_PEASANT_ROAD_4||random NPC flavor dialogue line 4 from kPeasantRoadLines|Road stones shift under load. Walk center, speak little, and let the cart complain.
NPC_LINE_PEASANT_DOCK_1||random NPC flavor dialogue line 1 from kPeasantDockLines|Moorings slip at tide turn. We drive stakes like the river owes us rent.
NPC_LINE_PEASANT_DOCK_2||random NPC flavor dialogue line 2 from kPeasantDockLines|Unclaimed crates sit on the quay until someone important forgets they lost them.
NPC_LINE_PEASANT_DOCK_3||random NPC flavor dialogue line 3 from kPeasantDockLines|Wet line eats skin fast. Wrap cloth or feed the rope.
NPC_LINE_PEASANT_FIGHT_1||random NPC flavor dialogue line 1 from kPeasantFightLines|We swing at posts after drills. Posts never duck, which makes them better teachers than cousins.
NPC_LINE_PEASANT_FIGHT_2||random NPC flavor dialogue line 2 from kPeasantFightLines|The yard is safer than the ridge. That is why the smart ones practice there first.
NPC_LINE_PEASANT_FIGHT_3||random NPC flavor dialogue line 3 from kPeasantFightLines|They call it practice. Last season's missing called it enough, too.
NPC_LINE_PEASANT_TRAVEL_1||random NPC flavor dialogue line 1 from kPeasantTravelLines|Light loads go on backs. Heavy carts wait for blades with names.
NPC_LINE_PEASANT_TRAVEL_2||random NPC flavor dialogue line 2 from kPeasantTravelLines|The ridge takes a share before walls show. Best pay attention before it chooses the price.
NPC_LINE_PEASANT_TRAVEL_3||random NPC flavor dialogue line 3 from kPeasantTravelLines|Fog swallows the path before noon. We walk by straps and curses.
NPC_LINE_HIGHMARK_PEASANT_1||random NPC flavor dialogue line 1 from kHighmarkPeasantLines|Silver Lances pass at dawn. Sweepers know the order by spur marks alone.
NPC_LINE_HIGHMARK_PEASANT_2||random NPC flavor dialogue line 2 from kHighmarkPeasantLines|Provision trains leave fat and come back hollow. The quartermasters still ask us to smile.
NPC_LINE_HIGHMARK_PEASANT_3||random NPC flavor dialogue line 3 from kHighmarkPeasantLines|White Seal priests clear the square after dusk. The stones hum, and nobody admits hearing it.
NPC_LINE_HIGHMARK_PEASANT_4||random NPC flavor dialogue line 4 from kHighmarkPeasantLines|The eastern gate sees more litters than wagons some days. We learn not to count faces.
NPC_LINE_HIGHMARK_PEASANT_5||random NPC flavor dialogue line 5 from kHighmarkPeasantLines|Every able hand gets asked for Scar work. Every unable hand gets asked what it can carry.
NPC_LINE_HIGHMARK_PEASANT_6||random NPC flavor dialogue line 6 from kHighmarkPeasantLines|Drums reach the lower streets before the lancers form. Children learn that rhythm too young.
NPC_LINE_HIGHMARK_PEASANT_7||random NPC flavor dialogue line 7 from kHighmarkPeasantLines|Scar wagons unload before dawn. Covered shapes go one way, empty blankets another.
NPC_LINE_TRAVELLERS_REST_TRAVELLER_1||random NPC flavor dialogue line 1 from kTravellersRestTravellerLines|South wagons arrive later each season. Nobody says the road is hungry until after the second drink.
NPC_LINE_TRAVELLERS_REST_TRAVELLER_2||random NPC flavor dialogue line 2 from kTravellersRestTravellerLines|The north ridges tighten before noon. You can feel the pack straps start lying.
NPC_LINE_TRAVELLERS_REST_TRAVELLER_3||random NPC flavor dialogue line 3 from kTravellersRestTravellerLines|Yard benches are for people who keep moving. Sleep too deeply and the road forgets you.
NPC_LINE_TRAVELLERS_REST_TRAVELLER_4||random NPC flavor dialogue line 4 from kTravellersRestTravellerLines|Highmark caravans rest animals here. Men count heads. Mules count grudges.
NPC_LINE_TRAVELLERS_REST_TRAVELLER_5||random NPC flavor dialogue line 5 from kTravellersRestTravellerLines|Drake signs show on high slopes after rain. Low fires, loose blades, no boasting.
NPC_LINE_TRAVELLERS_REST_TRAVELLER_6||random NPC flavor dialogue line 6 from kTravellersRestTravellerLines|Blackglass glints by the old road cuts. Walk past it and wash your hands anyway.
NPC_LINE_TRAVELLERS_REST_TRAVELLER_7||random NPC flavor dialogue line 7 from kTravellersRestTravellerLines|The stone-reader pays for odd finds. Small pieces buy supper; big pieces buy trouble.
NPC_LINE_TRAVELLERS_REST_TRAVELLER_8||random NPC flavor dialogue line 8 from kTravellersRestTravellerLines|Highmark is a word that buys drinks. Seeing Highmark is dearer.
NPC_LINE_TRAVELLERS_REST_RESEARCHER_1||random NPC flavor dialogue line 1 from kTravellersRestResearcherLines|Reedmire's water stones are not folk superstition. Superstition rarely arranges itself in shrine geometry.
NPC_LINE_TRAVELLERS_REST_RESEARCHER_2||random NPC flavor dialogue line 2 from kTravellersRestResearcherLines|Clean blackglass is rare. Most shards lie, but the pure ones sing the shape of whatever broke them.
NPC_LINE_TRAVELLERS_REST_RESEARCHER_3||random NPC flavor dialogue line 3 from kTravellersRestResearcherLines|The Rest is quiet enough for notes and loud enough that nobody hears me argue with them.
NPC_LINE_TRAVELLERS_REST_RESEARCHER_4||random NPC flavor dialogue line 4 from kTravellersRestResearcherLines|The bandit fort downroad sits on older stone. Criminals have such a gift for nesting on evidence.
NPC_LINE_TRAVELLERS_REST_RESEARCHER_5||random NPC flavor dialogue line 5 from kTravellersRestResearcherLines|Magic is not a source, it is a behavior. Blackglass behaves as if it remembers being commanded.
NPC_LINE_TRAVELLERS_REST_SHADY_1||random NPC flavor dialogue line 1 from kTravellersRestShadyLines|Faces pass the benches and come back with different pockets.
NPC_LINE_TRAVELLERS_REST_SHADY_2||random NPC flavor dialogue line 2 from kTravellersRestShadyLines|Coin wanting no witness drinks after the second lamp.
NPC_LINE_TRAVELLERS_REST_SHADY_3||random NPC flavor dialogue line 3 from kTravellersRestShadyLines|Door watchers drink slowly. Leaving before the yard fills is how they speak.
NPC_LINE_TRAVELLERS_REST_SHADY_4||random NPC flavor dialogue line 4 from kTravellersRestShadyLines|What fits in a cloak pocket travels well. What whispers stays buried.
NPC_LINE_TIDEHOOK_NETMENDER_1||random NPC flavor dialogue line 1 from kTidehookNetmenderLines|Cut bad knots while the line is warm. Cold rope lies better.
NPC_LINE_TIDEHOOK_NETMENDER_2||random NPC flavor dialogue line 2 from kTidehookNetmenderLines|Deep lines come back with weed, bone chips, and fewer fish than promised.
NPC_LINE_TIDEHOOK_NETMENDER_3||random NPC flavor dialogue line 3 from kTidehookNetmenderLines|Tar holds when new twine slips. Boil the coils and do not breathe too proudly.
NPC_LINE_TIDEHOOK_NETMENDER_4||random NPC flavor dialogue line 4 from kTidehookNetmenderLines|Skiffs drag torn nets home like wounded flags. We patch first and ask names later.
NPC_LINE_TIDEHOOK_NETMENDER_5||random NPC flavor dialogue line 5 from kTidehookNetmenderLines|North wind tastes of iron before boats show. Tie the yard lines short.
NPC_LINE_PORTER_1||random NPC flavor dialogue line 1 from kPorterLines|A patched strap cuts deeper on uphill streets. Shift early or bleed through your sleeve.
NPC_LINE_PORTER_2||random NPC flavor dialogue line 2 from kPorterLines|White Seal tags move before rain, weddings, and hungry children. In that order.
NPC_LINE_PORTER_3||random NPC flavor dialogue line 3 from kPorterLines|Scar camps call for rope every hour. Rope, then hands, then more rope.
NPC_LINE_LABORER_1||random NPC flavor dialogue line 1 from kLaborerLines|Lime sets fast when the wind is up. Mix small or chip your mistake out tomorrow.
NPC_LINE_LABORER_2||random NPC flavor dialogue line 2 from kLaborerLines|This crate hook lost a tooth. So did I. Both of us still work.
NPC_LINE_LABORER_3||random NPC flavor dialogue line 3 from kLaborerLines|Eastern-road loads leave before the count is full. Better late crates than lost backs.
NPC_LINE_PILGRIM_1||random NPC flavor dialogue line 1 from kPilgrimLines|The prayer cord still carries ridge-shrine dust. I leave it there so the road knows me.
NPC_LINE_PILGRIM_2||random NPC flavor dialogue line 2 from kPilgrimLines|Three altar marks wake the plain charm. The first is hope. The second is blisters.
NPC_LINE_PILGRIM_3||random NPC flavor dialogue line 3 from kPilgrimLines|The token stays wrapped until prayer. Rain gets into everything else.
NPC_LINE_STABLEHAND_1||random NPC flavor dialogue line 1 from kStablehandLines|The bay mare favors the near fore. She denies it like a lord denies debt.
NPC_LINE_STABLEHAND_2||random NPC flavor dialogue line 2 from kStablehandLines|Travelers ask for news after feed. Horses know the proper order.
NPC_LINE_STABLEHAND_3||random NPC flavor dialogue line 3 from kStablehandLines|Tack oil, hay dust, and lancer temper. That is the stable by noon.
NPC_LINE_HIGHMARK_PRIEST_1||random NPC flavor dialogue line 1 from kHighmarkPriestLines|Blank charms wait under cloth. A road mark taken too early is just vanity with wax on it.
NPC_LINE_HIGHMARK_PRIEST_2||random NPC flavor dialogue line 2 from kHighmarkPriestLines|Pilgrims bring three altars of dust before we speak of deeper work.
NPC_LINE_HIGHMARK_PRIEST_3||random NPC flavor dialogue line 3 from kHighmarkPriestLines|The square clears at dusk because the old seal still listens. We try not to waste its attention.
DIALOGUE_HIGHMARK_PRIEST_PILGRIMAGE_START_CHARM||White Seal Priest first Pilgrimage offer, gives plain charm|Traveler, wait. This plain charm is only blank bone and cord until the road answers it. Take it carefully.
DIALOGUE_HIGHMARK_PRIEST_PILGRIMAGE_START_ROUTE||White Seal Priest first Pilgrimage offer, route instruction|Touch it to the altars in Havenford, at the Roadside Shrine, and at Reedmire. When all three marks warm, bring it back to this cloth.
DIALOGUE_HIGHMARK_PRIEST_PILGRIMAGE_FIRST_MARK_PROGRESS||White Seal Priest Pilgrimage reminder, placeholder 0 marked altar count|The charm holds {0} marks. Three are required before I can set the Oldroot blessing.
DIALOGUE_HIGHMARK_PRIEST_PILGRIMAGE_REPLACE_CHARM||White Seal Priest replaces lost plain charm|Lost the charm? I can cut one more blank, but not endless blanks. Carry it to the unmarked altars and bring it back.
DIALOGUE_HIGHMARK_PRIEST_PILGRIMAGE_BLESS_HANDIN||White Seal Priest blesses marked Pilgrimage charm and gives Oldroot instruction|The road marks are clean. I have set the Oldroot blessing into the charm; take it to the altar in Oldroot Temple.
DIALOGUE_HIGHMARK_PRIEST_PILGRIMAGE_OLDROOT_REMINDER||White Seal Priest reminder while carrying dormant white seal charm|The dormant charm still waits on Oldroot Temple. Touch it to the altar there, then return if it wakes.
DIALOGUE_HIGHMARK_PRIEST_PILGRIMAGE_FINAL_HANDIN||White Seal Priest final Pilgrimage hand-in|Oldroot took the last mark. Set the charm down; I will close the rite before the wax cools.
DIALOGUE_HIGHMARK_PRIEST_PILGRIMAGE_FINAL_BLESSING||White Seal Priest final Pilgrimage reward|The finished charm is yours now. Its blessing should hold better on the road.
DIALOGUE_HIGHMARK_PRIEST_PILGRIMAGE_COMPLETE_IDLE||White Seal Priest idle line after Pilgrimage is complete|Your charm is filed and sealed. I cannot run the same pilgrimage twice for one name.
NPC_LINE_HIGHMARK_LANCER_1||random NPC flavor dialogue line 1 from kHighmarkLancerLines|The inner post holds because it must. Glory is for songs written far from gates.
NPC_LINE_HIGHMARK_LANCER_2||random NPC flavor dialogue line 2 from kHighmarkLancerLines|Scar trains leave heavy and return light. We learn to read empty saddle hooks.
NPC_LINE_HIGHMARK_LANCER_3||random NPC flavor dialogue line 3 from kHighmarkLancerLines|Fresh lancers climb from the southern yards. We fit mail first and pride last.
NPC_LINE_HIGHMARK_LANCER_4||random NPC flavor dialogue line 4 from kHighmarkLancerLines|Blackglass reaches the gate before the canons do. We log the shard, then pretend we did not hear it tick.
NPC_LINE_HIGHMARK_RESEARCHER_1||random NPC flavor dialogue line 1 from kHighmarkResearcherLines|The star answered the prism because the bloodline and old prism agreed. That sentence earns a sealed reprimand if it leaves this room.
NPC_LINE_HIGHMARK_RESEARCHER_2||random NPC flavor dialogue line 2 from kHighmarkResearcherLines|White Seal genealogy, ritual, and confession often share one page. The margins are usually the dangerous part.
NPC_LINE_HIGHMARK_RESEARCHER_3||random NPC flavor dialogue line 3 from kHighmarkResearcherLines|Blackglass is not evil. It is worse for lazy minds: obedient to pressures we barely understand.
NPC_LINE_HIGHMARK_RESEARCHER_4||random NPC flavor dialogue line 4 from kHighmarkResearcherLines|Lightglass is not blessed crystal. It is blackglass brought into order by blood, pattern, and old arithmetic.
NPC_LINE_HIGHMARK_RESEARCHER_5||random NPC flavor dialogue line 5 from kHighmarkResearcherLines|Every time someone says prophecy, I add another lock to the archive. This is inheritance, not permission from heaven.
