LAST_CHANCE_TAGLINE_01|32|last-chance randomized report tagline|Still standing. Barely.
LAST_CHANCE_TAGLINE_02|32|last-chance randomized report tagline|That one was too close.
LAST_CHANCE_TAGLINE_03|40|last-chance randomized report tagline|The amulet earned its keep.
LAST_CHANCE_TAGLINE_04|40|last-chance randomized report tagline|One more turn, one more problem.
LAST_CHANCE_TAGLINE_05|56|last-chance randomized report tagline|A practical reminder to buy better armor.
LAST_CHANCE_TAGLINE_06|40|last-chance randomized report tagline|The run stays alive, somehow.
LAST_CHANCE_TAGLINE_07|40|last-chance randomized report tagline|The retreat plan may need work.
LAST_CHANCE_TAGLINE_08|32|last-chance randomized report tagline|You survived at 1 HP.
LAST_CHANCE_TAGLINE_09|56|last-chance randomized report tagline|Current status: alive and rethinking choices.
LAST_CHANCE_TAGLINE_10|32|last-chance randomized report tagline|The death log can wait.
LAST_CHANCE_TAGLINE_11|48|last-chance randomized report tagline|A clean escape would have been cheaper.
LAST_CHANCE_TAGLINE_12|64|last-chance randomized report tagline|Check armor, bandages, and retreat routes before moving.
LAST_CHANCE_TAGLINE_13|32|last-chance randomized report tagline|The next room can wait.
LAST_CHANCE_TAGLINE_14|40|last-chance randomized report tagline|Good time to check the bandages.
LAST_CHANCE_TAGLINE_15|48|last-chance randomized report tagline|The scorekeeper has to use pencil for now.
LAST_CHANCE_TAGLINE_16|48|last-chance randomized report tagline|A little more caution would be understandable.
LAST_CHANCE_TAGLINE_17|36|last-chance randomized report tagline|The pack still has a pulse.
LAST_CHANCE_TAGLINE_18|56|last-chance randomized report tagline|Find stairs before needing another last chance.
LAST_CHANCE_ACHIEVEMENT_LINE|96|last-chance achievement report line, placeholders 0 use count, 1 max uses, 2 near-death phrase, 3 location|recovered {0:%d}/{1:%d} after {2} in {3}!
LAST_CHANCE_REPORT|112|last-chance Discord report, placeholders 0 use count, 1 max uses, 2 near-death phrase, 3 location, 4 elapsed time|recovered {0:%d}/{1:%d}: {2} in {3} after {4}
# Story dialogue pages
DIALOGUE_ALDREN_POST_WATCHTOWER_IDLE||NPC dialogue in talk_aldren after Watchtower Prism is no longer Aldren's active handoff; Root Breach, Highmark lead, or later story is active/complete|Havenford breathes easier, though I doubt your troubles ended at our gate. If Cael learned more of that amulet, I hope he spoke plainly.
DIALOGUE_ALDREN_CAVE_CHIEF_TURNIN||NPC dialogue in talk_aldren after the cave chief is killed; this page claims the reward, then Watchtower Start is appended|You did it. With the chieftain dead, the goblins lose their nerve and our militia can drive off the stragglers. The farms can mend fences instead of burying stock, and perhaps carts will dare the road to Traveller's Rest again. Take your reward with my thanks, friend.
DIALOGUE_ALDREN_CAVE_CHIEF_TURNIN_HALF_ORC||NPC dialogue in talk_aldren after the cave chief is killed for half-orcs; this page claims the reward, then Watchtower Start is appended|You did the work, and Havenford is safer for it. Some here will still watch your tusks before your deeds; let them watch this deed too. Take the pay. Garrick may have harder work if you want it.
DIALOGUE_ALDREN_CAVE_CHIEF_REMINDER||NPC dialogue in talk_aldren while Cave Chief is active|The eastern cave still sends goblins at our fences. Find the chieftain and end his hold on them.
DIALOGUE_ALDREN_CAVE_CHIEF_START||NPC dialogue in talk_aldren when starting Cave Chief|Welcome, traveler. You have reached Havenford in lean days. Goblins from the cave on the eastern ridge have been raiding farms, tearing fences, and carrying off livestock. They are too organized for ordinary cave vermin; someone in there is driving them. If you can kill that chieftain, we will pay what this village can muster. Take this gold and potion now, and come back alive if you can.
DIALOGUE_ALDREN_CAVE_CHIEF_START_HALF_ORC||NPC dialogue in talk_aldren when a half-orc starts Cave Chief|Traveler. I will not pretend folk here are easy with your kind, but work is work and danger is danger. Goblins in the eastern cave are raiding our farms under a chieftain. Kill him and Havenford will pay you fairly.
DIALOGUE_ALDREN_WATCHTOWER_START||NPC dialogue in talk_aldren appended to Cave Chief turn-in when starting Watchtower Prism; standalone branch is defensive for saves where Cave Chief is complete but Watchtower is not started|There is one more matter, and I do not like speaking of it. The ruined watchtower west of town has stood empty for years, but strange lights now show from its sealed upper room. That is old stone, older than our little worries. I am giving you the old key for the upper stair door. Go carefully, see what woke there, and bring back whatever you find.
DIALOGUE_ALDREN_WATCHTOWER_REMINDER||NPC dialogue in talk_aldren while Watchtower Prism is active before the prism is found|The ruined watchtower still shows lights from the sealed upper room. Use the old key I gave you for the upper stair door, find the cause, and bring it back.
DIALOGUE_ALDREN_WATCHTOWER_REPORT||NPC dialogue in talk_aldren after the player returns with the fractured prism|A fractured prism from the sealed floor? No, that is beyond village business. Your amulet answers its pulse, and I have no learning fit for such a thing.
DIALOGUE_ALDREN_WATCHTOWER_TO_SCHOLAR||NPC dialogue in talk_aldren after sending the player to the Traveller's Rest scholar|Take it to Scholar Cael at Traveller's Rest. He studies old stone, star glass, and other matters I would rather not misname. Follow the north road from town, turn east at the fork, and keep on until you see the inn.
DIALOGUE_MAELIN_SHRINE_SUPPLIES_AFTER_CAVE_CHIEF||NPC dialogue in talk_maelin after Cave Chief is complete|Blessings upon you. With the goblin chief dead, fear has loosened its grip on the commons. My shrine goods are still humble, but they may keep you standing.
DIALOGUE_MAELIN_SHRINE_SUPPLIES_BEFORE_CAVE_CHIEF||NPC dialogue in talk_maelin before Cave Chief is complete|Blessings upon you. Goblin raids have thinned our stores and our sleep alike. I have little, but the White Seal teaches that little must still serve.
DIALOGUE_VETHRIN_REEDMIRE_COMPLETE_IDLE||NPC dialogue in talk_vethrin after Reedmire Delivery is complete|Quiet times in Havenford these days. I do hear worrying things about up north beyond the dwarven gate. Dragons? Truly hard to believe.
DIALOGUE_VETHRIN_REEDMIRE_TURNIN||NPC dialogue in talk_vethrin when Nhalor has been slain|The water came alive? Well this will require further investigation indeed.
DIALOGUE_VETHRIN_REEDMIRE_REMINDER||NPC dialogue in talk_vethrin while Reedmire Delivery is active before Nhalor is slain|Take my note to Reth Oskel at Reedwater Docks. He said he took stones from Reedmire Shrine and the water moved after that. Get his account, then follow what he gives you.
DIALOGUE_VETHRIN_NOTE_REPLACEMENT||NPC dialogue in talk_vethrin when replacing a lost note for Reth|You lost the note? Typical. Yes of course I had a copy prepared, here. Please don't lose it again.
DIALOGUE_VETHRIN_TOO_GREEN||NPC dialogue in talk_vethrin when the player is below the Reedmire quest minimum level|Please leave me to my research.
DIALOGUE_VETHRIN_COTTAGE_TOO_GREEN||NPC dialogue in talk_vethrin when the player is below the Burned Cottage investigation minimum level|Please leave me to my research for now.
DIALOGUE_VETHRIN_COTTAGE_START||NPC dialogue in talk_vethrin when starting the Burned Cottage investigation|I need someone steady to look over the burned cottage. The fire was not ordinary; the ash still carries a magical trace, and the wolves around the ruin are not acting normal. Check the place carefully, then bring me whatever you find.
DIALOGUE_VETHRIN_COTTAGE_REMINDER||NPC dialogue in talk_vethrin while the Burned Cottage investigation is active|The burned cottage still needs eyes on it. Search the ruin carefully, then bring me whatever explains that fire. Watch the wolves; they are not acting normal.
DIALOGUE_VETHRIN_COTTAGE_TURNIN||NPC dialogue in talk_vethrin after the Burned Cottage altar is inspected|Water glyphs under a burned house. Peculiar. You found the truth of it, at least. Take this spellbook; practical payment is harder to misread than theory.
DIALOGUE_VETHRIN_COTTAGE_COMPLETE_IDLE||NPC dialogue in talk_vethrin after the Burned Cottage investigation is complete|I have enough notes on the burned cottage for now. If another cellar starts whispering, I shall try not to send you first.
DIALOGUE_VETHRIN_COTTAGE_REEDMIRE_WAIT||NPC dialogue in talk_vethrin after Burned Cottage is complete but Vethrin is not ready with the next lead|I need to do more research on this. Come see me again later.
DIALOGUE_VETHRIN_REEDMIRE_START||NPC dialogue in talk_vethrin when starting the Reedmire note delivery quest|Reth Oskel is the fisherman. He said he took stacked stones from Reedmire Shrine, and the water came alive after that. Take this sealed note to him at Reedwater Docks. If he still has the stones, get them and find the shrine southeast of the road.
DIALOGUE_VETHRIN_REEDMIRE_TOO_GREEN||NPC dialogue in talk_vethrin before the player is ready for Reedmire|There is a fisherman and a drowned shrine I need checked, but not by someone the marsh could swallow whole. Come back when you have survived a little more road.
DIALOGUE_TESSA_TRAIL_GEAR_AFTER_CAVE_CHIEF||NPC dialogue in talk_tessa after Cave Chief is complete|Hello, friend! The road is less hungry now, so I have more than food and lamp oil back on the rack. Rope, nets, traps, kits, packs: say what you need.
DIALOGUE_TESSA_TRAIL_GEAR_BEFORE_CAVE_CHIEF||NPC dialogue in talk_tessa before Cave Chief is complete|Hello, friend! Goblins still make every crate late, but I keep trail food, rope, light, and a few tools where I can. Get what you need before you head out.
DIALOGUE_BRANNOC_FORGE_STOCK||NPC dialogue in talk_brannoc for forge stock access|Forge is open. Leather, steel, and edges that will not embarrass you.
DIALOGUE_BRANNOC_HAVENFORD_START||NPC dialogue in talk_brannoc when starting Havenford Mines|The Havenford mine is in the eastern mountains. Break the huge boulders on the lower levels so ore can move again. Kobolds are in there, so bring a weapon.
DIALOGUE_BRANNOC_HAVENFORD_REMINDER||NPC dialogue in talk_brannoc while Havenford Mines is active|Havenford Mines, east of town. Break the huge boulders around the lower stairs so ore can move again.
DIALOGUE_BRANNOC_HAVENFORD_TURNIN||NPC dialogue in talk_brannoc after clearing Havenford Mines|That is Havenford stone, all right. Good work. The way is open again.
DIALOGUE_BRANNOC_HAVENFORD_REWARD||NPC dialogue in talk_brannoc after paying Havenford Mines reward|Thanks. Here, take this for your trouble.
DIALOGUE_BRANNOC_HAVENFORD_DONE||NPC dialogue in talk_brannoc after Havenford Mines is complete|Forge is open. If you need gear, say so.
DIALOGUE_HAVENFORD_WATCH_DONE||NPC dialogue in talk_havenford_watch after all Havenford Watch jobs are complete|You have done more for Havenford than some men wearing my colors. The ruins are quieter, travelers are moving again, and my patrols can breathe. If you get north beyond the mountains, look for the sergeant at Camp Kestrel. That post always needs people who finish what they start.
DIALOGUE_HAVENFORD_WATCH_SKRIT_TURNIN||NPC dialogue in talk_havenford_watch when Skrit has been killed|Skrit is dead? Good. Without their packleader, the kobolds will scatter and bite smaller. Havenford owes you again.
DIALOGUE_HAVENFORD_WATCH_SKRIT_REMINDER||NPC dialogue in talk_havenford_watch while Havenford Watch III is active|Skrit still needs ending. The longer he breathes, the more kobolds gather.
DIALOGUE_HAVENFORD_WATCH_BONES_TURNIN||NPC dialogue in talk_havenford_watch when Havenford Watch II proof is ready|Good work. Grave bones are grim pay-tokens, but they prove the dead are staying down. We have traced the kobold trouble north of the ruined tower, toward the old mountain works. Their packleader, Skrit, is hiding there. Find him and end this properly.
DIALOGUE_HAVENFORD_WATCH_BONES_REMINDER||NPC dialogue in talk_havenford_watch while Havenford Watch II is active|Undead still foul the old ground. Bring grave bones when the work is done.
DIALOGUE_HAVENFORD_WATCH_SCALPS_TURNIN||NPC dialogue in talk_havenford_watch when Havenford Watch I proof is ready|Fine work. Every kobold scalp means one less knife at a wagon wheel. The land is changing, and not only with goblins. Undead are rising from old ground now. Break any you find, bring grave bones as proof, and I will see you paid again.
DIALOGUE_HAVENFORD_WATCH_SCALPS_TURNIN_FINAL||NPC dialogue when Havenford Watch I is turned in after the Smuggler route was selected|Fine work. Every kobold scalp means one less knife at a wagon wheel. Here is your pay.
DIALOGUE_HAVENFORD_WATCH_SHADY_COMPANY||Garrick's indirect response after the Smuggler route was selected|Consorting with thieves brings trouble, friend. Trouble tends to linger after the coin is spent.
DIALOGUE_HAVENFORD_WATCH_SCALPS_REMINDER||NPC dialogue in talk_havenford_watch while Havenford Watch I is active|Kobolds still worry the roads. Bring scalps when you have them.
DIALOGUE_HAVENFORD_WATCH_START||NPC dialogue in talk_havenford_watch when starting Havenford Watch I|Garrick, Silver Lancer and local guard captain. The roads are unsafe, my patrols are thin, and I will pay for useful steel wherever I find it. Kill kobolds in the area and bring their scalps as proof. It is ugly work, but ugly work keeps carts moving.
DIALOGUE_HAVENFORD_WATCH_START_HALF_ORC||Half-orc variant of DIALOGUE_HAVENFORD_WATCH_START|Garrick. I run the local guard. I do not care for surprises, and half-orcs bring plenty, but coin is coin and dead kobolds are dead kobolds. Bring scalps as proof and you will be paid.
DIALOGUE_KINGS_BARROW_DONE||NPC dialogue in talk_edran after Fit for a King II is complete|Keep Kingsmark. I have Theryn's reading, your barrow report, and enough ink to finish the account.
DIALOGUE_KINGS_BARROW_RING_TURNIN||NPC dialogue in talk_edran when Kingsmark has been claimed|Kingsmark came out of the royal sarcophagus, then. Theryn's phrase worked at the king's tomb, King Halric was named, and the tomb held the ring.\nKeep it. I came for the account, not a dead king's jewelry.
DIALOGUE_KINGS_BARROW_SARCOPHAGUS_REMINDER||NPC dialogue in talk_edran after King Halric is slain before Kingsmark is claimed|King Halric is down. Open the royal sarcophagus before you leave; Kingsmark should be in the king's hand.
DIALOGUE_KINGS_BARROW_EXPEDITION_REMINDER||NPC dialogue in talk_edran while Fit for a King II is active|Theryn gave you the phrase for the king's tomb. King's Barrow is south of Highmark in the old Havenford March. Bring Lightglass, defeat King Halric, and open the royal sarcophagus for Kingsmark.
DIALOGUE_KINGS_BARROW_PHRASE_CONFIRMED||NPC dialogue in talk_edran after Theryn confirms the barrow phrase|Theryn read it, then. Good. The phrase belongs to the king's tomb, but it will not clear the barrow for you.\nKing's Barrow is south of Highmark in the old Havenford March. Bring Lightglass, defeat King Halric, then open the royal sarcophagus and take Kingsmark. Bring the account back to me in Highmark after Kingsmark is out.
DIALOGUE_KINGS_BARROW_MANUSCRIPT_REPLACEMENT||NPC dialogue in talk_edran when replacing the barrow manuscript|The manuscript is gone from your pack. I keep a second rubbing because couriers lose bags. Take this copy to Old Theryn Rusk in Havenford.
DIALOGUE_KINGS_BARROW_MANUSCRIPT_REMINDER||NPC dialogue in talk_edran while the player carries the barrow manuscript|Take Edran's manuscript to Old Theryn Rusk in Havenford's south house. Do not try the King's Barrow phrase until Theryn has read the copy.
DIALOGUE_KINGS_BARROW_TOO_GREEN||NPC dialogue in talk_edran when the player is below the Fit for a King level gate|No commission from me today. The work I need is hard road work, not a first Highmark errand.
DIALOGUE_KINGS_BARROW_HALF_ORC_REFUSAL||NPC dialogue in talk_edran when refusing Fit for a King to half-orc player|No. King's Barrow is old March dead, and I will not be the pilgrim who sends orc blood to knock on Halric's door. Find other work in Highmark.
DIALOGUE_KINGS_BARROW_START||NPC dialogue in talk_edran when starting Fit for a King I|I am Edran Vale. Every shrine clerk in Highmark wants to know whether this phrase belongs to King Halric's tomb, so I need a courier with sense.\nI copied the words from an old King's Barrow account. The hand is old March script, and Old Theryn Rusk in Havenford knew that script before I was born.\nTake this manuscript to Theryn's south house and have him read the phrase. If he confirms it, bring the answer back to me in Highmark. I need the account; if Kingsmark is truly inside, I am not asking for the ring.
DIALOGUE_RETH_REEDMIRE_DONE||NPC dialogue in talk_reth after Reedmire is complete|Reedmire sleeps. The stones keep the altar quiet.
DIALOGUE_RETH_NHALOR_SLAIN||NPC dialogue in talk_reth after Nhalor is slain before Vethrin is paid|Nhalor is down. The altar keeps its stones.
DIALOGUE_RETH_REEDMIRE_REMINDER||NPC dialogue in talk_reth while the Reedmire shrine ritual remains unresolved|Reedmire Shrine is southeast off the road. Set one smooth stone on each corner stack. If Nhalor rises from the pool, kill it before you leave.
DIALOGUE_RETH_NOTE_HANDIN||NPC dialogue in talk_reth when handing in Vethrin's note|Vethrin's note. Fine. I took the stacked stones from the four shrine corners. Thought one of them might explain why the water moved. When I lifted the last one, the pool stood up like a man made of water. I ran, and I kept the stones.\pTake them. Reedmire Shrine is southeast off the road from here. Set one stone back on each stack. If the water rises again, kill Nhalor before you leave.
DIALOGUE_RETH_NO_QUEST_IDLE||NPC dialogue in talk_reth before Vethrin starts the Reedmire quest|These reeds are not your ground. Pass on.
DIALOGUE_RETH_QUIET_REEDMIRE||NPC dialogue in talk_reth at peaceful Reedmire|Nothing wrong with this water. Nothing wrong with this bottle either. Leave both where they are.
DIALOGUE_THAULD_CORPSE_REPORT||NPC dialogue in talk_thauld when reporting the dead fisherman in Floodgate Cistern|A dead fisher in the cistern? Damn waste. He will not need this now. Take it and make better use of it than the dark did.
DIALOGUE_THAULD_ARRIVAL_HANDOFF||NPC dialogue in talk_thauld after arriving at Reedwater Docks from the tutorial boat crossing|Rough crossing, but the hull held. Garran sent word ahead, so I know enough not to ask foolish questions. If you are bound inland, take the north road to Havenford and do not wander from it. The land is waking mean, and old stories are starting to cost lives. Rest here, buy what you lack, then move.
DIALOGUE_THAULD_DOCK_REMINDER||NPC dialogue in talk_thauld after the opening handoff is complete|North road for Havenford. When the water behaves, this boat can carry folk again.
DIALOGUE_STORMWRECK_THAULD_DEPARTURE||NPC dialogue in talk_stormwreck_thauld at the far cove|There you are. The hull is patched enough to cross the last stretch, and the water is quieter on this side. Get aboard. Reedwater is close.
DIALOGUE_RAT_CELLAR_DONE||NPC dialogue in talk_bress after the Rat Cellar quest is complete|Cellar is mine again, and the sacks may stay sacks instead of rat beds.
DIALOGUE_RAT_CELLAR_TURNIN||NPC dialogue in talk_bress when the giant rat is slain|Big one is dead? Good. That breaks the nest. Take the pay; I'll have to spend what's left over on new grain.
DIALOGUE_RAT_CELLAR_REMINDER||NPC dialogue in talk_bress while the Rat Cellar quest is active|The big rat still owns my cellar. I would like it evicted, with a blade.
DIALOGUE_RAT_CELLAR_START||NPC dialogue in talk_bress when starting the Rat Cellar quest|Rats took the cellar, and one brute down there has the rest acting bold. Kill the big one and I will pay.
DIALOGUE_MIRA_DOCKSIDE_STOCK||NPC dialogue in talk_mira for dockside stock|Oil, food, a knife that will cut more than string. Dock stock is plain, but plain keeps travelers breathing.
DIALOGUE_MARN_BUNK_AVAILABLE||NPC dialogue in talk_marn when bunk rental is available|Bunks upstairs, dry enough and watched enough. Pay the rate and rest.
DIALOGUE_MARN_HALF_ORC||Half-orc variant of DIALOGUE_MARN_BUNK_AVAILABLE|Coin buys a bunk. Keep your hands quiet and nobody has trouble.
DIALOGUE_VOSK_ROUTE_CLOSED||NPC dialogue in talk_vosk before Tidehook skiff route is open|South channel is closed. I like breathing more than rowing blind.
DIALOGUE_VOSK_WAITING_MARK||NPC dialogue in talk_vosk before Tidehook route opens, second page|Still waiting on the harbor mark. Until it comes, the skiff stays tied.
DIALOGUE_VOSK_TIDEHOOK_ROUTE_OPEN||NPC dialogue in talk_vosk after Tidehook skiff route is open|South channel is open. Pay the fare and I will run you to Tidehook.
DIALOGUE_VEYSHA_SKIFF_READY||NPC dialogue in talk_veysha after Tidehook skiff arrival|Tide marks are set. Pay the hand and the skiff runs north.
DIALOGUE_VEYSHA_CHANNEL_WARNING||NPC dialogue in talk_veysha channel warning, second page|Step back from the edge. That channel keeps what it takes.
DIALOGUE_QUADE_REEDWATER_ROUTE_OPEN||NPC dialogue in talk_quade for Reedwater skiff route|North water is clear enough. Fare first, then Reedwater.
DIALOGUE_KETHRA_RACK_OPEN||NPC dialogue in talk_kethra for spear rack shop|Spears on the rack. Fish, boar, or bandit, the point does not care.
DIALOGUE_NESKA_TAVERN_FOOD||NPC dialogue in talk_neska for tavern food shop|Beer from the cask, stew from the pot, coin on the counter. No singing unless you pay double.
DIALOGUE_BRAN_DELIVERY_DONE||NPC dialogue in talk_bran after the parcel delivery is complete|Orrick has it? Good. One less thing for the tide to steal from me.
DIALOGUE_BRAN_PARCEL_REMINDER||NPC dialogue in talk_bran while carrying Bran's parcel|That parcel is for Orrick at Traveller's Rest, far northeast along the inland road. Keep it dry.
DIALOGUE_BRAN_PARCEL_REPLACEMENT||NPC dialogue in talk_bran when replacing Bran's parcel|Lost it? Hah. Take this one, then. Orrick waits, and he counts late as lost.
DIALOGUE_BRAN_BEER_REMINDER||NPC dialogue in talk_bran while waiting for beer|Still dry here. The tavern is close enough I can smell the cask.
DIALOGUE_BRAN_BEER_START||NPC dialogue in talk_bran when starting the beer fetch quest|My cup is empty and both hands are full of torn net. Bring one beer over and I will remember your face kindly.
DIALOGUE_BRAN_BEER_HANDIN_PARCEL||NPC dialogue in talk_bran when beer is delivered and the parcel quest starts|That sits right. Now earn the better errand: parcel for Orrick at Traveller's Rest, far northeast along the inland road. Keep it dry if you can manage it.
DIALOGUE_NELL_ROOM_AVAILABLE||NPC dialogue in talk_nell when room rental is available|Beds by the hearth, warm if the fire behaves. Pay the rate and rest.
DIALOGUE_LYSS_ROOM_AVAILABLE||NPC dialogue in talk_lyss when room rental is available|Private rooms by night. Pay up front and rest quiet.
DIALOGUE_STONECLEFT_INNKEEPER_BED_AVAILABLE||NPC dialogue in talk_stonecleft_innkeeper when bed rental is available|Hall beds. Pay the alewife and rest under stone.
DIALOGUE_NELL_HALF_ORC||Half-orc variant of DIALOGUE_NELL_ROOM_AVAILABLE|Coin buys the bed. Rest, keep the peace, and let folk get used to you from across the room.
DIALOGUE_LYSS_HALF_ORC||Half-orc variant of DIALOGUE_LYSS_ROOM_AVAILABLE|Room for coin. Pay the house and keep quiet.
DIALOGUE_STONECLEFT_INNKEEPER_HALF_ORC||Half-orc variant of DIALOGUE_STONECLEFT_INNKEEPER_BED_AVAILABLE|Bed for coin. Pay and rest. Hall keeps its own.
DIALOGUE_STONECLEFT_GATEHALL_LAMP_DONE||NPC dialogue in talk_stonecleft_supplier at the gatehall after Lamp Run is complete|Lamp run is closed. The deep lamps are stocked for another shift; gatehall supplies are open.
DIALOGUE_STONECLEFT_GATEHALL_LAMP_TURNIN||NPC dialogue in talk_stonecleft_supplier at the gatehall when handing in Lamp Run supplies|Set the oil and rations here. Harl counts them into the gatehall shelves and pays you now.
DIALOGUE_STONECLEFT_GATEHALL_LAMP_MISSING||NPC dialogue in talk_stonecleft_supplier at the gatehall when Lamp Run supplies are incomplete|The gatehall shelves are still short. Harl needs ten rations and ten oil flasks before he can sign off the run.
DIALOGUE_STONECLEFT_GATEHALL_LAMP_COUNT||NPC dialogue progress line in talk_stonecleft_supplier, {0}=ration count, {1}=oil flask count|Right now you carry {0} rations and {1} oil flasks.
DIALOGUE_STONECLEFT_GATEHALL_SHOP||NPC dialogue in talk_stonecleft_supplier at the gatehall with no active Lamp Run|Gatehall supplies: oil, rations, rope, and road kit.
DIALOGUE_STONECLEFT_SUPPLY_LAMP_DONE||NPC dialogue in talk_stonecleft_supplier at the lower supply hall after Lamp Run is complete|Harl signed off on the lamp run. The gatehall has food and oil again, and my count is clean.
DIALOGUE_STONECLEFT_SUPPLY_LAMP_REMINDER||NPC dialogue in talk_stonecleft_supplier at the lower supply hall while Lamp Run is active|Lamp run is still yours. Harl Brack at the gatehall needs ten rations and ten oil flasks; buy what you are short before you report in.
DIALOGUE_STONECLEFT_SUPPLY_LAMP_START||NPC dialogue in talk_stonecleft_supplier at the lower supply hall when starting Lamp Run|Paid lamp run, if you want it. Gatehall's lower posts are short: ten rations and ten oil flasks to Harl Brack upstairs. Bring them yourself, and he pays when they reach his shelves.
DIALOGUE_STONECLEFT_SUPPLY_SHOP||NPC dialogue in talk_stonecleft_supplier at the lower supply hall with no active Lamp Run|Supply hall stock: rations, oil, rope, and spare road gear.
DIALOGUE_BRANNA_BED_AVAILABLE||NPC dialogue in talk_branna when bed rental is available|Beds for the road, stew if the pot lasts, quiet if the guests behave. Pay the rate and rest.
DIALOGUE_BRANNA_HALF_ORC||Half-orc variant of DIALOGUE_BRANNA_BED_AVAILABLE|Coin buys a bed. Keep your temper tied and the yard keeps its peace.
DIALOGUE_ORRICK_PARCEL_TURNIN||Shopkeeper Orrick parcel delivery hand-in|Bran's parcel, finally. Good. I can close that tally before the ink dries twice.
DIALOGUE_ORRICK_OLD_CAVE_DONE||Shopkeeper Orrick post-Old Cave chatter|Still nothing special down there, then. Good. Sometimes an old cave earns the name honestly.
DIALOGUE_ORRICK_MIXED_GOODS||Shopkeeper Orrick mixed goods shop description|Oil, food, straps, cheap steel. Mixed goods for travelers who forgot something important.
DIALOGUE_ORRICK_OLD_CAVE_TURNIN||Shopkeeper Orrick Old Cave turn-in|So there really was nothing special down there. Hah. Just an old cave with old trouble in it. That is useful news, and useful news gets paid.
DIALOGUE_ORRICK_OLD_CAVE_REMINDER||Shopkeeper Orrick Old Cave reminder|The old cave still wants checking. Reach the lower halls, then come back before I send someone worse.
DIALOGUE_ORRICK_TOO_GREEN||Shopkeeper Orrick Old Cave level gate|Not that errand today. Buy food, oil, and rope if you need them; smaller work is wiser for now.
DIALOGUE_ORRICK_OLD_CAVE_START||Shopkeeper Orrick Old Cave first offer|The old cave nearby has been taking rumors and returning none. Reach the lower halls, see what waits there, and I will pay for the answer.
DIALOGUE_ORRICK_OLD_CAVE_SPIDER_START||Shopkeeper Orrick Spider Nest first offer|Travelers near the old cave have been finding web in their packs and bite marks on their mules. Find the spider nesting below and kill it. I will pay for a safer road.
DIALOGUE_ORRICK_OLD_CAVE_SPIDER_REMINDER||Shopkeeper Orrick Spider Nest reminder|The old cave still has a spider problem. Find the thing nesting below and kill it before it starts hunting outside.
DIALOGUE_ORRICK_OLD_CAVE_SPIDER_TURNIN||Shopkeeper Orrick Spider Nest turn-in|Needlelegs, was it? Nasty name for a nasty thing. With that spider dead, travelers can use the road without watching every shadow. Here is your pay.
DIALOGUE_ORRICK_OLD_CAVE_SPIDER_DONE||Shopkeeper Orrick post-Spider Nest chatter|No fresh webs near the road since you killed Needlelegs. I will take that kind of quiet any day.
DIALOGUE_CALDUS_DOCKS_DONE||Ser Caldus post-Desolate Docks chatter|The Desolate Docks are quiet. A hard post stays quiet only while someone remembers what it cost.
DIALOGUE_CALDUS_DOCKS_DONE_HALF_ORC||Ser Caldus half-orc post-Desolate Docks chatter|The Desolate Docks are quiet. Let others count bloodlines; I count finished work.
DIALOGUE_CALDUS_DOCKS_TURNIN||Ser Caldus Desolate Docks turn-in after quest start|Krosh is dead? Then the docks have lost their captain, and the river road can breathe again.
DIALOGUE_CALDUS_DOCKS_TURNIN_HALF_ORC||Ser Caldus half-orc Desolate Docks turn-in after quest start|Krosh is dead by your hand. That is the report that matters.
DIALOGUE_CALDUS_DOCKS_PAY||Ser Caldus Desolate Docks reward line|Take the pay. Traveller's Rest owes for work that keeps the road open.
DIALOGUE_CALDUS_DOCKS_PAY_HALF_ORC||Ser Caldus half-orc Desolate Docks reward line|Take the pay. You did the work, and the road is safer for it.
DIALOGUE_CALDUS_DOCKS_REMINDER||Ser Caldus Desolate Docks reminder|Krosh still holds the Desolate Docks. Remove him, and the rest should break.
DIALOGUE_CALDUS_DOCKS_REMINDER_HALF_ORC||Ser Caldus half-orc Desolate Docks reminder|Krosh still holds the docks. Remove him, and the rest should break.
DIALOGUE_CALDUS_DOCKS_TOO_GREEN||Ser Caldus pre-offer level gate|Dangerous times around Traveller's Rest. Keep your blade close and your questions closer.
DIALOGUE_CALDUS_DOCKS_TOO_GREEN_HALF_ORC||Ser Caldus half-orc pre-offer level gate|Dangerous times around Traveller's Rest. Keep your blade close; the road respects caution more than blood.
DIALOGUE_CALDUS_DOCKS_START||Ser Caldus Desolate Docks first offer|Orcs have taken the Desolate Docks, and Krosh is holding them together. Kill him, clear the place, and return for your pay.
DIALOGUE_CALDUS_DOCKS_START_HALF_ORC||Ser Caldus half-orc Desolate Docks first offer|Orcs have taken the Desolate Docks, and Krosh is holding them together. Kill him, clear the place, and return for your pay.
DIALOGUE_CALDUS_ORC_FORTRESS_REMINDER||Ser Caldus points from the cleared docks toward the Orc Fortress|Krosh carried orders from a fortress west of Stonecleft. The docks were only its river hand. Find the place and break whoever commands it.
DIALOGUE_CALDUS_ORC_FORTRESS_FIND_BORRI||Ser Caldus reminds the player to free Borri after Gorvuk dies|Gorvuk is dead, but a Stonecleft dwarf was still held below. I would not call the fortress finished while he remains there.
DIALOGUE_CALDUS_ORC_FORTRESS_REPORT||Ser Caldus receives the Orc Fortress report and reveals the War Camp route|That explains the tracks turning north. The survivors are gathering in open country. Take this, and keep after them before the camp settles in.
DIALOGUE_CALDUS_ORC_WAR_CAMP_REMINDER||Ser Caldus reminds the player about the Orc War Camp|The war camp lies farther north, out in the open country. Break its chief before the scattered bands gather there.
DIALOGUE_CALDUS_ORC_WAR_CAMP_TURNIN||Ser Caldus receives the final Orc War Camp report|Their camp is broken? Good. Without a place to gather, the survivors are only fugitives. You have earned the rest of the road pay.
DIALOGUE_CALDUS_ORC_CAMPAIGN_DONE||Ser Caldus after the Orc War Camp campaign|The north road has been quiet since the camp fell. That is as close to peace as this country gives us.
DIALOGUE_CALDUS_ORC_BORRI_ROUTE_ACK||Ser Caldus acknowledges that the player followed the Stonecleft lead|Word already came down from Stonecleft. Sounds like you have the trail.
DIALOGUE_VELRA_ASH_DONE||Peddler Velra post-Ash Tower chatter|Rhazvek is ash, the tower is quieter, and my buyers are suddenly less brave about asking where the ring came from.
DIALOGUE_VELRA_ARCANE_CASE||Peddler Velra arcane case shop description|Sealed scrolls, capped wands, warded boxes. Do not open what you cannot pay for.
DIALOGUE_NYMIRA_SHOP||Tower wizard Nymira offers her observatory stock|Rhazvek never crossed the warding circle. You did. Have a look at what I keep above the ash.
DIALOGUE_INFINITE_DUNGEON_NIXEL||Nixel offers a room and inn supplies|Time does not pass here in the polite way, but sleep remains fond of beds. Mine are clean.
DIALOGUE_INFINITE_DUNGEON_PIVEN||Piven offers provisions and tools|Rope, lamps, little certainties. Take enough. The stairs dislike certainty, which is why I keep selling it.
DIALOGUE_INFINITE_DUNGEON_QUINEL||Quinel offers magic goods and services|This wand has already been used tomorrow. It seems perfectly well today. I also examine things and lift curses.
DIALOGUE_INFINITE_DUNGEON_TOVIK||Tovik offers martial goods and services|Steel remembers every blow. Mine has been persuaded to remember only the useful ones. I can examine or mend yours.
DIALOGUE_CADAN_APPRENTICE_SHOP||NPC dialogue in talk_cadan_apprentice offering low-level spellbooks|I am still copying the first circles cleanly. The spare books are for sale, if you do not mind an apprentice's hand.
DIALOGUE_VELRA_ASH_TURNIN||Peddler Velra Ash Tower turn-in with scale|Rhazvek's scale. Hot work, clean enough. The Ashen Ring is yours.
DIALOGUE_VELRA_ASH_REMINDER||Peddler Velra Ash Tower reminder|The Ash Tower still has Rhazvek, and Rhazvek still has the scale. Bring it if you want the ring.
DIALOGUE_VELRA_ASH_TOO_GREEN||Peddler Velra Ash Tower level gate|Not that commission. Not yet. Buy a small scroll and keep to smaller trouble for now.
DIALOGUE_VELRA_ASH_START||Peddler Velra Ash Tower first offer|Rhazvek, a young red drake, has made the Ash Tower his perch. Bring me one scale from him and I will trade you the Ashen Ring.
DIALOGUE_DORRAN_CORE_HANDIN||Runeforge core hand-in|That is the core. Wet, scored, and whole enough. I can seat it again. The runeforge is lit enough for blackglass.
DIALOGUE_DORRAN_DUERGAR_DONE_REWARD||Armorer Dorran Deadrock Mineworks reward line|Good. Stonecleft can stop waiting for the next theft. Take the pay. I have better gear on the racks now if you need it.
DIALOGUE_DORRAN_OLD_MINEWORKS_START||Armorer Dorran Deadrock Mineworks quest start after core hand-in|Throkk says duergar stole the core. Their captain, Vargrom, holds Deadrock Mineworks in the hills far southeast of Traveller's Rest. Kill him, and I will pay you. If you need gear first, the magic armory is open.
DIALOGUE_DORRAN_VARGROM_TURNIN||Armorer Dorran Vargrom turn-in|Vargrom is dead? Good. That is one less thief with Stonecleft in reach.
DIALOGUE_DORRAN_REPAIRED_STOCK||Armorer Dorran magic armory stock access|The magic armory is open. Buy what keeps you alive.
DIALOGUE_DORRAN_REPAIRED_VARGROM_REMINDER||Armorer Dorran Vargrom reminder while shop is open|Vargrom still holds Deadrock Mineworks in the hills far southeast of Traveller's Rest. Kill him if you want the pay. The magic armory is open if you need gear first.
DIALOGUE_DORRAN_REPAIR_WAITING||legacy Master Smith Throkk repair reminder while runeforge is active|The core is seated. I want a day or two of steady heat before I brag about it, but the runeforge is lit enough for blackglass.
DIALOGUE_DORRAN_REPAIR_HOURS_COME_BACK||legacy repair wait line with time phrase, {0}=time phrase|Give it {0}, then come back.
DIALOGUE_DORRAN_CORE_LOCATION_FOUND||Runeforge core location reminder|Dead duergar in the lower cistern? Then look there for the core. Bring it back before the water buries it.
DIALOGUE_DORRAN_VALVE_REMINDER||Floodgate valve reminder|Floodgate Cistern is still our best clue. Use the runed handle on the lower sluice and find out what happened down there.
DIALOGUE_DORRAN_RUNEFORGE_START||Armorer Dorran first runeforge quest offer|Something went wrong below Floodgate Cistern when the runeforge failed. That is our best clue. Take this runed valve handle; the lower sluice has no handle of its own. Get down there and find out what happened.
DIALOGUE_DORRAN_ARMORY_CLOSED||Armorer Dorran armory closed idle|Throkk handles forge trouble. The magic armory is closed until that is settled.
DIALOGUE_STONECLEFT_SURFACE_GUARD_STAIR_OPENED||Stonecleft surface guard dialogue when the upper stair door is opened by this talk|We got word you need to go through to Highmark. We'll open the gates, but make straight for Stonecleft.
DIALOGUE_STONECLEFT_SURFACE_GUARD_STAIR_ALREADY_OPEN||Stonecleft surface guard dialogue when the upper stair door is already open|Gate's still open. What else do you need?
DIALOGUE_STONECLEFT_SURFACE_GUARD_STAIR_UNAUTHORIZED||Stonecleft surface guard dialogue when the player is not authorized for the upper stair|Gate stays shut until we get word from Cael at Traveller's Rest.
DIALOGUE_STONECLEFT_SURFACE_GUARD_TURN_BACK||Stonecleft surface guard turn-back page when the player is not authorized for the upper stair|If you need Highmark, speak with him first. Otherwise stay on this side.
DIALOGUE_STONECLEFT_DEEP_GUARD_DWARF_UNAUTHORIZED||Stonecleft deep guard dwarf-player refusal before lower pass authorization|Lower gate is sealed. Clan blood does not move it; Thrunna does.
DIALOGUE_STONECLEFT_DEEP_GUARD_DWARF_WAIT_WARDENS||Stonecleft deep guard dwarf-player wait-for-wardens page before lower pass authorization|Wait for Throkk or the wardens to clear the pass.
DIALOGUE_STONECLEFT_DEEP_GUARD_OUTSIDER_UNAUTHORIZED||Stonecleft deep guard non-dwarf refusal before lower pass authorization|Lower gate is sealed. Stonecleft has not opened the pass to guests.
DIALOGUE_STONECLEFT_DEEP_GUARD_OUTSIDER_WAIT_WARDENS||Stonecleft deep guard non-dwarf wait-for-wardens page before lower pass authorization|Wait for Throkk or the wardens to clear the pass.
DIALOGUE_STONECLEFT_DEEP_GUARD_DWARF_GATE_OPENED||Stonecleft deep guard dwarf-player dialogue when lower gate is opened by this talk|North gate is opening, cousin. Keep north through the Underway and keep your lamp trimmed.
DIALOGUE_STONECLEFT_DEEP_GUARD_OUTSIDER_GATE_OPENED||Stonecleft deep guard non-dwarf dialogue when lower gate is opened by this talk|North gate is opening, traveler. Keep north through the Underway and stay out of the work cuts.
DIALOGUE_STONECLEFT_DEEP_GUARD_GATE_ALREADY_OPEN||Stonecleft deep guard dialogue when lower gate is already open|Lower gate is clear. The Underway runs north.
DIALOGUE_STONECLEFT_DEEP_GUARD_POST_OPEN||Stonecleft deep guard fallback dialogue after lower post is open|Deep post is open. Mind the lamps below.
DIALOGUE_NAERYS_GUEST_MAT_AVAILABLE||NPC dialogue in talk_naerys when guest mat rental is available|Guest mats wait. Pay the warden and rest within the veil.
DIALOGUE_NAERYS_HALF_ORC||Half-orc variant of DIALOGUE_NAERYS_GUEST_MAT_AVAILABLE|Bed for coin. Pay and rest. The veil keeps its own.
DIALOGUE_SARN_MARKET_STALL||NPC dialogue in talk_sarn for market stall shop|Road kit, dry straps, cart cloth, and no temple prices. Tell me what broke before you ask what is cheap.
DIALOGUE_BRETHRA_PROVISION_STALL||NPC dialogue in talk_brethra for provision stall shop|Oil is sealed, rope is measured, kits are packed for travel. Buy what you can carry and do not unstack my coils.
DIALOGUE_MAVETH_APOTHECARY_OLDROOT_DONE||Apothecary Maveth post-Bitter Stock shop chatter|The Oldroot batch held. Stronger healing and resistance bottles are on the shelf. Point before you unstopper anything green.
DIALOGUE_MAVETH_APOTHECARY_BITTER_DONE||Apothecary Maveth post-Bitter Stock shop chatter|The new batch held. Stronger healing and resistance bottles are on the shelf. Point before you unstopper anything green.
DIALOGUE_MAVETH_APOTHECARY_OLDROOT_TURNIN||Apothecary Maveth Bitter Stock turn-in|Six leaves, whole and dark. Good. The bitter edge is still there.\nTake this pay and a restoration potion. Once I grind the rest, stronger bottles go on the shelf.
DIALOGUE_MAVETH_APOTHECARY_WIDOWRUN_TURNIN||Apothecary Maveth venom-gland turn-in|Six glands, tied clean and still wet. Good. There is enough venom left to cut into medicine.\nTake this pay and a restoration potion. Once I finish the batch, stronger bottles go on the shelf.
DIALOGUE_MAVETH_APOTHECARY_OLDROOT_REMINDER||Apothecary Maveth Bitter Stock reminder|Oldroot Temple. Six usable leaves. Cut dark leaves from living oldroot; loose floor growth is trash.
DIALOGUE_MAVETH_APOTHECARY_WIDOWRUN_REMINDER||Apothecary Maveth Widowrun reminder|Widowrun Cave. Six intact venom glands. Bring them wrapped; a leaking gland is no use to me.
DIALOGUE_MAVETH_APOTHECARY_BITTER_REMINDER||Apothecary Maveth Bitter Stock reminder before either ingredient is complete|I can work with six dark oldroot leaves from Oldroot Temple, or six intact venom glands from Widowrun Cave.
DIALOGUE_MAVETH_APOTHECARY_OLDROOT_COUNT||Apothecary Maveth Bitter Stock progress line, {0}=oldroot leaf count|You have {0} usable leaves. I need six before I waste clean mortar on the batch.
DIALOGUE_MAVETH_APOTHECARY_WIDOWRUN_COUNT||Apothecary Maveth Widowrun progress line, {0}=venom gland count|You have {0} intact glands. I need six before I waste clean glass on the batch.
DIALOGUE_MAVETH_APOTHECARY_BITTER_COUNT||Apothecary Maveth Bitter Stock progress line, {0}=leaf count, {1}=gland count|You have {0} usable leaves and {1} intact glands. Six of either will make the batch.
DIALOGUE_MAVETH_APOTHECARY_OLDROOT_START||Apothecary Maveth Bitter Stock first offer|Careful. Those bottles are sealed tight. Highmark caravans bought through my strong stock, and my Oldroot gatherer came back fevered.\nI need six whole oldroot leaves from Oldroot Temple. Cut dark leaves from living oldroot, not floor growth. Bring them back for coin and a restoration potion.
DIALOGUE_MAVETH_APOTHECARY_BITTER_START||Apothecary Maveth Bitter Stock first offer|Careful. Those bottles are sealed tight. Highmark caravans bought through my strong stock.\nI can rebuild it with six dark leaves from Oldroot Temple, or six intact venom glands from Widowrun Cave. Bring either set for coin and a restoration potion.
DIALOGUE_MAVETH_APOTHECARY_CASE||Apothecary Maveth apothecary case shop bark|Sealed draughts, dated salves, clean corks. The glowing bottles stay behind the counter. Say what hurts or browse like you mean to buy.
DIALOGUE_JAETH_BOWYER_RACK||NPC dialogue in talk_jaeth for bowyer rack shop|Bows on the left, bolts below, good string in the oiled wrap. Touch the grain, not the points.
DIALOGUE_NERRIK_DRAUGHT_DONE||Researcher Nerrik post-Perfect Draught chatter|The perfect draught is finished. If you have blackglass fragments, the worktable can make more elixirs. Do not touch the brown bottle.
DIALOGUE_NERRIK_TABLE_WARNING||Researcher Nerrik low-level table warning|No. The table work is deep-cut alchemy, not a lesson for green hands. Come back when one mistake will not kill you.
DIALOGUE_NERRIK_DRAUGHT_START||Researcher Nerrik Perfect Draught first offer|You. Good, careful hands. I am working toward a perfect draught, but I need preserved monster samples first.\nTake these jars of preservation ointment. Use one on a fresh corpse, or throw one at the creature before you kill it.\nBring me the samples and I can make them into elixirs. With these samples I can slowly perfect the recipe.
DIALOGUE_NERRIK_DRAUGHT_SAMPLE||Researcher Nerrik Perfect Draught sample hand-in, placeholder 0 monster type|A preserved {0} corpse. Good. Still tight, still useful. I can cut a clean sample from this.
DIALOGUE_NERRIK_DRAUGHT_BATCH||Researcher Nerrik Perfect Draught step reward, placeholder 0 attribute name|This sample settles the {0} mixture. Take the elixir; I only need a shaving for the next draft.
DIALOGUE_NERRIK_DRAUGHT_FINAL||Researcher Nerrik Perfect Draught final turn-in|Good. The perfect draught holds together. Drink it here while the blackglass is still quiet.
DIALOGUE_NERRIK_DRAUGHT_NEED_OINTMENT||Researcher Nerrik Perfect Draught reminder without ointment|You need preservation ointment before hunting the next sample. Maveth sometimes sells jars, and curio shelves may have them.
DIALOGUE_NERRIK_DRAUGHT_USE_OINTMENT||Researcher Nerrik Perfect Draught preservation reminder|Use the ointment before rot starts. Rub it into the fresh corpse I named, or throw the jar at that creature before the kill.
DIALOGUE_NERRIK_DRAUGHT_TARGET||Researcher Nerrik Perfect Draught target line, placeholder 0 monster type|Next sample: preserve a {0} corpse and bring it back to me.
DIALOGUE_NERRIK_DRAUGHT_FINAL_TARGET||Researcher Nerrik Perfect Draught final target line|For the last draught, bring me a preserved adult dragon corpse and one blackglass shard. Young dragons will not do.
DIALOGUE_NERRIK_DRAUGHT_FINAL_SAMPLE||Researcher Nerrik Perfect Draught final sample hand-in|An adult dragon sample and a blackglass shard. Good. That is enough body and enough bite for the final mix.
DIALOGUE_NERRIK_DRAUGHT_FINAL_NEED_SHARD||Researcher Nerrik Perfect Draught final sample missing shard line|The dragon sample is usable. Now bring one blackglass shard; the final draught needs something hard enough to hold the change.
DIALOGUE_NERRIK_DRAUGHT_FINAL_NEED_SAMPLE||Researcher Nerrik Perfect Draught final sample reminder|The last sample must come from an adult dragon or older. Preserve the corpse and bring it here with one blackglass shard.
DIALOGUE_AELRION_THREAD_DONE||Bowyer Aelrion post-Moonwell Thread shop chatter|Second String is out of my hands, and the better rack is stocked. Keep finished bows dry, or buy another string.
DIALOGUE_AELRION_THREAD_TURNIN||Bowyer Aelrion Moonwell Thread turn-in|Six strands, none frayed. Good. These will hold.\nTake this pay, and take Second String. I will twist the rest into the better rack.
DIALOGUE_AELRION_THREAD_REMINDER||Bowyer Aelrion Moonwell Thread reminder|Did you find the threads yet? Moonwell Observatory catches them near the old frame, and cult dead or specter rooms sometimes carry strands away.
DIALOGUE_AELRION_THREAD_COUNT||Bowyer Aelrion Moonwell Thread progress line, {0}=moonwell thread count|You have found {0}. Six strands will make the bow worth stringing.
DIALOGUE_AELRION_THREAD_START||Bowyer Aelrion Moonwell Thread first offer|Looking at the good rack? Then I will tell you why it is not good enough. My best strings are plain gut, and damp weather wins too many arguments.\nMoonwell thread holds a bow under wet, cold, and bad handling. Bring me six strands from Moonwell Observatory; cult dead, specter rooms, and the old frame can hold them. I will pay coin and make you a bow worth remembering.
DIALOGUE_AELRION_BOWYER_RACK||Bowyer Aelrion bowyer rack shop bark|Dry yew, waxed strings, counted arrowheads. Keep wet gloves off the finished bows.
DIALOGUE_LANCER_ORDERS_DONE||Highmark lancer post-Orders for Kestrel chatter|Vaust heard the message? Good. Kestrel can post scouts with current routes instead of last week's guesswork.
DIALOGUE_LANCER_ORDERS_REMINDER||Highmark lancer Orders for Kestrel reminder|Captain Vaust Thane at Camp Kestrel needs the Highmark message. Put it in his hand, not on a camp table.
DIALOGUE_LANCER_ORDERS_START||Highmark lancer Orders for Kestrel first offer|You there, traveler. Highmark has no runner to spare, and Camp Kestrel needs to know which west roads are open.\nIf you are heading to Camp Kestrel, carry that message to Captain Vaust Thane. He pays when it reaches his hand.
DIALOGUE_LANCER_HARPIES_TURNIN||Highmark lancer Northern Watch I turn-in|Twelve harpies confirmed. North road scouts can watch tracks again instead of the sky. I have your pay; next board is ogres.
DIALOGUE_LANCER_OGRES_TURNIN||Highmark lancer Northern Watch II turn-in|Eight ogres confirmed. Hill carts can move without a double guard. I have your pay; next board is hill giants.
DIALOGUE_LANCER_GIANTS_TURNIN||Highmark lancer Northern Watch III turn-in|Two hill giants confirmed. Highmark can send banners and supply carts back onto the hill roads. Take your pay; the armory added an armor piece.
DIALOGUE_LANCER_NORTHERN_REMINDER||Highmark lancer active Northern Watch bounty reminder|Northern ground still needs clearing. Keep the count clean and the claims cleaner.
DIALOGUE_LANCER_NORTHERN_START||Highmark lancer Northern Watch first offer|Greycliff Quarry is west of Highmark, and harpies are dragging scouts off the quarry road and the cliff routes toward Telwynd. Clear the harpies, then report back. I pay in coin.
DIALOGUE_LANCER_HARPY_COUNT||Highmark lancer active Northern Watch I reminder|Clear the harpies around Greycliff Quarry west of Highmark, then report back when the quarry road is safe enough for scouts.
DIALOGUE_LANCER_OGRE_COUNT||Highmark lancer ogre progress count, placeholder 0 ogre kill count|Ogre count stands at {0}. Eight clears the second board.
DIALOGUE_LANCER_GIANT_COUNT||Highmark lancer hill giant progress count, placeholder 0 hill giant kill count|Hill giant count stands at {0}. Two ends the watch contract.
DIALOGUE_OSKARN_CURIO_CASE||NPC dialogue in talk_oskarn for curio case shop|Curio case. Stones, tokens, and repair kits for the road.
DIALOGUE_BRANN_GOODS_OPEN||NPC dialogue in talk_brann for iron goods shop|Iron goods from clan hands: bars, tools, shields, and no patience for haggling theater.
DIALOGUE_BRANN_LOWER_PASS_CLOSED||NPC dialogue in talk_brann when lower pass is still closed|Lower pass stays shut. Iron waits until the road stops eating caravans.
DIALOGUE_DARRON_LANCE_ARMORY||NPC dialogue in talk_darron for Lance armory shop|Mail on the upper hooks is Lance pattern. Traveler steel is below. I sell sound work, not parade shine.
DIALOGUE_YRVETH_WHITE_SEAL_RELIQUARY||NPC dialogue in talk_yrveth for White Seal reliquary shop|Blessed oils, wrapped ward-steel, and relic tools by catalogue number. Handle the seals with respect or let me handle them for you.
DIALOGUE_QUESSA_SCRIPTORIUM||NPC dialogue in talk_quessa for Seal Scriptorium shop|Copied notes, old leaves, and spellbooks kept dry for once. Browse with clean hands and a quieter voice.
DIALOGUE_THERYN_HIGHWIND_CATACOMBS_FOUND||Theryn Rusk Highwind catacombs already found|You found the Highwind Catacombs before I finished the map. Good. The answer was under the monastery after all.
DIALOGUE_THERYN_HIGHWIND_CATACOMBS_LEAD||Theryn Rusk Highwind catacombs lead|Highwind Monastery is only the upper site. The old burial halls sit under it.\nSearch the monastery for the catacomb entrance and step inside. Then return to Telwynd with proof the lower way is real.
DIALOGUE_THERYN_BARROW_PHRASE||Theryn Rusk barrow manuscript hand-in phrase|Give me the page. Hm. Old March hand, royal names, and a burial line about Halric's road.\nKing Halric and Kingsmark share the line. At the royal sarcophagus, say: Halric holds the road.
DIALOGUE_THERYN_BARROW_PHRASE_REMINDER||Theryn Rusk barrow phrase reminder|You have the phrase. At the royal sarcophagus, say: Halric holds the road.
DIALOGUE_THERYN_OPENING_WORDS_LEARNED||legacy Theryn Rusk final blood seal aid learned|The final blood seal needs Istarian work, not a spoken guess. Return with Lightglass and the right manuscript before you trust that stone.
DIALOGUE_THERYN_OPENING_WORDS_REMINDER||legacy Theryn Rusk final blood seal aid reminder|Return to the final blood seal with Lightglass and the Istarian manuscript.
DIALOGUE_THERYN_MANUSCRIPT_LEAD||Theryn Rusk final blood seal manuscript lead|Old Istarian under blackglass, and Tharec was right to send you here.\nThere may be one book that helps: an Ancient Istarian Manuscript buried with King Halric in King's Barrow. Go to King's Barrow and see if you can find it.
DIALOGUE_THERYN_MANUSCRIPT_REMINDER||Theryn Rusk final blood seal manuscript reminder|King's Barrow is the place. Look among Halric's old hoard for the Ancient Istarian Manuscript.
DIALOGUE_THERYN_MANUSCRIPT_READIED||Theryn Rusk final blood seal manuscript readied|Yes. This is old Istarian work, older than the Marches by a long road.\nTake the manuscript to the final blood seal. Mark the page with your blood and read the Istarian aloud. If the seal remembers your line, the door should open.
DIALOGUE_TRAVELLERS_REST_SCHOLAR_WATCHTOWER_COMPLETE||Traveller's Rest scholar Watchtower Prism completion page; Root Breach Start is appended|Aldren's messenger, yes? Good. Set the prism down carefully. Your amulet is answering it before I have even touched the glass, which means this is older than a village watchtower and far less forgiving. Let me look.
DIALOGUE_TRAVELLERS_REST_SCHOLAR_ROOT_START||Traveller's Rest scholar dialogue starting Starfall Burrow|There is Starfall force still caught inside this fracture. Not much, but enough to point toward the old burrow beyond the watchtower. Starfall Burrow has been quiet too long for comfort, and if the prism woke there, something below it may answer your amulet as well. Go down, learn what guards the place, and return with whatever truth survives the trip.
DIALOGUE_TRAVELLERS_REST_SCHOLAR_ROOT_REMINDER||Traveller's Rest scholar Starfall Burrow reminder|Starfall Burrow is the next answer. Go beyond the watchtower, search its depths, and do not trust quiet blackglass.
DIALOGUE_TRAVELLERS_REST_SCHOLAR_ROOT_COMPLETE||Traveller's Rest scholar Starfall Burrow completion page; Highmark lead and reward are appended|A drake guarding a true blackglass fragment, and it spoke to your blood? That is no roadside oddity. The old wound is stirring again, and anyone who studies such things will feel the floor move under them. I will send warning to Telwynd, but you need more than my notes now.
DIALOGUE_TRAVELLERS_REST_SCHOLAR_ROOT_HIGHMARK_LEAD||Traveller's Rest scholar Starfall Burrow Highmark lead|Take the fragment to Highmark and speak with the White Seal. The road north starts at South Gate, runs through Stonecleft, and climbs The Underway to North Gate. Show the dwarves what you carry and make for the capital.
DIALOGUE_TRAVELLERS_REST_SCHOLAR_ROOT_REWARD||Traveller's Rest scholar Starfall Burrow reward line|Take this for the road. The Underway is no safe country, but it is the only road to Highmark.
DIALOGUE_TRAVELLERS_REST_SCHOLAR_ROOT_DONE||Traveller's Rest scholar post-Starfall Burrow idle line after Root Breach is complete|Do not linger on my account. Highmark and the White Seal need to see that fragment before rumor outruns you.
DIALOGUE_THROKK_STONEWARD_BREAKER||Throkk Stoneward Gate breaker|You saw the Stoneward Gate and lived to complain about it? Good. Dwarven hands built that gate, and I know the release for that old lock. Go back below Camp Kestrel; it should open now.
DIALOGUE_THROKK_STONEWARD_KEY_START||Throkk gives the Stoneward Key for the Stoneward Gate|You found the Stoneward Gate, then. Aye, that is dwarven make, but some elven glassworker got a hand into the lock. Rare craft: half forge, half elven glass, and tied to dragon-blood by the look of it.\nI can give you the Stoneward Key. The rest is on you: find a drake or dragon, spill it, and dip the key in fresh draconic blood before the corpse turns. I am not lending you a dragon too, friend.
DIALOGUE_THROKK_STONEWARD_KEY_REMINDER||Throkk reminder after giving the Stoneward Key|The Stoneward Key still needs fresh draconic blood. Find a drake or dragon, use the key on the corpse before it rots, then take the blooded key back below.
DIALOGUE_THROKK_STONEWARD_KEY_BLOODED||Throkk reminder after the Stoneward Key is blooded|That blood woke the glass, good. Take the Stoneward Key back below. The old gate should answer it now.
DIALOGUE_THROKK_BLACKGLASS_FORGE_COLD||Throkk blackglass forge blocked while runeforge is cold|The runeforge is still cold. Core, heat, and time come before blackglass.
DIALOGUE_THROKK_BLACKGLASS_FORGE_WITH_SHARD||Throkk blackglass forge access with shard|That shard rings true. The runeforge is ready.
DIALOGUE_THROKK_STONEWARD_OPEN||Throkk after Stoneward Gate opened|The Stoneward broke clean. Deep gate is open, and whatever waits below has fewer excuses now.
DIALOGUE_THROKK_UNDERWAY_TURNIN||Throkk Underway turn-in|By the forge, you made it back alive. With The Underway open, Stonecleft can breathe and Highmark is no longer a story on the far side of stone. If you mean to go there, go now.
DIALOGUE_THROKK_BLACKGLASS_FORGE_NO_SHARD||Throkk blackglass forge access without shard|The runeforge is lit and steady. Bring true blackglass when you want it worked.
DIALOGUE_THROKK_UNDERWAY_CLEAR||Throkk Underway clear idle|The Underway is clear at last. Took a stranger to shame the old gate open, but open is open.
DIALOGUE_THROKK_UNDERWAY_REMINDER||Throkk Underway reminder|The drake is still holding North Gate. Kill it, and you can get through to Highmark.
DIALOGUE_THROKK_UNDERWAY_START||Throkk Underway first offer|Highmark, is it? Then you need The Underway. North Gate is blocked by a drake; while it breathes, nothing gets through.
DIALOGUE_THROKK_UNDERWAY_START_OBJECTIVE||Throkk Underway objective|No one here is eager to feed it another helm. I will have the gate warden let you through. Kill the drake at North Gate, then you can get through to Highmark. Once you are out, keep north to the city.

# Quest log entries
QUEST_LOG_TUTORIAL_NOTE_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Tutorial Note|Deliver Harren's note to the dockmaster.
QUEST_LOG_TUTORIAL_NOTE_DETAIL||quest log detail for Tutorial Note|Harren gave me a note for Dockmaster Garran at the harbor.
QUEST_LOG_TUTORIAL_CLASS_ACTION_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Tutorial Class Action|Use your class technique in a fight.
QUEST_LOG_TUTORIAL_CLASS_ACTION_DETAIL||quest log detail for Tutorial Class Action|Guard Breck wants to see a class action before I leave Brindle Quay.\nOpen class actions with {class_actions}, then use one on the training dummy.
QUEST_LOG_TUTORIAL_FIRST_AID_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Tutorial First Aid|Tend your wounds with a bandage.
QUEST_LOG_TUTORIAL_FIRST_AID_DETAIL||quest log detail for Tutorial First Aid|Use a field dressing to bind wounds from the fight.
QUEST_LOG_TUTORIAL_SLEEP_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Tutorial Sleep|Sleep at the inn.
QUEST_LOG_TUTORIAL_SLEEP_DETAIL||quest log detail for Tutorial Sleep|The dockmaster said to rest at Orrin's inn before the boat leaves.
QUEST_LOG_TUTORIAL_CAMP_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Tutorial Camp|Rest using the camping kit.
QUEST_LOG_TUTORIAL_CAMP_DETAIL||quest log detail for Tutorial Camp|Orrin gave me a camping kit after the inn rest. Use it to rest on the road.
QUEST_LOG_TUTORIAL_FEED_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Tutorial Feed|Eat to sate your hunger.
QUEST_LOG_TUTORIAL_FEED_DETAIL||quest log detail for Tutorial Feed|Hunger set in. Eat rations or tavern food to recover.
QUEST_LOG_THANK_HARL_TITLE||quest log title for Thank Harl|Thank Captain Thauld
QUEST_LOG_THANK_HARL_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Thank Harl|Thank Captain Thauld at the docks.
QUEST_LOG_THANK_HARL_DETAIL||quest log detail for Thank Harl|Captain Thauld brought the boat through the storm. Thank him at Reedwater Docks.
QUEST_LOG_HEAD_TO_HAVENFORD_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Head To Havenford|Reach Havenford by the north road.
QUEST_LOG_HEAD_TO_HAVENFORD_DETAIL||quest log detail for Head To Havenford|Captain Thauld said the north road from Reedwater leads to Havenford.
QUEST_LOG_CAVE_CHIEF_RETURN_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Cave Chief Return|Report the cave chief's death to Aldren.
QUEST_LOG_CAVE_CHIEF_RETURN_DETAIL||quest log detail for Cave Chief Return|The cave chief fell in the ridge cave. Aldren in Havenford should know.
QUEST_LOG_CAVE_CHIEF_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Cave Chief|Silence the cave chief in the ridge cave.
QUEST_LOG_CAVE_CHIEF_DETAIL||quest log detail for Cave Chief|Aldren says the goblin raids come from the eastern ridge cave and are too organized for ordinary vermin. I should find the chieftain driving them, kill him, and return to Havenford.
QUEST_LOG_ROOT_BREACH_LEAD_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Root Breach Lead|Investigate the Starfall Burrow.
QUEST_LOG_ROOT_BREACH_LEAD_DETAIL||quest log detail for Root Breach Lead|Scholar Cael says the prism points north from the Ruined Watchtower to Starfall Burrow. Something below that old breach is answering my amulet.
QUEST_LOG_WATCHTOWER_START_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective after Cave Chief before Watchtower Prism starts|Investigate the ruined watchtower past the ridge.
QUEST_LOG_WATCHTOWER_START_DETAIL||quest log detail after Cave Chief before Watchtower Prism starts|Aldren said lights show at the ruined watchtower past the ridge, and he gave me the old key for the sealed upper stair door. I should investigate the upper room and bring back whatever stirs there.
QUEST_LOG_WATCHTOWER_SEARCH_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective while searching Ruined Watchtower for the prism|Search the Ruined Watchtower for the prism.
QUEST_LOG_WATCHTOWER_SEARCH_DETAIL||quest log detail while searching Ruined Watchtower for the prism|Aldren gave me the old key for the sealed upper stair door. I should search the Ruined Watchtower, find the prism, and bring it back before the stirring grows worse.
QUEST_LOG_WATCHTOWER_RETURN_CHIEF_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective after finding the fractured prism|Return the fractured prism to Aldren.
QUEST_LOG_WATCHTOWER_RETURN_CHIEF_DETAIL||quest log detail after finding the fractured prism|The fractured prism came from the watchtower. The amulet answers its pulse. Aldren in Havenford should see it.
QUEST_LOG_WATCHTOWER_TO_SCHOLAR_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective after Elder sends the prism to Traveller's Rest|Take the prism to the scholar at Traveller's Rest.
QUEST_LOG_WATCHTOWER_TO_SCHOLAR_DETAIL||quest log detail after Elder sends the prism to Traveller's Rest|The fractured prism came from the watchtower, and Aldren says Scholar Cael at Traveller's Rest must see it. I should take the north road from Havenford, turn east at the fork, and keep on until I see the inn.
QUEST_LOG_ROOT_BREACH_RETURN_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Root Breach Return|Take the blackglass shard to Scholar Cael.
QUEST_LOG_ROOT_BREACH_RETURN_DETAIL||quest log detail for Root Breach Return|I have the blackglass shard from Starfall Burrow. Scholar Cael at Traveller's Rest should see it.
QUEST_LOG_ROOT_BREACH_COLLECT_SHARD_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective after Vrask dies before the shard is picked up|Collect the blackglass shard in the Starfall Burrow.
QUEST_LOG_ROOT_BREACH_COLLECT_SHARD_DETAIL||quest log detail after Vrask dies before the shard is picked up|Vrask fell in the Starfall Burrow, and a blackglass shard remains where he died. I should pick it up before returning to Scholar Cael.
QUEST_LOG_ROOT_BREACH_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Root Breach|Slay the drake in the Starfall Burrow.
QUEST_LOG_ROOT_BREACH_DETAIL||quest log detail for Root Breach|Starfall Burrow lies north of the Ruined Watchtower, where roots and blackglass run under the ridge. A drake guards the lower breach; I should kill it and bring back any shard the amulet answers.
QUEST_LOG_UNDERWAY_REACH_SOUTH_GATE_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for reaching South Gate|Travel northwest from Traveller's Rest to South Gate.
QUEST_LOG_UNDERWAY_REACH_SOUTH_GATE_DETAIL||quest log detail for reaching South Gate|Scholar Cael says Highmark lies beyond the mountains. The dwarven road begins at South Gate; I should take the northern road from Traveller's Rest to the mountain gate.
QUEST_LOG_UNDERWAY_REACH_STONECLEFT_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for reaching Stonecleft|Reach Stonecleft.
QUEST_LOG_UNDERWAY_REACH_STONECLEFT_DETAIL||quest log detail for reaching Stonecleft|South Gate opens into the South Gate Tunnels. I should continue through the tunnels to Stonecleft and ask the dwarves how to reach Highmark.
QUEST_LOG_UNDERWAY_ASK_THROKK_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Underway Ask Throkk|Clear the drake at North Gate.
QUEST_LOG_UNDERWAY_ASK_THROKK_DETAIL||quest log detail for Underway Ask Throkk|Stonecleft's north road is blocked, and Throkk says a drake holds North Gate. I should clear the gate before the dwarves can trust The Underway again.
QUEST_LOG_UNDERWAY_RETURN_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Underway Return|Continue north to Highmark.
QUEST_LOG_UNDERWAY_RETURN_DETAIL||quest log detail for Underway Return|The drake fell at North Gate, and the road through the mountains is open. I can continue north to Highmark.
QUEST_LOG_UNDERWAY_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Underway|Clear the drake at North Gate.
QUEST_LOG_UNDERWAY_DETAIL||quest log detail for Underway|Throkk says The Underway is the road to Highmark, but a drake blocks North Gate. I should kill it and continue north once the road opens.
QUEST_LOG_WHITE_SEAL_I_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for White Seal I|Reach Highmark.
QUEST_LOG_WHITE_SEAL_I_DETAIL||quest log detail for White Seal I|The Underway is open. I should follow the dwarven road through the mountains and continue to Highmark, where the White Seal can examine the fragment.
QUEST_LOG_BEACON_PRISM_TALK_THAREC_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for speaking with Tharec after reaching Highmark|Speak with High Canon Tharec in Highmark.
QUEST_LOG_BEACON_PRISM_TALK_THAREC_DETAIL||quest log detail for speaking with Tharec after reaching Highmark|Highmark is reached. High Canon Tharec can explain what the White Seal knows about the star, the bloodline, and the dragons stirring below.
QUEST_LOG_BEACON_PRISM_TALK_ORYN_OBJECTIVE||legacy quest log objective for speaking with Oryn after Tharec starts the Beacon work|Speak with High Canon Tharec in Highmark.
QUEST_LOG_BEACON_PRISM_TALK_ORYN_DETAIL||legacy quest log detail for speaking with Oryn after Tharec starts the Beacon work|Tharec handles the Beacon Prism rite. I should recover the prism and bring it back to him.
QUEST_LOG_BEACON_PRISM_RETURN_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Beacon Prism Return|Return the Beacon Prism to High Canon Tharec.
QUEST_LOG_BEACON_PRISM_RETURN_DETAIL||quest log detail for Beacon Prism Return|The Beacon Prism is recovered. Tharec can set the prism and use my blood to turn the star to Lightglass.
QUEST_LOG_BEACON_PRISM_RECOVER_CLAIMED_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Beacon Prism Recover Claimed|Recover the Beacon Prism and return to High Canon Tharec.
QUEST_LOG_BEACON_PRISM_RECOVER_CLAIMED_DETAIL||quest log detail for Beacon Prism Recover Claimed|The prism was claimed from the White Seal Tower, but it is not in my pack. Tharec still needs it in Highmark.
QUEST_LOG_BEACON_PRISM_CLAIM_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Beacon Prism Claim|Claim the Beacon Prism from the White Seal Tower.
QUEST_LOG_BEACON_PRISM_CLAIM_DETAIL||quest log detail for Beacon Prism Claim|The dragon fell at the beacon. The Beacon Prism still glows above the chamber.
QUEST_LOG_BEACON_PRISM_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Beacon Prism|Recover the Beacon Prism from the White Seal Tower far down the east road.
QUEST_LOG_BEACON_PRISM_DETAIL||quest log detail for Beacon Prism|Tharec says the Beacon Prism is in the Tower of the White Seal far down the east road from Highmark. A dragon holds the tower. Recover the prism and bring it back to him.
QUEST_LOG_BEACON_PRISM_PREPARE_VAULT_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Beacon Prism fallback return|Return to High Canon Tharec.
QUEST_LOG_BEACON_PRISM_PREPARE_VAULT_DETAIL||quest log detail for Beacon Prism fallback return|The star should be Lightglass now, but Tharec still needs to settle the Beacon Prism rite.
QUEST_LOG_WHITE_VAULT_OPEN_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for White Vault Open|Open the White Vault.
QUEST_LOG_WHITE_VAULT_OPEN_DETAIL||quest log detail for White Vault Open|The prism is set. Sacristan Oryn waits beside the vault stair in Highmark's White Seal hall. Something draconic waits below.
QUEST_LOG_WHITE_VAULT_RETURN_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for White Vault Return|Return to Sacristan Oryn.
QUEST_LOG_WHITE_VAULT_RETURN_DETAIL||quest log detail for White Vault Return|The greater drake fell in the inner chamber. The White Vault is quiet enough for Oryn to inspect.
QUEST_LOG_WHITE_VAULT_RETURN_FINAL_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for White Vault Return Final|Return to Sacristan Oryn.
QUEST_LOG_WHITE_VAULT_RETURN_FINAL_DETAIL||quest log detail for White Vault Return Final|The vault beast is slain. The White Vault is quiet enough for Oryn to inspect.
QUEST_LOG_WHITE_VAULT_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for White Vault|Slay the beast in the White Vault.
QUEST_LOG_WHITE_VAULT_DETAIL||quest log detail for White Vault|Oryn opened the White Vault stair. Something draconic waits in the lower chamber. Kill it, then return to him.
QUEST_LOG_FINAL_DESCENT_II_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Final Descent Ii|Face the primordial dragon in the Starfall Core.
QUEST_LOG_FINAL_DESCENT_II_DETAIL||quest log detail for Final Descent Ii|The Lightglass star answers in the Starfall Core. The primordial dragon waits where the deep rumble becomes a voice.
QUEST_LOG_FINAL_DESCENT_I_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Final Descent I|Enter the Starfall Core.
QUEST_LOG_FINAL_DESCENT_I_DETAIL||quest log detail for Final Descent I|The final blood seal is open. A core rift waits below it, bright with blackglass glare, leading into the Starfall Core.
QUEST_LOG_BLOOD_OF_THE_ANCIENTS_III_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Blood Of The Ancients Iii|Open the final blood seal.
QUEST_LOG_BLOOD_OF_THE_ANCIENTS_III_DETAIL||quest log detail for Blood Of The Ancients Iii|Theryn readied the Ancient Istarian Manuscript. At the final blood seal, I should mark the page with my blood and read it aloud while the Lightglass star answers.
QUEST_LOG_BLOOD_OF_THE_ANCIENTS_II_OBJECTIVE||legacy quest log objective for Blood Of The Ancients II|Find the Ancient Istarian Manuscript.
QUEST_LOG_BLOOD_OF_THE_ANCIENTS_II_DETAIL||legacy quest log detail for Blood Of The Ancients II|The final blood seal answers the Lightglass star, but old Istarian work is still missing. Theryn Rusk in Havenford may know what manuscript can help.
QUEST_LOG_BLOOD_OF_THE_ANCIENTS_II_THAREC_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Blood Of The Ancients II after seeing the final blood seal|Ask High Canon Tharec about the final blood seal.
QUEST_LOG_BLOOD_OF_THE_ANCIENTS_II_THAREC_DETAIL||quest log detail for Blood Of The Ancients II after seeing the final blood seal|The final blood seal is ancient Istarian, not dwarven work. It answered my blood and the Lightglass star, but did not open. I should tell Tharec what I discovered down here.
QUEST_LOG_BLOOD_OF_THE_ANCIENTS_II_THERYN_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Blood Of The Ancients II after Tharec sends the player to Theryn|Ask Old Theryn Rusk about the Istarian seal.
QUEST_LOG_BLOOD_OF_THE_ANCIENTS_II_THERYN_DETAIL||quest log detail for Blood Of The Ancients II after Tharec sends the player to Theryn|Tharec thinks the seal is old Istarian work and admits he is not certain. Theryn Rusk in Havenford may know what kind of manuscript can make it answer.
QUEST_LOG_BLOOD_OF_THE_ANCIENTS_II_BARROW_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Blood Of The Ancients II manuscript search|Recover the Ancient Istarian Manuscript from King's Barrow.
QUEST_LOG_BLOOD_OF_THE_ANCIENTS_II_BARROW_DETAIL||quest log detail for Blood Of The Ancients II manuscript search|Theryn says an Ancient Istarian Manuscript may be buried with King Halric in King's Barrow. I should search the barrow for it.
QUEST_LOG_BLOOD_OF_THE_ANCIENTS_II_RETURN_THERYN_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Blood Of The Ancients II manuscript return|Take the Ancient Istarian Manuscript to Old Theryn Rusk.
QUEST_LOG_BLOOD_OF_THE_ANCIENTS_II_RETURN_THERYN_DETAIL||quest log detail for Blood Of The Ancients II manuscript return|King Halric is dead again, and the Ancient Istarian Manuscript is in my pack. Theryn Rusk in Havenford should read it before I return to the final blood seal.
QUEST_LOG_BLOOD_OF_THE_ANCIENTS_II_MANUSCRIPT_LOST_DETAIL||quest log detail when the manuscript was claimed but is missing|The Ancient Istarian Manuscript came out of King's Barrow, but it is not in my pack. I need it before Theryn can ready the final blood seal working.
QUEST_LOG_BLOOD_OF_THE_ANCIENTS_I_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Blood Of The Ancients I|Find the final blood seal.
QUEST_LOG_BLOOD_OF_THE_ANCIENTS_I_DETAIL||quest log detail for Blood Of The Ancients I|The Stoneward Gate is open, and the route drops past it into deeper blackglass. Somewhere in the Sundering Depths, the final blood seal is waiting.
QUEST_LOG_DEPTHS_OF_STARFALL_III_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Depths Of Starfall Iii|Find and open the Stoneward Gate.
QUEST_LOG_DEPTHS_OF_STARFALL_III_DETAIL||quest log detail for Depths Of Starfall Iii|The lower Istarian route should lead through the Stoneward Gate. I need to find it and work out what keeps it shut.
QUEST_LOG_DEPTHS_OF_STARFALL_III_ASK_THROKK_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Depths Of Starfall III ask Throkk state|Ask in Stonecleft about the Stoneward Gate.
QUEST_LOG_DEPTHS_OF_STARFALL_III_ASK_THROKK_DETAIL||quest log detail for Depths Of Starfall III ask Throkk state|The Stoneward Gate is inscribed with dwarven runes around the lock. I do not know how to wake it, but the dwarves in Stonecleft may recognize the craft.
QUEST_LOG_DEPTHS_OF_STARFALL_III_BLOOD_KEY_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Depths Of Starfall III blood key state|Find fresh draconic blood for the Stoneward Key.
QUEST_LOG_DEPTHS_OF_STARFALL_III_BLOOD_KEY_DETAIL||quest log detail for Depths Of Starfall III blood key state|Throkk gave me the Stoneward Key, dwarven work set with elven glass. I will have to kill a drake or dragon, then use the key on the corpse before it rots.
QUEST_LOG_DEPTHS_OF_STARFALL_III_RETURN_GATE_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Depths Of Starfall III return gate state|Return to the Stoneward Gate with the blooded key.
QUEST_LOG_DEPTHS_OF_STARFALL_III_RETURN_GATE_DETAIL||quest log detail for Depths Of Starfall III return gate state|The Stoneward Key is blooded. I should take it back to the Stoneward Gate in the lower Istarian Tunnels.
QUEST_LOG_DEPTHS_OF_STARFALL_II_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Depths Of Starfall Ii|Delve deeper below Blackglass Cavern.
QUEST_LOG_DEPTHS_OF_STARFALL_II_DETAIL||quest log detail for Depths Of Starfall Ii|The lower Blackglass descent opens into old Istarian tunnels. I should keep going down and find what is feeding the blackglass.
QUEST_LOG_DEPTHS_OF_STARFALL_I_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Depths Of Starfall I|Enter Blackglass Cavern.
QUEST_LOG_DEPTHS_OF_STARFALL_I_DETAIL||quest log detail for Depths Of Starfall I|The Lightglass star is clear at last. Blackglass Cavern is the strongest source of the corruption rising from below. I should go down and find what holds the lower way.
QUEST_LOG_GLASSROOT_HOLLOW_RETURN_TITLE||quest log title for Moonwell Reverie Return|Moonwell Reverie
QUEST_LOG_GLASSROOT_HOLLOW_RETURN_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Moonwell Reverie Return|Go to Telwynd in the forest north of Moonwell Observatory.
QUEST_LOG_GLASSROOT_HOLLOW_RETURN_DETAIL||quest log detail for Moonwell Reverie Return|I saw Telwynd in the forest north of the observatory. It is revealed on the map. I should go there and speak with Warden Sairveth.
QUEST_LOG_GLASSROOT_HOLLOW_TITLE||quest log title for Moonwell Reverie|Moonwell Reverie
QUEST_LOG_GLASSROOT_HOLLOW_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Moonwell Reverie|Kill Mordraxis in Glassroot Hollow.
QUEST_LOG_GLASSROOT_HOLLOW_DETAIL||quest log detail for Moonwell Reverie|Eiradha says Telwynd is hidden in the forest north of Moonwell Observatory. Mordraxis dragged the Moonwell lens to Glassroot Hollow, east from the crossroads outside Highmark. I should kill the drake and recover it.
QUEST_LOG_GLASSROOT_HOLLOW_LENS_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective after recovering the Moonwell lens|Set the Moonwell lens in the observatory frame.
QUEST_LOG_GLASSROOT_HOLLOW_LENS_DETAIL||quest log detail after recovering the Moonwell lens|I recovered the Moonwell lens from Mordraxis. I should set it in the frame at Moonwell Observatory. Through the lens I should see Telwynd clearly.
QUEST_LOG_GHOSTWOOD_SMOKE_RETURN_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Ghostwood Smoke Return|Return to the Kestrel Lancer at Camp Kestrel.
QUEST_LOG_GHOSTWOOD_SMOKE_RETURN_DETAIL||quest log detail for Ghostwood Smoke Return|Veyr is slain. The ghostwood smoke has lifted. The Lancer should know.
QUEST_LOG_GHOSTWOOD_SMOKE_ASK_EIRADHA_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Ghostwood Smoke Ask Eiradha|Ask Eiradha about the ghostwood.
QUEST_LOG_GHOSTWOOD_SMOKE_ASK_EIRADHA_DETAIL||quest log detail for Ghostwood Smoke Ask Eiradha|The Kestrel Lancer at Camp Kestrel said Eiradha may have the trace on the ghostwood smoke.
QUEST_LOG_GHOSTWOOD_SMOKE_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Ghostwood Smoke|Follow the ghostwood smoke to the old tower and kill Veyr.
QUEST_LOG_GHOSTWOOD_SMOKE_DETAIL||quest log detail for Ghostwood Smoke|Eiradha traced the trouble. Veyr holds the tower in the Ghostwood. Follow the smoke west and end it.
QUEST_LOG_BREAK_ROCKMAW_KEEP_I_RETURN_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Break Rockmaw Keep I Return|Return to the Watch Sergeant at Camp Kestrel.
QUEST_LOG_BREAK_ROCKMAW_KEEP_I_RETURN_DETAIL||quest log detail for Break Rockmaw Keep I Return|Maug and Brond are slain. The rockmaw keep is broken. The sergeant should know.
QUEST_LOG_BREAK_ROCKMAW_KEEP_I_BROND_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Break Rockmaw Keep I Brond|Kill Brond, the Ogre Champion in Rockmaw Keep.
QUEST_LOG_BREAK_ROCKMAW_KEEP_I_BROND_DETAIL||quest log detail for Break Rockmaw Keep I Brond|Maug is slain. Only Brond remains in the keep. Finish it.
QUEST_LOG_BREAK_ROCKMAW_KEEP_I_MAUG_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Break Rockmaw Keep I Maug|Kill Maug, the Ettin in Rockmaw Keep.
QUEST_LOG_BREAK_ROCKMAW_KEEP_I_MAUG_DETAIL||quest log detail for Break Rockmaw Keep I Maug|Brond is slain. Only Maug remains. End it.
QUEST_LOG_BREAK_ROCKMAW_KEEP_I_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Break Rockmaw Keep I|Kill the leaders of Rockmaw Keep.
QUEST_LOG_BREAK_ROCKMAW_KEEP_I_DETAIL||quest log detail for Break Rockmaw Keep I|Rockmaw Keep near the coastal mountains is a threat. Break its leaders for the Watch Sergeant at Camp Kestrel.
QUEST_LOG_BREAK_ROCKMAW_KEEP_II_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Break Rockmaw Keep Ii|Enter Rockmaw Keep west of Camp Kestrel and inspect Kestrel's outer-yard outpost.
QUEST_LOG_BREAK_ROCKMAW_KEEP_II_DETAIL||quest log detail for Break Rockmaw Keep Ii|Maug and Brond are slain. Kestrel now holds Rockmaw Keep's outer yard; step inside the keep entrance to see the new beds, stores, and field forge.
QUEST_LOG_MOON_BITTEN_CAVE_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Moon-Bitten Cave|Hunt Varroth in Inconspicuous Cave.
QUEST_LOG_MOON_BITTEN_CAVE_DETAIL||quest log detail for Moon-Bitten Cave|The Watch Sergeant says Varroth's pack is below Inconspicuous Cave, east of Highmark. Kill Varroth and report back to Camp Kestrel.
QUEST_LOG_MOON_BITTEN_CAVE_RETURN_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Moon-Bitten Cave after Varroth dies|Return to the Watch Sergeant at Camp Kestrel.
QUEST_LOG_MOON_BITTEN_CAVE_RETURN_DETAIL||quest log detail for Moon-Bitten Cave after Varroth dies|Varroth is slain. The hidden pack is scattered. The sergeant should know.
QUEST_LOG_KESTREL_HUNT_GRUMMOK_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for the Grummok Kestrel Hunt|Hunt Grummok in Bloodied Cave.
QUEST_LOG_KESTREL_HUNT_GRUMMOK_DETAIL||quest log detail for the Grummok Kestrel Hunt|The Watch Sergeant says a troll band is gathering in Bloodied Cave, northeast of Camp Kestrel. Kill Grummok and report back to camp.
QUEST_LOG_KESTREL_HUNT_GRUMMOK_RETURN_DETAIL||quest log detail after Grummok dies|Grummok is slain. His troll band is broken. The sergeant should know.
QUEST_LOG_CLEAR_MOONWELL_ROAD_RETURN_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Clear Moonwell Road Return|Return to Warden Sairveth in Telwynd.
QUEST_LOG_CLEAR_MOONWELL_ROAD_RETURN_DETAIL||quest log detail for Clear Moonwell Road Return|The Moonwell Tunnels are clear. Warden Sairveth in Telwynd should know.
QUEST_LOG_CLEAR_MOONWELL_ROAD_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Clear Moonwell Road|Clear the Moonwell Tunnels.
QUEST_LOG_CLEAR_MOONWELL_ROAD_DETAIL||quest log detail for Clear Moonwell Road|Warden Sairveth says the Moonwell Tunnels south of Telwynd are blocked, and Telwynd's workers cannot safely pass. I should set both tunnel dials to open the far exit so the grove can reach the old site again.
QUEST_LOG_ELDERWYRM_GROVE_RETURN_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Elderwyrm Grove Return|Return to Warden Sairveth in Telwynd.
QUEST_LOG_ELDERWYRM_GROVE_RETURN_DETAIL||quest log detail for Elderwyrm Grove Return|The elderwyrm is slain. The grove is reclaimed. Warden Sairveth in Telwynd should know.
QUEST_LOG_ELDERWYRM_GROVE_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Elderwyrm Grove|Reclaim Elderwyrm Grove.
QUEST_LOG_ELDERWYRM_GROVE_DETAIL||quest log detail for Elderwyrm Grove|Sairveth and Eivyss say Elderwyrm Grove, in the furthest northern mountains, is failing under old ward trouble, and Caerwyn has bent the green magic around himself. I should reclaim the grove before Telwynd sends workers through.
QUEST_LOG_BURIED_HIGHWIND_REPORT_CATACOMBS_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Buried Highwind Report Catacombs|Search the Highwind Catacombs.
QUEST_LOG_BURIED_HIGHWIND_REPORT_CATACOMBS_DETAIL||quest log detail for Buried Highwind Report Catacombs|You found the catacombs. The highwind is buried there.
QUEST_LOG_BURIED_HIGHWIND_FIND_CATACOMBS_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Buried Highwind Find Catacombs|Find the stair to Highwind's catacombs.
QUEST_LOG_BURIED_HIGHWIND_FIND_CATACOMBS_DETAIL||quest log detail for Buried Highwind Find Catacombs|Theryn Rusk says the old Highwind trail points under the monastery. I should search the grounds for the stair into Highwind's catacombs.
QUEST_LOG_BURIED_HIGHWIND_ASK_THERYN_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Buried Highwind Ask Theryn|Ask Theryn Rusk in Havenford.
QUEST_LOG_BURIED_HIGHWIND_ASK_THERYN_DETAIL||quest log detail for Buried Highwind Ask Theryn|You inspected the monastery. Ask Theryn Rusk in Havenford what it means.
QUEST_LOG_BURIED_HIGHWIND_RETURN_MARKS_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Buried Highwind Return Marks|Return to Warden Sairveth in Telwynd.
QUEST_LOG_BURIED_HIGHWIND_RETURN_MARKS_DETAIL||quest log detail for Buried Highwind Return Marks|You inspected the monastery. Warden Sairveth in Telwynd should know.
QUEST_LOG_BURIED_HIGHWIND_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Buried Highwind|Find the buried highwind.
QUEST_LOG_BURIED_HIGHWIND_DETAIL||quest log detail for Buried Highwind|The buried Highwind is tied to the old monastery in the far east hills and the catacombs beneath it. I should search those places and follow whatever proof survives.
QUEST_LOG_LOST_PURIFIER_RETURN_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Lost Purifier Return|Return to Antiquary Tovan at White Seal Antiquities in Highmark.
QUEST_LOG_LOST_PURIFIER_RETURN_DETAIL||quest log detail after rescuing Tovan from Highmark Aqueduct|Antiquary Tovan is rescued from Highmark Aqueduct. Return to him at White Seal Antiquities in Highmark.
QUEST_LOG_LOST_PURIFIER_RETURN_LIGHTHOUSE_DETAIL||quest log detail after rescuing Tovan from the lighthouse basement|Antiquary Tovan is rescued from beneath the Old Imperial Lighthouse. Return to him at White Seal Antiquities in Highmark.
QUEST_LOG_LOST_PURIFIER_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for the Highmark Aqueduct variant|Find Antiquary Tovan in Highmark Aqueduct.
QUEST_LOG_LOST_PURIFIER_DETAIL||quest log detail for the Highmark Aqueduct variant|Antiquary Tovan vanished in Highmark Aqueduct, in the hills west of Highmark, while tracing an old purifier. I should search the waterworks and bring him back if he is still alive.
QUEST_LOG_LOST_PURIFIER_LIGHTHOUSE_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for the lighthouse basement variant|Find Antiquary Tovan beneath the Old Imperial Lighthouse.
QUEST_LOG_LOST_PURIFIER_LIGHTHOUSE_DETAIL||quest log detail for the lighthouse basement variant|Antiquary Tovan vanished in the flooded basement beneath the Old Imperial Lighthouse, far southeast of Highmark beyond Traveller's Rest. I should search below the tower and bring him back if he is still alive.
QUEST_LOG_PILGRIMAGE_FIRST_OBJECTIVE_COUNT||quest log objective for Pilgrimage first phase, placeholder 0 altar count|Mark the altars. ({0}/3)
QUEST_LOG_PILGRIMAGE_FIRST_DETAIL||quest log detail for Pilgrimage first phase|The White Seal Priest gave a plain charm. Mark the altars at Havenford, the Roadside Shrine, and Reedmire until it warms.
QUEST_LOG_PILGRIMAGE_RETURN_BLESS_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Pilgrimage after first altars|Return to the White Seal Priest in Highmark.
QUEST_LOG_PILGRIMAGE_RETURN_BLESS_DETAIL||quest log detail for Pilgrimage after first altars|The plain charm holds all three marks. Return it to the White Seal Priest in Highmark.
QUEST_LOG_PILGRIMAGE_OLDROOT_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Pilgrimage Oldroot phase|Take the dormant charm to the altar at Oldroot Temple.
QUEST_LOG_PILGRIMAGE_OLDROOT_DETAIL||quest log detail for Pilgrimage Oldroot phase|The dormant white seal charm needs the oldroot altar in Oldroot Temple, in the forest near Highmark. The roots will wake it.
QUEST_LOG_PILGRIMAGE_RETURN_FINAL_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Pilgrimage final hand-in|Return the white seal charm to the White Seal Priest in Highmark.
QUEST_LOG_PILGRIMAGE_RETURN_FINAL_DETAIL||quest log detail for Pilgrimage final hand-in|The charm wakes from the oldroot. Return it to the White Seal Priest in Highmark.
QUEST_LOG_MOONWELL_ALIGNMENT_TELWYND_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Moonwell Alignment before lens attunement|Take the misaligned lens to Telwynd for attunement.
QUEST_LOG_MOONWELL_ALIGNMENT_TELWYND_DETAIL||quest log detail for Moonwell Alignment before lens attunement|Veydras in Highmark gave a misaligned moonwell lens from the seal stores. Eivyss in Telwynd can attune it.
QUEST_LOG_MOONWELL_ALIGNMENT_REPLACE_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Moonwell Alignment when the misaligned lens is missing|Return to Veydras in Highmark for a replacement lens.
QUEST_LOG_MOONWELL_ALIGNMENT_REPLACE_DETAIL||quest log detail for Moonwell Alignment when the misaligned lens is missing|Veydras in Highmark can replace the missing misaligned moonwell lens from the seal stores.
QUEST_LOG_MOONWELL_ALIGNMENT_INSTALL_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Moonwell Alignment after lens attunement|Install the attuned lens at Moonwell Observatory.
QUEST_LOG_MOONWELL_ALIGNMENT_INSTALL_DETAIL||quest log detail for Moonwell Alignment after lens attunement|The lens is attuned. Seat it in the cracked Moonwell frame at the observatory south of Telwynd.
QUEST_LOG_MOONWELL_ALIGNMENT_RECOVER_ATTUNED_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Moonwell Alignment when the attuned lens is missing|Recover the attuned lens from Eivyss in Telwynd.
QUEST_LOG_MOONWELL_ALIGNMENT_RECOVER_ATTUNED_DETAIL||quest log detail for Moonwell Alignment when the attuned lens is missing|The attuned moonwell lens is missing. Eivyss in Telwynd can restore it.
QUEST_LOG_MOONWELL_ALIGNMENT_RETURN_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Moonwell Alignment final hand-in|Return to Veydras in Highmark.
QUEST_LOG_MOONWELL_ALIGNMENT_RETURN_DETAIL||quest log detail for Moonwell Alignment final hand-in|The attuned lens is seated in the Moonwell frame. The observatory light steadies. Return to Veydras in Highmark.
QUEST_LOG_CLEANSING_VAULT_RETURN_ORYN_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Cleansing the Vault if the starting crystal is missing|Return to Sacristan Oryn.
QUEST_LOG_CLEANSING_VAULT_RETURN_ORYN_DETAIL||quest log detail for Cleansing the Vault if the starting crystal is missing|Oryn says the White Vault is open but still fouled. He should know if the tainted crystal is missing.
QUEST_LOG_CLEANSING_VAULT_TAKE_EIVYSS_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Cleansing the Vault after receiving the tainted crystal|Take the Tainted White Vault Crystal to Eivyss Glass-Singer.
QUEST_LOG_CLEANSING_VAULT_TAKE_EIVYSS_DETAIL||quest log detail for Cleansing the Vault after receiving the tainted crystal|Oryn gave me a tainted crystal from the White Vault. Eivyss Glass-Singer in Telwynd may know how to tune it for a cleaner rite.
QUEST_LOG_CLEANSING_VAULT_RECOVER_TAINTED_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Cleansing the Vault when the tainted crystal is missing|Recover the Tainted White Vault Crystal.
QUEST_LOG_CLEANSING_VAULT_RECOVER_TAINTED_DETAIL||quest log detail for Cleansing the Vault when the tainted crystal is missing|The tainted White Vault crystal is missing. Eivyss cannot tune what I am not carrying.
QUEST_LOG_CLEANSING_VAULT_MOONWELL_RITE_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Cleansing the Vault after Eivyss tunes the crystal|Take the Resonant White Vault Crystal to the lower Moonwell rite.
QUEST_LOG_CLEANSING_VAULT_MOONWELL_RITE_DETAIL||quest log detail for Cleansing the Vault after Eivyss tunes the crystal|Eivyss tuned the crystal. I should take it to the lower ritual chamber beneath Moonwell Observatory and touch it to the Moonwell Rite.
QUEST_LOG_CLEANSING_VAULT_RECOVER_RESONANT_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Cleansing the Vault when the resonant crystal is missing|Recover the Resonant White Vault Crystal.
QUEST_LOG_CLEANSING_VAULT_RECOVER_RESONANT_DETAIL||quest log detail for Cleansing the Vault when the resonant crystal is missing|The resonant White Vault crystal is missing. The lower Moonwell rite needs it.
QUEST_LOG_CLEANSING_VAULT_DEFEAT_ECHO_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Cleansing the Vault after the Moonwell Echo appears|Defeat the Moonwell Echo.
QUEST_LOG_CLEANSING_VAULT_DEFEAT_ECHO_DETAIL||quest log detail for Cleansing the Vault after the Moonwell Echo appears|The Moonwell Rite woke a pale echo in the lower chamber. The rite will not finish while it holds the crystal's light.
QUEST_LOG_CLEANSING_VAULT_FINISH_RITE_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Cleansing the Vault after the Moonwell Echo dies|Touch the crystal to the Moonwell Rite again.
QUEST_LOG_CLEANSING_VAULT_FINISH_RITE_DETAIL||quest log detail for Cleansing the Vault after the Moonwell Echo dies|The Moonwell Echo is gone. The lower rite should be able to send the crystal's clean resonance back to the White Vault.
QUEST_LOG_CLEANSING_VAULT_RETURN_FINAL_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Cleansing the Vault final hand-in|Return to Sacristan Oryn.
QUEST_LOG_CLEANSING_VAULT_RETURN_FINAL_DETAIL||quest log detail for Cleansing the Vault final hand-in|The lower Moonwell rite answered, and the White Vault's pressure broke from far away. Oryn should know the chamber has settled.
QUEST_LOG_BITTER_STOCK_RETURN_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Bitter Stock Return|Return to Apothecary Maveth in Highmark.
QUEST_LOG_BITTER_STOCK_RETURN_DETAIL||quest log detail for Bitter Stock Return|The oldroot leaves are ready. Return to Apothecary Maveth in Highmark.
QUEST_LOG_BITTER_STOCK_RETURN_WIDOWRUN_DETAIL||quest log detail after completing the Widowrun ingredient set|The Widowrun venom glands are ready. Return to Apothecary Maveth in Highmark.
QUEST_LOG_BITTER_STOCK_OBJECTIVE_COUNT||quest log objective for Bitter Stock progress, placeholder 0 oldroot leaf count|Gather oldroot leaves. ({0}/6)
QUEST_LOG_BITTER_STOCK_DETAIL||quest log detail for Bitter Stock|Oldroot Temple, in the forest near Highmark, yields leaves that strengthen the stock. Bring six to Apothecary Maveth in Highmark.
QUEST_LOG_BITTER_STOCK_WIDOWRUN_OBJECTIVE_COUNT||quest log objective after the Widowrun ingredient is locked, placeholder 0 venom gland count|Gather Widowrun venom glands. ({0}/6)
QUEST_LOG_BITTER_STOCK_WIDOWRUN_DETAIL||quest log detail after the Widowrun ingredient is locked|The spiders in Widowrun Cave carry venom Maveth can cut into medicine. Bring six intact glands to Highmark.
QUEST_LOG_BITTER_STOCK_EITHER_OBJECTIVE_COUNT||quest log objective before either Bitter Stock ingredient is complete, placeholders 0 leaf count and 1 gland count|Gather oldroot leaves or venom glands. ({0}/6 leaves; {1}/6 glands)
QUEST_LOG_BITTER_STOCK_EITHER_DETAIL||quest log detail before either Bitter Stock ingredient is complete|Maveth can use six dark leaves from Oldroot Temple or six intact venom glands from Widowrun Cave. Both lie near Highmark.
QUEST_LOG_MOONWELL_THREAD_RETURN_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Moonwell Thread Return|Return to Bowyer Aelrion in Telwynd.
QUEST_LOG_MOONWELL_THREAD_RETURN_DETAIL||quest log detail for Moonwell Thread Return|I found enough moonwell thread for Aelrion. He should be at his bowyer rack in Telwynd.
QUEST_LOG_MOONWELL_THREAD_OBJECTIVE_COUNT||quest log objective for Moonwell Thread progress, placeholder 0 moonwell thread count|Find moonwell threads for Aelrion. Found: {0}.
QUEST_LOG_MOONWELL_THREAD_DETAIL||quest log detail for Moonwell Thread|Aelrion says Moonwell Observatory catches pale thread near the old frame, and cult dead or specter rooms sometimes carry strands away. Six strands will let him string a stronger bow.
QUEST_LOG_PERFECT_DRAUGHT_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Perfect Draught, placeholder 0 monster type|Preserve a {0} corpse for Nerrik.
QUEST_LOG_PERFECT_DRAUGHT_DETAIL||quest log detail for Perfect Draught, placeholders 0 current sample, 1 total samples, 2 monster type|Sample {0} of {1}: Nerrik wants a preserved {2} corpse. I should use preservation ointment on a fresh corpse, or throw a jar at the monster before killing it.
QUEST_LOG_PERFECT_DRAUGHT_RETURN_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Perfect Draught when carrying target corpse|Bring the preserved corpse to Nerrik.
QUEST_LOG_PERFECT_DRAUGHT_RETURN_DETAIL||quest log detail for Perfect Draught when carrying target corpse, placeholders 0 monster type, 1 current sample, 2 total samples|Sample {1} of {2}: I have the preserved {0} corpse. I should bring it back to Nerrik in Highmark.
QUEST_LOG_PERFECT_DRAUGHT_FINAL_RETURN_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Perfect Draught VII when materials are ready|Bring the dragon sample and shard to Nerrik.
QUEST_LOG_PERFECT_DRAUGHT_FINAL_RETURN_DETAIL||quest log detail for Perfect Draught VII when materials are ready|I have a preserved adult dragon corpse and a blackglass shard. Nerrik can finish the perfect draught in Highmark.
QUEST_LOG_PERFECT_DRAUGHT_FINAL_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Perfect Draught VII|Bring Nerrik a preserved adult dragon corpse and a blackglass shard.
QUEST_LOG_PERFECT_DRAUGHT_FINAL_DETAIL||quest log detail for Perfect Draught VII|Nerrik's final draught needs a preserved corpse from an adult dragon or older, plus one blackglass shard to hold the mixture steady. Young dragons do not count.
QUEST_LOG_ORDERS_FOR_KESTREL_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Orders For Kestrel|Carry the message to the commander at Camp Kestrel.
QUEST_LOG_ORDERS_FOR_KESTREL_DETAIL||quest log detail for Orders For Kestrel|A Silver Lancer says Camp Kestrel needs to know which west roads are open. I should carry the message to the camp and put it in the commander's hand.
QUEST_LOG_NORTHERN_WATCH_I_OBJECTIVE_COUNT||quest log objective for Northern Watch I, placeholder 0 harpy kill count|Clear harpies from the northern hills. ({0}/12)
QUEST_LOG_NORTHERN_WATCH_I_DETAIL||quest log detail for Northern Watch I|Harpies are hitting Greycliff Quarry west of Highmark and the cliff routes toward Telwynd. Clear enough of them for the Silver Lancer.
QUEST_LOG_NORTHERN_WATCH_I_RETURN_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Northern Watch I turn-in|Return to the Silver Lancer in Highmark.
QUEST_LOG_NORTHERN_WATCH_I_RETURN_DETAIL||quest log detail for Northern Watch I turn-in|Harpy kills. The northern hills are thinner for it. Return to the Silver Lancer in Highmark.
QUEST_LOG_NORTHERN_WATCH_II_OBJECTIVE_COUNT||quest log objective for Northern Watch II, placeholder 0 ogre kill count|Clear ogres from the northern ground. ({0}/8)
QUEST_LOG_NORTHERN_WATCH_II_DETAIL||quest log detail for Northern Watch II|Ogres hold the northern ground. Bring eight kills to the Silver Lancer in Highmark.
QUEST_LOG_NORTHERN_WATCH_II_RETURN_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Northern Watch II turn-in|Return to the Silver Lancer in Highmark.
QUEST_LOG_NORTHERN_WATCH_II_RETURN_DETAIL||quest log detail for Northern Watch II turn-in|Ogre kills. The northern ground is steadier for it. Return to the Silver Lancer in Highmark.
QUEST_LOG_NORTHERN_WATCH_III_OBJECTIVE_COUNT||quest log objective for Northern Watch III, placeholder 0 hill giant kill count|Clear hill giants from the north. ({0}/2)
QUEST_LOG_NORTHERN_WATCH_III_DETAIL||quest log detail for Northern Watch III|Hill giants hold the north. Bring two kills to the Silver Lancer in Highmark.
QUEST_LOG_NORTHERN_WATCH_III_RETURN_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Northern Watch III turn-in|Return to the Silver Lancer in Highmark.
QUEST_LOG_NORTHERN_WATCH_III_RETURN_DETAIL||quest log detail for Northern Watch III turn-in|Giants down. The northern watch is complete. Return to the Silver Lancer in Highmark.
QUEST_LOG_RAT_CELLAR_RETURN_TITLE||quest log title for Rat Cellar Return|Clear the Rat Cellar
QUEST_LOG_RAT_CELLAR_RETURN_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Rat Cellar Return|Return to Fisherman Bress.
QUEST_LOG_RAT_CELLAR_RETURN_DETAIL||quest log detail for Rat Cellar Return|Big one's down. The nest is broken. Return to Fisherman Bress.
QUEST_LOG_RAT_CELLAR_TITLE||quest log title for Rat Cellar|Clear the Rat Cellar
QUEST_LOG_RAT_CELLAR_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Rat Cellar|Clear the Rat Cellar.
QUEST_LOG_RAT_CELLAR_DETAIL||quest log detail for Rat Cellar|Fisherman Bress says rats have taken over the cellar and a bigger one is running the nest. I should clear the cellar before it spreads into the docks.
QUEST_LOG_SMUGGLER_BADGE_RETURN_TITLE||quest log title for Smuggler Badge Return|Smuggler's Debt I
QUEST_LOG_SMUGGLER_BADGE_RETURN_OBJECTIVE_PLACE||quest log objective for found smuggler seal, placeholder 0 smuggler location phrase|Return the lead seal to the Smuggler {0}.
QUEST_LOG_SMUGGLER_BADGE_RETURN_DETAIL_PLACE||quest log detail for found smuggler seal, placeholder 0 smuggler location phrase|The lead seal is in hand. I should return it to the Smuggler {0} and collect the first pay before asking about the larger job.
QUEST_LOG_SMUGGLER_BADGE_TITLE||quest log title for Smuggler Badge|Smuggler's Debt I
QUEST_LOG_SMUGGLER_BADGE_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Smuggler Badge|Find the Smuggler's lead seal in Smuggler Grotto.
QUEST_LOG_SMUGGLER_BADGE_DETAIL||quest log detail for Smuggler Badge|The Smuggler said his old crew is using Smuggler Grotto for wet storage. He told me to take the east road toward King's Barrow, turn south to the grotto, and bring back his lead seal whole.
QUEST_LOG_SMUGGLER_DEBT_II_RETURN_TITLE||quest log title for Smuggler Debt Ii Return|Smuggler's Debt II
QUEST_LOG_SMUGGLER_DEBT_II_RETURN_OBJECTIVE_PLACE||quest log objective for found smuggler lockbox, placeholder 0 smuggler location phrase|Return the shut lockbox to the Smuggler {0}.
QUEST_LOG_SMUGGLER_DEBT_II_RETURN_DETAIL_PLACE||quest log detail for found smuggler lockbox, placeholder 0 smuggler location phrase|The Smuggler's iron lockbox is in hand and still shut. I should return it to the Smuggler {0} for the promised pay.
QUEST_LOG_SMUGGLER_DEBT_II_RECOVER_LOCKBOX_TITLE||quest log title for Smuggler Debt Ii Recover Lockbox|Smuggler's Debt II
QUEST_LOG_SMUGGLER_DEBT_II_RECOVER_LOCKBOX_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Smuggler Debt Ii Recover Lockbox|Recover the Smuggler's lockbox from the hidden lower cove.
QUEST_LOG_SMUGGLER_DEBT_II_RECOVER_LOCKBOX_DETAIL||quest log detail for Smuggler Debt Ii Recover Lockbox|The hidden lower cove is clear enough to search now, but the Smuggler's iron lockbox still needs to be found and returned shut.
QUEST_LOG_SMUGGLER_DEBT_II_TITLE||quest log title for Smuggler Debt Ii|Smuggler's Debt II
QUEST_LOG_SMUGGLER_DEBT_II_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Smuggler Debt Ii|Find the hidden stair by the pond outside Smuggler Grotto, then recover the lockbox.
QUEST_LOG_SMUGGLER_DEBT_II_DETAIL||quest log detail for Smuggler Debt Ii|After I returned the seal, the Smuggler said the grotto has a hidden lower floor. He said to search around the pond outside for a concealed stair down to the lower cove, then bring his iron lockbox back shut.
QUEST_LOG_SMUGGLER_DEBT_III_RETURN_TITLE||quest log title for Smuggler Debt Iii return|Smuggler's Debt III
QUEST_LOG_SMUGGLER_DEBT_III_RETURN_OBJECTIVE_PLACE||quest log objective after Dorun Varr is slain, placeholder 0 smuggler location phrase|Return to the Smuggler {0}.
QUEST_LOG_SMUGGLER_DEBT_III_RETURN_DETAIL_PLACE||quest log detail after Dorun Varr is slain, placeholder 0 smuggler location phrase|Dorun Varr is dead. I should return to the Smuggler {0} and collect the promised reward.
QUEST_LOG_SMUGGLER_DEBT_III_TITLE||quest log title for Smuggler Debt Iii|Smuggler's Debt III
QUEST_LOG_SMUGGLER_DEBT_III_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Smuggler Debt Iii|Kill Dorun Varr at Bandit Toll Camp.
QUEST_LOG_SMUGGLER_DEBT_III_DETAIL||quest log detail for Smuggler Debt Iii|The Smuggler said Dorun Varr crossed him and now runs Bandit Toll Camp. He wants Dorun dead.
QUEST_LOG_HAVENFORD_MINES_RETURN_TITLE||quest log title for Havenford Mines return|Havenford Mines
QUEST_LOG_HAVENFORD_MINES_RETURN_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Havenford Mines return|Return to Brannoc in Havenford.
QUEST_LOG_HAVENFORD_MINES_RETURN_DETAIL||quest log detail for Havenford Mines return|The huge boulders are broken. Brannoc can reopen the ore route and improve his forge stock.
QUEST_LOG_HAVENFORD_MINES_TITLE||quest log title for Havenford Mines|Havenford Mines
QUEST_LOG_HAVENFORD_MINES_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Havenford Mines|Break the huge boulders in Havenford Mines.
QUEST_LOG_HAVENFORD_MINES_DETAIL||quest log detail for Havenford Mines|Brannoc needs the lower mine stairs opened so ore carts can move again. Havenford Mines lies in the mountains east of Havenford.
QUEST_LOG_BURNED_COTTAGE_INVESTIGATION_RETURN_TITLE||quest log title for Burned Cottage Investigation return|Investigate the Burned Cottage
QUEST_LOG_BURNED_COTTAGE_INVESTIGATION_RETURN_OBJECTIVE_PLACE||quest log objective after inspecting the Burned Cottage altar, placeholder 0 Vethrin location phrase|Return to Vethrin {0}.
QUEST_LOG_BURNED_COTTAGE_INVESTIGATION_RETURN_DETAIL_PLACE||quest log detail after inspecting the Burned Cottage altar, placeholder 0 Vethrin location phrase|The hidden altar below the Burned Cottage is marked with water glyphs and uneven shallow pools. Return to Vethrin {0}.
QUEST_LOG_BURNED_COTTAGE_INVESTIGATION_TITLE||quest log title for Burned Cottage Investigation|Investigate the Burned Cottage
QUEST_LOG_BURNED_COTTAGE_INVESTIGATION_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Burned Cottage Investigation|Search the Burned Cottage for the source of the strange fire.
QUEST_LOG_BURNED_COTTAGE_INVESTIGATION_DETAIL||quest log detail for Burned Cottage Investigation|Vethrin suspects the cottage in the small forest just out of town burned under magical fire, and the wolves around the ruin are not acting normal. I should search the place carefully for a sign of what happened.
QUEST_LOG_REEDMIRE_DELIVERY_RETURN_TITLE||quest log title for Reedmire Delivery Return|Investigate Reedmire Shrine
QUEST_LOG_REEDMIRE_DELIVERY_RETURN_OBJECTIVE_PLACE||quest log objective after Nhalor is slain, placeholder 0 Vethrin location phrase|Return to Vethrin {0}.
QUEST_LOG_REEDMIRE_DELIVERY_RETURN_DETAIL_PLACE||quest log detail after Nhalor is slain, placeholder 0 Vethrin location phrase|Nhalor is down. Return to Vethrin {0}.
QUEST_LOG_REEDMIRE_DELIVERY_KILL_NHALOR_TITLE||quest log title for Reedmire Delivery Kill Nhalor|Investigate Reedmire Shrine
QUEST_LOG_REEDMIRE_DELIVERY_KILL_NHALOR_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Reedmire Delivery Kill Nhalor|Kill Nhalor at Reedmire Shrine.
QUEST_LOG_REEDMIRE_DELIVERY_KILL_NHALOR_DETAIL||quest log detail for Reedmire Delivery Kill Nhalor|Reth's stones are set at Reedmire Shrine, and Nhalor walks the water there. I should end it and return the news to Vethrin.
QUEST_LOG_REEDMIRE_DELIVERY_PLACE_STONES_TITLE||quest log title for Reedmire Delivery Place Stones|Investigate Reedmire Shrine
QUEST_LOG_REEDMIRE_DELIVERY_PLACE_STONES_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Reedmire Delivery Place Stones|Place Reth's stones on the four Reedmire Shrine stacks.
QUEST_LOG_REEDMIRE_DELIVERY_PLACE_STONES_DETAIL_COUNT||quest log detail for Reedmire stone placement, placeholder 0 placed stone count|Reth said Reedmire Shrine is southeast off the road. I need to set one smooth stone on each of the four stacks. {0} placed.
QUEST_LOG_REEDMIRE_DELIVERY_DELIVER_NOTE_TITLE||quest log title for Reedmire Delivery Deliver Note|Carry Vethrin's Note
QUEST_LOG_REEDMIRE_DELIVERY_DELIVER_NOTE_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Reedmire Delivery Deliver Note|Deliver Vethrin's sealed note to Reth Oskel at Reedwater Docks.
QUEST_LOG_REEDMIRE_DELIVERY_DELIVER_NOTE_DETAIL||quest log detail for Reedmire Delivery Deliver Note|Vethrin gave me a sealed note for Reth Oskel at Reedwater Docks. Reth took stones from Reedmire Shrine and saw the water move. I should deliver the note and ask how to reach the shrine.
QUEST_LOG_REEDMIRE_DELIVERY_REPLACE_NOTE_TITLE||quest log title for Reedmire Delivery Replace Note|Carry Vethrin's Note
QUEST_LOG_REEDMIRE_DELIVERY_REPLACE_NOTE_OBJECTIVE_PLACE||quest log objective for missing Vethrin note, placeholder 0 Vethrin location phrase|Return to Vethrin {0} for the note.
QUEST_LOG_REEDMIRE_DELIVERY_REPLACE_NOTE_DETAIL||quest log detail for Reedmire Delivery Replace Note|The sealed note for Reth Oskel is missing from my pack. Vethrin can write another copy if I return before Reedwater.
QUEST_LOG_STONECLEFT_RUNEFORGE_I_RETURN_CORE_TITLE||quest log title for Stonecleft Runeforge I Return Core|Stonecleft Runeforge I
QUEST_LOG_STONECLEFT_RUNEFORGE_I_RETURN_CORE_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Stonecleft Runeforge I Return Core|Return the Runeforge Core to Stonecleft.
QUEST_LOG_STONECLEFT_RUNEFORGE_I_RETURN_CORE_DETAIL||quest log detail for Stonecleft Runeforge I Return Core|The Runeforge Core was found near dead duergar in Floodgate Cistern. Stonecleft needs it before the runeforge can work blackglass.
QUEST_LOG_STONECLEFT_RUNEFORGE_I_RECOVER_CORE_TITLE||quest log title for Stonecleft Runeforge I Recover Core|Stonecleft Runeforge I
QUEST_LOG_STONECLEFT_RUNEFORGE_I_RECOVER_CORE_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Stonecleft Runeforge I Recover Core|Recover the Runeforge Core, then return it to Stonecleft.
QUEST_LOG_STONECLEFT_RUNEFORGE_I_RECOVER_CORE_DETAIL||quest log detail for Stonecleft Runeforge I Recover Core|I found the Runeforge Core in Floodgate Cistern, but it is no longer in my pack. The runeforge cannot restart until the core is back in Stonecleft.
QUEST_LOG_STONECLEFT_RUNEFORGE_I_SEARCH_CORPSE_TITLE||quest log title for Stonecleft Runeforge I Search Corpse|Stonecleft Runeforge I
QUEST_LOG_STONECLEFT_RUNEFORGE_I_SEARCH_CORPSE_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Stonecleft Runeforge I Search Corpse|Recover the Runeforge Core near the dead duergar in Floodgate Cistern.
QUEST_LOG_STONECLEFT_RUNEFORGE_I_SEARCH_CORPSE_DETAIL||quest log detail for Stonecleft Runeforge I Search Corpse|Dead duergar lie near the lower stairs with crude tools and fresh scrape marks around the sluice. If the missing core is still there, it should be near their bodies.
QUEST_LOG_STONECLEFT_RUNEFORGE_I_TITLE||quest log title for Stonecleft Runeforge I|Stonecleft Runeforge I
QUEST_LOG_STONECLEFT_RUNEFORGE_I_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Stonecleft Runeforge I|Investigate Floodgate Cistern's lower floors with the runed valve handle.
QUEST_LOG_STONECLEFT_RUNEFORGE_I_DETAIL||quest log detail for Stonecleft Runeforge I|Floodgate Cistern is Dorran's best clue to the runeforge failure. It lies just off the southern road, and the runed valve handle fits the sealed lower sluice.
QUEST_LOG_STONECLEFT_RUNEFORGE_I_REPAIRING_TITLE||quest log title for Stonecleft Runeforge I Repairing|Stonecleft Runeforge I
QUEST_LOG_STONECLEFT_RUNEFORGE_I_REPAIRING_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Stonecleft Runeforge I Repairing|Wait for Master Smith Throkk to restart the runeforge.
QUEST_LOG_STONECLEFT_RUNEFORGE_I_REPAIRING_DETAIL_HOURS||legacy quest log detail while runeforge repairs, placeholder 0 time phrase|The runeforge repairs will take about {0}.
QUEST_LOG_STONECLEFT_RUNEFORGE_II_RETURN_TITLE||quest log title for Stonecleft Runeforge Ii Return|Deadrock Mineworks
QUEST_LOG_STONECLEFT_RUNEFORGE_II_RETURN_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Stonecleft Runeforge Ii Return|Return to Armorer Dorran in Stonecleft.
QUEST_LOG_STONECLEFT_RUNEFORGE_II_RETURN_DETAIL||quest log detail for Stonecleft Runeforge Ii Return|Vargrom is dead in Deadrock Mineworks. Dorran promised pay for killing him.
QUEST_LOG_STONECLEFT_RUNEFORGE_II_TITLE||quest log title for Stonecleft Runeforge Ii|Deadrock Mineworks
QUEST_LOG_STONECLEFT_RUNEFORGE_II_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Stonecleft Runeforge Ii|Kill Vargrom, the Blackglass Duergar Captain, in Deadrock Mineworks.
QUEST_LOG_STONECLEFT_RUNEFORGE_II_DETAIL||quest log detail for Stonecleft Runeforge Ii|Dorran says Vargrom, the duergar captain, holds Deadrock Mineworks in the hills far southeast of Traveller's Rest. He will pay for Vargrom's death.
QUEST_LOG_STONECLEFT_LAMP_RUN_TITLE||quest log title for Stonecleft Lamp Run|Lamp Run
QUEST_LOG_STONECLEFT_LAMP_RUN_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Stonecleft Lamp Run|Bring 10 rations and 10 oil flasks to Harl Brack in Stonecleft Gatehall.
QUEST_LOG_STONECLEFT_LAMP_RUN_DETAIL_LOAD||quest log detail for Lamp Run carried supplies, placeholders 0 rations count, 1 oil flask count|Sellan asked me to supply the gatehall lower lamp posts. I have {0} rations and {1} oil flasks; Harl Brack needs ten of each.
QUEST_LOG_THIRSTY_FISHERMAN_I_TITLE||quest log title for Thirsty Fisherman I|Beer for Bran
QUEST_LOG_THIRSTY_FISHERMAN_I_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Thirsty Fisherman I|Bring a beer to Fisherman Bran at Reedwater Docks.
QUEST_LOG_THIRSTY_FISHERMAN_I_DETAIL||quest log detail for Thirsty Fisherman I|Fisherman Bran is stuck at Reedwater Docks with torn nets and no free hands. Any tavern beer will do; I should bring him one before the tide changes.
QUEST_LOG_THIRSTY_FISHERMAN_II_RETURN_TITLE||quest log title for Thirsty Fisherman Ii Return|Bran's Parcel
QUEST_LOG_THIRSTY_FISHERMAN_II_RETURN_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Thirsty Fisherman Ii Return|Deliver Fisherman Bran's parcel to Shopkeeper Orrick at Traveller's Rest.
QUEST_LOG_THIRSTY_FISHERMAN_II_RETURN_DETAIL||quest log detail for Thirsty Fisherman Ii Return|Bran gave me a waxed parcel for Shopkeeper Orrick at Traveller's Rest, far northeast along the inland road. He said the cord holds and the parcel should stay dry. I should put it in Orrick's hand and collect the delivery pay.
QUEST_LOG_THIRSTY_FISHERMAN_II_REPLACE_PARCEL_TITLE||quest log title for Thirsty Fisherman Ii Replace Parcel|Bran's Parcel
QUEST_LOG_THIRSTY_FISHERMAN_II_REPLACE_PARCEL_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Thirsty Fisherman Ii Replace Parcel|Return to Fisherman Bran at Reedwater Docks for another parcel.
QUEST_LOG_THIRSTY_FISHERMAN_II_REPLACE_PARCEL_DETAIL||quest log detail for Thirsty Fisherman Ii Replace Parcel|The parcel for Shopkeeper Orrick is missing from my pack. Bran can tie another one if I return to Reedwater.
QUEST_LOG_TRAVELLERS_REST_OLD_CAVE_RETURN_TITLE||quest log title for Travellers Rest Old Cave Return|Check the Old Cave
QUEST_LOG_TRAVELLERS_REST_OLD_CAVE_RETURN_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Travellers Rest Old Cave Return|Return to Shopkeeper Orrick at Traveller's Rest.
QUEST_LOG_TRAVELLERS_REST_OLD_CAVE_RETURN_DETAIL||quest log detail for Travellers Rest Old Cave Return|I explored Old Cave for Shopkeeper Orrick and reached the bottom. It looks like there was no hidden secret down there, just an old cave with old trouble in it. I should return to Traveller's Rest.
QUEST_LOG_TRAVELLERS_REST_OLD_CAVE_TITLE||quest log title for Travellers Rest Old Cave|Check the Old Cave
QUEST_LOG_TRAVELLERS_REST_OLD_CAVE_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Travellers Rest Old Cave|Reach the bottom floor of Old Cave.
QUEST_LOG_TRAVELLERS_REST_OLD_CAVE_DETAIL||quest log detail for Travellers Rest Old Cave|Shopkeeper Orrick at Traveller's Rest pays for first-hand cave warnings that help travelers stay alive. He wants a fresh look at Old Cave east of the inn. I need to reach the bottom, look around, and return alive.
QUEST_LOG_TRAVELLERS_REST_OLD_CAVE_SPIDER_TITLE||quest log title for Travellers Rest Old Cave Spider Nest|Clear the Old Cave Nest
QUEST_LOG_TRAVELLERS_REST_OLD_CAVE_SPIDER_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Travellers Rest Old Cave Spider Nest|Find and kill the spider nesting in Old Cave.
QUEST_LOG_TRAVELLERS_REST_OLD_CAVE_SPIDER_DETAIL||quest log detail for Travellers Rest Old Cave Spider Nest|Shopkeeper Orrick says travelers near Old Cave have found webs in their packs and bites on their mules. I need to descend into Old Cave, find the spider responsible, and kill it.
QUEST_LOG_TRAVELLERS_REST_OLD_CAVE_SPIDER_RETURN_TITLE||quest log title after killing Needlelegs|Clear the Old Cave Nest
QUEST_LOG_TRAVELLERS_REST_OLD_CAVE_SPIDER_RETURN_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective after killing Needlelegs|Return to Shopkeeper Orrick at Traveller's Rest.
QUEST_LOG_TRAVELLERS_REST_OLD_CAVE_SPIDER_RETURN_DETAIL||quest log detail after killing Needlelegs|I killed Needlelegs in the webbed depths of Old Cave. I should return to Shopkeeper Orrick at Traveller's Rest.
QUEST_LOG_TRAVELLERS_REST_DESOLATE_DOCKS_RETURN_TITLE||quest log title for Travellers Rest Desolate Docks Return|Clear the Desolate Docks
QUEST_LOG_TRAVELLERS_REST_DESOLATE_DOCKS_RETURN_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Travellers Rest Desolate Docks Return|Return to Ser Caldus at Traveller's Rest.
QUEST_LOG_TRAVELLERS_REST_DESOLATE_DOCKS_RETURN_DETAIL||quest log detail for Travellers Rest Desolate Docks Return|Krosh is dead at the Desolate Docks. Ser Caldus is waiting at Traveller's Rest. I should return to him and collect the promised pay.
QUEST_LOG_TRAVELLERS_REST_DESOLATE_DOCKS_TITLE||quest log title for Travellers Rest Desolate Docks|Clear the Desolate Docks
QUEST_LOG_TRAVELLERS_REST_DESOLATE_DOCKS_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Travellers Rest Desolate Docks|Kill Krosh, the Orc Warrior, at the Desolate Docks.
QUEST_LOG_TRAVELLERS_REST_DESOLATE_DOCKS_DETAIL||quest log detail for Travellers Rest Desolate Docks|Ser Caldus wants Krosh dead at the Desolate Docks, on the peninsula northeast of Traveller's Rest. The ruined dock settlement has orc salvage crews in the occupied basements. I need to find Krosh, kill him, and return.
QUEST_LOG_ORC_FORTRESS_OBJECTIVE||Orc campaign Fortress objective before either goal is complete|Kill Gorvuk and free the captive dwarf in the Orc Fortress.
QUEST_LOG_ORC_FORTRESS_DETAIL||Orc campaign Fortress detail before either goal is complete|Krosh carried orders from the Orc Fortress west of Stonecleft. Gorvuk commands the warband, and a Stonecleft dwarf is held somewhere inside. I need to kill Gorvuk and bring the prisoner out alive.
QUEST_LOG_ORC_FORTRESS_RESCUE_OBJECTIVE||Orc campaign Fortress objective after Gorvuk dies|Find and free the captive dwarf in the Orc Fortress.
QUEST_LOG_ORC_FORTRESS_RESCUE_DETAIL||Orc campaign Fortress detail after Gorvuk dies|Gorvuk is dead, but the captive dwarf is still somewhere in the fortress. I need to find him before I leave.
QUEST_LOG_ORC_FORTRESS_KILL_OBJECTIVE||Orc campaign Fortress objective after Borri is freed|Kill Gorvuk in the Orc Fortress.
QUEST_LOG_ORC_FORTRESS_KILL_DETAIL||Orc campaign Fortress detail after Borri is freed|Borri is making his way back to Stonecleft. Gorvuk still commands the fortress and must die.
QUEST_LOG_ORC_FORTRESS_REPORT_OBJECTIVE||Orc campaign Fortress objective after both goals|Report what happened at the Orc Fortress.
QUEST_LOG_ORC_FORTRESS_REPORT_DETAIL||Orc campaign Fortress detail before the route-selecting report|Gorvuk is dead and Borri is free. I should see Borri in Stonecleft, or tell Caldus at Traveller's Rest what became of the fortress.
QUEST_LOG_ORC_WARRENS_OBJECTIVE||Borri-route Orc Warrens objective|Kill the orc chief in the Orc Warrens.
QUEST_LOG_ORC_WARRENS_DETAIL||Borri-route Orc Warrens detail|Borri found the survivors' trail into cramped warrens farther north. I need to find their chief and break the last warband.
QUEST_LOG_ORC_WARRENS_RETURN_OBJECTIVE||Borri-route Orc Warrens return objective|Return to Borri in Stonecleft.
QUEST_LOG_ORC_WARRENS_RETURN_DETAIL||Borri-route Orc Warrens return detail|The chief of the Orc Warrens is dead. Borri will want to know the northern warband is finished.
QUEST_LOG_ORC_WAR_CAMP_OBJECTIVE||Caldus-route Orc War Camp objective|Kill the orc chief in the Orc War Camp.
QUEST_LOG_ORC_WAR_CAMP_DETAIL||Caldus-route Orc War Camp detail|The fortress survivors are gathering at a war camp farther north, in the open country. I need to kill their chief before the scattered bands unite.
QUEST_LOG_ORC_WAR_CAMP_RETURN_OBJECTIVE||Caldus-route Orc War Camp return objective|Return to Ser Caldus at Traveller's Rest.
QUEST_LOG_ORC_WAR_CAMP_RETURN_DETAIL||Caldus-route Orc War Camp return detail|The chief of the Orc War Camp is dead. I should return to Ser Caldus at Traveller's Rest for the rest of the road pay.
QUEST_LOG_TRAVELLERS_REST_ASH_TOWER_RETURN_SCALE_TITLE||quest log title for Travellers Rest Ash Tower Return Scale|Ash Tower Commission
QUEST_LOG_TRAVELLERS_REST_ASH_TOWER_RETURN_SCALE_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Travellers Rest Ash Tower Return Scale|Return to Peddler Velra at Traveller's Rest with a drake scale.
QUEST_LOG_TRAVELLERS_REST_ASH_TOWER_RETURN_SCALE_DETAIL||quest log detail for Travellers Rest Ash Tower Return Scale|Rhazvek is dead, and I have a drake scale for Velra's ring work. She said the scale carries the heat she needs to finish the commission.
QUEST_LOG_TRAVELLERS_REST_ASH_TOWER_RECOVER_SCALE_TITLE||quest log title for Travellers Rest Ash Tower Recover Scale|Ash Tower Commission
QUEST_LOG_TRAVELLERS_REST_ASH_TOWER_RECOVER_SCALE_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Travellers Rest Ash Tower Recover Scale|Recover a drake scale for Peddler Velra.
QUEST_LOG_TRAVELLERS_REST_ASH_TOWER_RECOVER_SCALE_DETAIL||quest log detail for Travellers Rest Ash Tower Recover Scale|Rhazvek is dead, but Velra still needs one drake scale to finish the Ashen Ring. I should search Ash Tower, east-southeast of Traveller's Rest, where he fell.
QUEST_LOG_TRAVELLERS_REST_ASH_TOWER_TITLE||quest log title for Travellers Rest Ash Tower|Ash Tower Commission
QUEST_LOG_TRAVELLERS_REST_ASH_TOWER_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Travellers Rest Ash Tower|Kill Rhazvek in Ash Tower and bring Velra a drake scale.
QUEST_LOG_TRAVELLERS_REST_ASH_TOWER_DETAIL||quest log detail for Travellers Rest Ash Tower|Peddler Velra gave me two fire resistance potions and a wand of cone of cold. She needs one drake scale from Rhazvek in Ash Tower, east-southeast of Traveller's Rest, to finish the Ashen Ring.
QUEST_LOG_HAVENFORD_WATCH_I_RETURN_TITLE||quest log title for Havenford Watch I Return|Havenford Watch I
QUEST_LOG_HAVENFORD_WATCH_I_RETURN_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Havenford Watch I Return|Return to Garrick in Havenford.
QUEST_LOG_HAVENFORD_WATCH_I_RETURN_DETAIL||quest log detail for Havenford Watch I Return|I have enough proof from the kobolds for Garrick's first watch job. I should return to Havenford and collect the first watch pay.
QUEST_LOG_HAVENFORD_WATCH_I_TITLE||quest log title for Havenford Watch I|Havenford Watch I
QUEST_LOG_HAVENFORD_WATCH_I_OBJECTIVE_COUNT||quest log objective for Havenford Watch I proof progress, placeholder 0 kobold scalp count|Gather kobold scalps for Garrick. ({0}/20)
QUEST_LOG_HAVENFORD_WATCH_I_DETAIL||quest log detail for Havenford Watch I|Garrick wants twenty kobold scalps before the first watch job is finished. The kobolds steal fodder, cut straps, and draw patrols off the road.
QUEST_LOG_HAVENFORD_WATCH_II_RETURN_TITLE||quest log title for Havenford Watch Ii Return|Havenford Watch II
QUEST_LOG_HAVENFORD_WATCH_II_RETURN_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Havenford Watch Ii Return|Return to Garrick in Havenford.
QUEST_LOG_HAVENFORD_WATCH_II_RETURN_DETAIL||quest log detail for Havenford Watch Ii Return|I have enough grave bones for Garrick's second watch job. I should return to Havenford and collect the next watch pay.
QUEST_LOG_HAVENFORD_WATCH_II_TITLE||quest log title for Havenford Watch Ii|Havenford Watch II
QUEST_LOG_HAVENFORD_WATCH_II_OBJECTIVE_COUNT||quest log objective for Havenford Watch II proof progress, placeholder 0 grave bone count|Gather grave bones for Garrick. ({0}/20)
QUEST_LOG_HAVENFORD_WATCH_II_DETAIL||quest log detail for Havenford Watch Ii|Garrick wants twenty grave bones from skeletons or zombies for the second watch job. The dead are moving strangely along the roads.
QUEST_LOG_HAVENFORD_WATCH_III_RETURN_TITLE||quest log title for Havenford Watch Iii Return|Havenford Watch III
QUEST_LOG_HAVENFORD_WATCH_III_RETURN_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Havenford Watch Iii Return|Return to Garrick in Havenford.
QUEST_LOG_HAVENFORD_WATCH_III_RETURN_DETAIL||quest log detail for Havenford Watch Iii Return|Skrit, the Kobold Packleader, is dead in the mine north of the watchtower. Garrick said this closes the last watch job he can manage from Havenford.
QUEST_LOG_HAVENFORD_WATCH_III_TITLE||quest log title for Havenford Watch Iii|Havenford Watch III
QUEST_LOG_HAVENFORD_WATCH_III_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Havenford Watch Iii|Kill Skrit, the Kobold Packleader, in the mine north of the watchtower.
QUEST_LOG_HAVENFORD_WATCH_III_DETAIL||quest log detail for Havenford Watch Iii|Garrick wants Skrit dead for the last Havenford watch job. Skrit gathers kobolds in the mine north of the ruined watchtower and feeds raids along the west road. I need to reach the bottom, kill him, and return to Havenford.
QUEST_LOG_FIT_FOR_A_KING_I_DELIVER_MANUSCRIPT_TITLE||quest log title for Fit For A King I Deliver Manuscript|Fit for a King I
QUEST_LOG_FIT_FOR_A_KING_I_DELIVER_MANUSCRIPT_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Fit For A King I Deliver Manuscript|Take Pilgrim Edran's manuscript to Theryn Rusk in Havenford.
QUEST_LOG_FIT_FOR_A_KING_I_DELIVER_MANUSCRIPT_DETAIL||quest log detail for Fit For A King I Deliver Manuscript|Pilgrim Edran copied a royal burial phrase tied to King's Barrow. He does not trust his reading of the old March hand. Theryn Rusk in Havenford should be able to read it.
QUEST_LOG_FIT_FOR_A_KING_I_REPLACE_MANUSCRIPT_TITLE||quest log title for Fit For A King I Replace Manuscript|Fit for a King I
QUEST_LOG_FIT_FOR_A_KING_I_REPLACE_MANUSCRIPT_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Fit For A King I Replace Manuscript|Return to Pilgrim Edran in Highmark for another manuscript copy.
QUEST_LOG_FIT_FOR_A_KING_I_REPLACE_MANUSCRIPT_DETAIL||quest log detail for Fit For A King I Replace Manuscript|Edran's barrow manuscript is missing from my pack. He can make another copy from his notes in Highmark.
QUEST_LOG_FIT_FOR_A_KING_II_RETURN_TITLE||quest log title for Fit For A King Ii Return|Fit for a King II
QUEST_LOG_FIT_FOR_A_KING_II_RETURN_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Fit For A King Ii Return|Return to Pilgrim Edran in Highmark.
QUEST_LOG_FIT_FOR_A_KING_II_RETURN_DETAIL||quest log detail for Fit For A King Ii Return|King Halric is dead again, and Kingsmark is out of the royal sarcophagus. Pilgrim Edran wanted the barrow account more than the ring itself.
QUEST_LOG_FIT_FOR_A_KING_II_CLAIM_RING_TITLE||quest log title for Fit For A King Ii Claim Ring|Fit for a King II
QUEST_LOG_FIT_FOR_A_KING_II_CLAIM_RING_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Fit For A King Ii Claim Ring|Open the royal sarcophagus in King's Barrow.
QUEST_LOG_FIT_FOR_A_KING_II_CLAIM_RING_DETAIL||quest log detail for Fit For A King Ii Claim Ring|King Halric, the barrow wight, has fallen. The royal sarcophagus should now answer to the phrase learned from Theryn. Kingsmark is supposed to be buried with the old king.
QUEST_LOG_FIT_FOR_A_KING_II_TITLE||quest log title for Fit For A King Ii|Fit for a King II
QUEST_LOG_FIT_FOR_A_KING_II_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Fit For A King Ii|Enter King's Barrow and defeat King Halric.
QUEST_LOG_FIT_FOR_A_KING_II_DETAIL||quest log detail for Fit For A King Ii|Old Theryn read Pilgrim Edran's manuscript and gave me the royal phrase: Halric holds the road. King's Barrow lies far south beyond the mountains; Lightglass should open the entrance, but Edran warned that it is not an ordinary tomb.
QUEST_LOG_ORC_BASE_I_TITLE||quest log title for Orc Base I|Orc Fortress Sketch
QUEST_LOG_ORC_BASE_I_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Orc Base I|Take the orc fortress sketch to the Stonecleft gate warden.
QUEST_LOG_ORC_BASE_I_DETAIL||quest log detail for Orc Base I|Branna at Traveller's Rest handed over a rough sketch left after the Old Cave trouble. The Stonecleft gate warden can judge whether it shows a real orc fortress.
QUEST_LOG_ORC_BASE_RETURN_TITLE||quest log title for Orc Base Return|Break the Orc Fortress
QUEST_LOG_ORC_BASE_RETURN_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Orc Base Return|Return to the Stonecleft gate warden.
QUEST_LOG_ORC_BASE_RETURN_DETAIL||quest log detail for Orc Base Return|Gorvuk is dead, and the Orc Fortress west of Stonecleft has lost its warboss. The gate warden promised a hammer and coin.
QUEST_LOG_ORC_BASE_TITLE||quest log title for Orc Base|Break the Orc Fortress
QUEST_LOG_ORC_BASE_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Orc Base|Kill Gorvuk, the warboss in the revealed Orc Fortress.
QUEST_LOG_ORC_BASE_DETAIL||quest log detail for Orc Base|The gate warden took the sketch and revealed the Orc Fortress west of Stonecleft, off the rough track southwest of the main road. Gorvuk commands the warband there. I need to get inside, kill him, and return to the warden.
QUEST_LOG_MISSING_HUSBAND_RESCUED_TITLE||quest log title for Missing Husband Rescued|Find the Missing Farmer
QUEST_LOG_MISSING_HUSBAND_RESCUED_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Missing Husband Rescued|Return to Havenford and speak with Farmer Thom.
QUEST_LOG_MISSING_HUSBAND_RESCUED_DETAIL||quest log detail for Missing Husband Rescued|The missing farmer is alive and headed home. Maveth is waiting in Havenford without knowing whether to hope or mourn.
QUEST_LOG_MISSING_HUSBAND_SEARCH_SHRINE_TITLE||quest log title for Missing Husband Search Shrine|Find the Missing Farmer
QUEST_LOG_MISSING_HUSBAND_SEARCH_SHRINE_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Missing Husband Search Shrine|Find Thom or proof of what happened.
QUEST_LOG_MISSING_HUSBAND_SEARCH_SHRINE_DETAIL||quest log detail for Missing Husband Search Shrine|Maveth's husband Thom vanished after following tracks out of Havenford. She does not know where he ended up. Search nearby trouble spots and bring him home, or bring proof of what happened.
QUEST_LOG_MISSING_HUSBAND_SEARCH_GOBLIN_CAVE_TITLE||quest log title for Missing Husband Search Goblin Cave|Find the Missing Farmer
QUEST_LOG_MISSING_HUSBAND_SEARCH_GOBLIN_CAVE_OBJECTIVE||quest log objective for Missing Husband Search Goblin Cave|Find Thom or proof of what happened.
QUEST_LOG_MISSING_HUSBAND_SEARCH_GOBLIN_CAVE_DETAIL||quest log detail for Missing Husband Search Goblin Cave|Maveth's husband Thom vanished after following tracks out of Havenford. She does not know where he ended up. Search nearby trouble spots and bring him home, or bring proof of what happened.
QUEST_LOG_PLACE_AT_TRAVELLERS_REST|32|quest log place phrase for NPCs moved to Traveller's Rest|at Traveller's Rest
QUEST_LOG_PLACE_IN_HAVENFORD|24|quest log place phrase for NPCs still in Havenford|in Havenford
DIALOGUE_THAREC_LIGHTGLASS_SHARD_REFERRAL||High Canon Tharec post-rite true shard referral|That is a pure blackglass shard, not a keepsake. Veydras can set it into the White Seal pattern and make a Lightglass fragment of it. Do not carry it longer than need requires.
DIALOGUE_THAREC_LIGHTGLASS_STAR_BLACKGLASS_LEAD||High Canon Tharec post-vault Blackglass Cavern lead|Your inherited star is Lightglass now: blackglass given law by your blood and our oldest patterns. With this Lightglass and your bloodline, the Scar may be closed. Blackglass Cavern west of Camp Kestrel is the clearest source we can still reach. Go down there and end what is feeding it. If you find blackglass shards, bring them to Veydras; he can judge what the White Seal can make of them.
DIALOGUE_THAREC_FINAL_SEAL_THERYN_LEAD||High Canon Tharec final blood seal Theryn lead|That seal is ancient Istarian work, older than Highmark and older than the Starfall. It answered your blood and Lightglass, so it is no dwarven gate and no White Seal ward I can safely name. Ask Old Theryn Rusk in Havenford. He has spent his life reading pre-Starfall Istarian hands, and he may know what manuscript can make the seal finish its answer.
DIALOGUE_THAREC_FINAL_SEAL_THERYN_REMINDER||High Canon Tharec final blood seal Theryn reminder|Tell Theryn Rusk about the final blood seal below the blackglass descent. It is pre-Starfall Istarian work, and the Lightglass star answered it.
DIALOGUE_THAREC_VAULT_ALREADY_PURIFIED||High Canon Tharec when Lightglass star already exists before vault turn-in|The star is already Lightglass, and that is the proof I needed. Keep it close; the lower seals will know that instrument when the road reaches them.
DIALOGUE_THAREC_WHITE_VAULT_TURNIN||High Canon Tharec White Vault redirect|The vault beast is dead. Good. Oryn can finish the chamber work from here. Your path leads deeper now: Blackglass Cavern west of Camp Kestrel is where the pressure is strongest.
DIALOGUE_THAREC_WHITE_VAULT_REMINDER||High Canon Tharec White Vault reminder|Oryn opened the White Vault stair. If you mean to reclaim that chamber, kill what waits below and return to him.
DIALOGUE_THAREC_BEACON_RETURN_TO_ORYN||High Canon Tharec Beacon Prism hand-in|Set the Beacon Prism here. When it is lit, press your blood to the star. The blackglass takes order: the star is Lightglass now. With that light and your bloodline, the Scar may still be closed. Blackglass Cavern west of Camp Kestrel is the strongest source we can reach; go down and end what is feeding it.
DIALOGUE_ORYN_BEACON_HANDIN||legacy Sacristan Oryn Beacon Prism hand-in redirect|The Beacon Prism belongs with Tharec's rite. Take it to him; my work begins when the lower ward opens.
DIALOGUE_ORYN_BEACON_SET||legacy Sacristan Oryn Beacon Prism setup redirect|Tharec must settle the star before I risk the White Vault stair. Bring the prism to him.
DIALOGUE_ORYN_BEACON_SET_HALF_ORC||legacy Sacristan Oryn Beacon Prism setup redirect half-orc variant|Tharec must settle the star before I risk the White Vault stair. Bring the prism to him.
DIALOGUE_THAREC_BEACON_READY||High Canon Tharec Beacon Prism completed and White Vault prepared|The star is Lightglass now. With that light and your bloodline, the Scar may still be closed. Blackglass Cavern west of Camp Kestrel is the strongest source we can reach; go down and end what is feeding it.
DIALOGUE_THAREC_BEACON_REMINDER||High Canon Tharec Beacon Prism reminder|The Beacon Prism remains in the Tower of the White Seal, far down the east road. Kill the dragon, recover the prism, and bring it back to me.
DIALOGUE_THAREC_BEACON_ORYN_REMINDER||legacy High Canon Tharec reminder to speak with Oryn for Beacon Prism work|The Beacon Prism remains in the Tower of the White Seal, far down the east road. Kill the dragon, recover the prism, and bring it back to me.
DIALOGUE_THAREC_NEEDS_PROOF||High Canon Tharec refuses sealed work without proof|You ask for sealed work on old blood and bare claims. Bring proof I can test, then we will speak.
DIALOGUE_THAREC_BEACON_START||High Canon Tharec first Beacon Prism offer|That heirloom at your throat is not ornament. It is a blackglass star keyed to seal-priest blood. The old Istarian seals were built for bloodlines, and the dragons stirring below are answering that same broken pressure.\nThe Beacon Prism in the Tower of the White Seal can turn blackglass toward Lightglass when it is lit with a living sample. The tower lies far down the east road from Highmark. Kill the dragon there, recover the prism, and bring it back to me.
DIALOGUE_ORYN_BEACON_START||legacy Sacristan Oryn Beacon Prism recovery redirect|Tharec handles the Beacon Prism rite. Recover the prism from the Tower of the White Seal, then bring it back to him.
DIALOGUE_ORYN_BEACON_REMINDER||legacy Sacristan Oryn Beacon Prism recovery reminder|The Beacon Prism belongs with Tharec. Bring it to him when it is recovered.
DIALOGUE_ORYN_CLEANSING_START||Sacristan Oryn starts Cleansing the Vault|The vault beast is dead, but the lower chamber still feels wrong. I drew this tainted crystal from the White Vault before the stair sealed again.\nTake it to Eivyss Glass-Singer in Telwynd. If Telwynd can tune it clean, the lower Moonwell rite may carry that work back here while we make the vault fit for people again.
DIALOGUE_ORYN_CLEANSING_CRYSTAL_MISSING||Sacristan Oryn reminder when the tainted White Vault crystal is missing|The White Vault crystal is not with you. Find it, then take it to Eivyss Glass-Singer in Telwynd.
DIALOGUE_ORYN_CLEANSING_TELWYND_REMINDER||Sacristan Oryn reminder to take the tainted crystal to Eivyss|Take the Tainted White Vault Crystal to Eivyss Glass-Singer in Telwynd. If anyone can tune White Seal glass without cracking it, he can.
DIALOGUE_ORYN_CLEANSING_MOONWELL_REMINDER||Sacristan Oryn reminder to use the lower Moonwell rite|Eivyss tuned the crystal? Then take it below Moonwell Observatory. The lower ritual chamber is old enough to answer this kind of work.
DIALOGUE_ORYN_CLEANSING_COMPLETE_RITE||Sacristan Oryn Cleansing the Vault completion rite page|The vault is quiet. Not empty, never that, but quiet enough that I can trust the stair again.
DIALOGUE_ORYN_CLEANSING_COMPLETE_REWARD||Sacristan Oryn Cleansing the Vault completion reward page|You have done the White Seal a rare service. Take this reward and a Lightglass fragment. Use both with care.
DIALOGUE_VEYDRAS_TOVAN_DONE||Veydras idle after Antiquary Tovan's rescue is complete|Tovan is safe, limping, and already arguing with catalog labels. The purifier line holds.
DIALOGUE_VEYDRAS_TOVAN_RESCUED||Veydras reminder after the Highmark Aqueduct rescue|Tovan made it back from the aqueduct. Collect your reward from him before he decides gratitude needs a receipt.
DIALOGUE_VEYDRAS_TOVAN_RESCUED_LIGHTHOUSE||Veydras reminder after the lighthouse basement rescue|Tovan made it back from the old lighthouse. Collect your reward from him before he decides gratitude needs a receipt.
DIALOGUE_VEYDRAS_TOVAN_REMINDER||Veydras reminder for the Highmark Aqueduct variant|Tovan remains in Highmark Aqueduct, in the hills west of the city. Find him before water, vermin, or his own stubbornness finishes the job.
DIALOGUE_VEYDRAS_TOVAN_REMINDER_LIGHTHOUSE||Veydras reminder for the lighthouse basement variant|Tovan remains beneath the Old Imperial Lighthouse, far southeast beyond Traveller's Rest. Find him before the flooded stones or his own stubbornness finishes the job.
DIALOGUE_VEYDRAS_TOVAN_START||Veydras Lost Purifier offer for the Highmark Aqueduct variant|Antiquary Tovan went into Highmark Aqueduct, in the hills west of the city, to trace an old purifier and did not return. He is careful, not immortal. Find him.
DIALOGUE_VEYDRAS_TOVAN_START_LIGHTHOUSE||Veydras Lost Purifier offer for the lighthouse basement variant|Antiquary Tovan went below the Old Imperial Lighthouse, far southeast beyond Traveller's Rest, to trace an old purifier and did not return. He is careful, not immortal. Find him.
DIALOGUE_VEYDRAS_LIGHTGLASS_LOCKED||Veydras lightglass worktable locked before Tharec unlocks it|Tharec has not signed the table over to you. Lightglass looks orderly until bad handling costs someone fingers. Usually mine.
DIALOGUE_VEYDRAS_LIGHTGLASS_OPEN||Veydras lightglass worktable access|The Lightglass table is open. Bring pure blackglass shards, choose the work you want, and do not improvise where the White Seal wrote numbers.
DIALOGUE_VEYDRAS_MOONWELL_START||Veydras Moonwell Alignment first offer|Moonwell Observatory is drifting again. My readings and the old frame disagree by the same count every time. The lens is wrong.\nTake this misaligned lens to Eivyss Glass-Singer in Telwynd. He can tune it; then seat it in the Moonwell Observatory frame and report back to me.
DIALOGUE_VEYDRAS_MOONWELL_TO_TELWYND||Veydras Moonwell Alignment Telwynd step reminder|Take the lens to Eivyss Glass-Singer in Telwynd. Highmark can cut glass; Telwynd knows how to tune it.
DIALOGUE_VEYDRAS_MOONWELL_TO_OBSERVATORY||Veydras Moonwell Alignment observatory step reminder|Eivyss tuned the lens. Seat it in the Moonwell Observatory frame, then come back with the reading.
DIALOGUE_VEYDRAS_MOONWELL_COMPLETE||Veydras Moonwell Alignment completion|Well done. The observatory frame is steady, and Telwynd's tuning agrees with my numbers.\nTake this purse and this Lightglass fragment. That saves me a climb and an argument at Telwynd's gate.
DIALOGUE_TOVAN_AQUEDUCT_RESCUE||Antiquary Tovan rescue dialogue in Highmark Aqueduct|You came down this far for an old antiquary? Good. My leg is done arguing with the stones; help me back to Highmark before the aqueduct changes its mind.
DIALOGUE_TOVAN_LIGHTHOUSE_RESCUE||Antiquary Tovan rescue dialogue beneath the Old Imperial Lighthouse|You came this far for an old antiquary? Good. My leg is done arguing with these flooded stones; help me back to Highmark before the tide returns.
DIALOGUE_TOVAN_AQUEDUCT_UNAVAILABLE||Antiquary Tovan unavailable during the Highmark Aqueduct variant|White Seal Antiquities remains closed while Tovan is missing in Highmark Aqueduct. Rescue the keeper before browsing his cases.
DIALOGUE_TOVAN_LIGHTHOUSE_UNAVAILABLE||Antiquary Tovan unavailable during the lighthouse basement variant|White Seal Antiquities remains closed while Tovan is missing beneath the Old Imperial Lighthouse. Rescue the keeper before browsing his cases.
DIALOGUE_TOVAN_REWARD||Antiquary Tovan Lost Purifier reward and shop unlock|You got me out with most of my bones in their proper order. Here is the promised pay, and White Seal Antiquities is open to you.
DIALOGUE_TOVAN_SHOP_IDLE||Antiquary Tovan post-quest shop chatter|White Seal Antiquities is open. Look closely, ask before touching, and do not call anything junk where I can hear it.
DIALOGUE_ORYN_VAULT_SEALED||Sacristan Oryn post-quest sealed vault chatter|The White Vault is sealed again, and this time it feels like a seal rather than a prayer.
DIALOGUE_ORYN_VAULT_RITE_DONE||Sacristan Oryn redirect after White Vault rite completion|The star is Lightglass, but something still stirs below. I will not call the vault safe while it breathes.
DIALOGUE_ORYN_VAULT_DRAKE_SLAIN||Sacristan Oryn redirect after the White Vault drake is killed|The vault beast is slain. The chamber is quiet enough that I can hear my own hands shake.
DIALOGUE_ORYN_VAULT_REMINDER||Sacristan Oryn active White Vault reminder|The lower ward is open. I can feel the vault breathing through the stair. End what waits below before the old pattern spends itself holding the door.
DIALOGUE_ORYN_VAULT_NOT_READY||Sacristan Oryn locked stair before Beacon Prism setup|The vault stair remains locked. Until the Beacon Prism is set, opening it would be courage without discipline.
DIALOGUE_ORYN_VAULT_START||Sacristan Oryn White Vault start instructions|The Beacon Prism is set, and the star is Lightglass. I can open the lower ward, but listen before you descend: the White Vault has held something draconic in the dark for too long. If it wakes fully, the stones will not keep the sound small. Return when it is dead.
DIALOGUE_KESTREL_SCOUT_GHOSTWOOD_DONE||Kestrel scout Ghostwood post-quest chatter|West patrols are finding the road again. We keep a double watch, but the names match the roster now.
DIALOGUE_KESTREL_SCOUT_GHOSTWOOD_REWARD||Kestrel scout Ghostwood Smoke quest reward|Veyr is dead? Then the smoke lifting makes sense. We lost patrols to that tower.\nTake the Lancer purse. I will send west patrols that way again.
DIALOGUE_KESTREL_SCOUT_ASK_EIRADHA||Kestrel scout reminder to ask Eiradha about Ghostwood|Before you go west, ask Envoy Eiradha in Highmark. This smoke has old ward work in it, and elves know more of that than we do.
DIALOGUE_KESTREL_SCOUT_GHOSTWOOD_REMINDER||Kestrel scout reminder after Eiradha consultation|Eiradha gave her answer. Ghostwood is next. Follow the west road to the old tower, kill Veyr, and return when the smoke clears.
DIALOGUE_KESTREL_SCOUT_TOO_GREEN||Kestrel scout level-gated Ghostwood warning|Not for you yet. The smoke reports are taking trained patrols, and I am not sending another name into that list today.
DIALOGUE_KESTREL_SCOUT_GHOSTWOOD_START||Kestrel scout Ghostwood Smoke first offer|You there, traveler. If you can keep west on a bad road, I need you. Two patrols vanished near Ghostwood after dusk. We found cold ash, dropped packs, no bodies.\nGo to Highmark and ask Envoy Eiradha about the smoke before you enter it. Kestrel pays when patrols can use the west road again.
DIALOGUE_WATCH_SERGEANT_ROCKMAW_OUTPOST_OPEN||Kestrel Watch Sergeant Rockmaw outpost inspection reminder|Rockmaw's outer yard is ours: beds, crates, field forge, barricaded lower stair.\nGo west to Rockmaw Keep and step into the outer yard. The supplier sells field stock, the smith patches gear, and the aid-station Lancer has cots.
DIALOGUE_WATCH_SERGEANT_ROCKMAW_HOLDING||Kestrel Watch Sergeant post-Rockmaw idle|Rockmaw is holding. Two Lancers on the lower stair, crates under canvas, forge still hot. Better than yesterday's report.
DIALOGUE_WATCH_SERGEANT_ROCKMAW_TURNIN||Kestrel Watch Sergeant Rockmaw leaders turn-in|Maug and Brond are dead? Good. Heads shorten my report; the kills open the road.\nKestrel moves now. We take Rockmaw's outer yard, block the lower stair, and set beds, crates, and a field forge. Take the Rockmaw pay.
DIALOGUE_WATCH_SERGEANT_ROCKMAW_REMINDER||Kestrel Watch Sergeant Rockmaw active reminder|Rockmaw Keep, west road. Kill Maug and Brond. Bring their heads if you can carry them.
DIALOGUE_WATCH_SERGEANT_TOO_GREEN||Kestrel Watch Sergeant level-gated Rockmaw warning|Not yet. The next yard breaks trained pickets. Learn the west road before I put your name on it.
DIALOGUE_WATCH_SERGEANT_ROCKMAW_START||Kestrel Watch Sergeant Rockmaw first offer|You came to Kestrel without a post assignment. Good. I need blades on road work.\nRockmaw Keep blocks the west road. Maug, an ettin, gives orders; Brond, an ogre champion, holds the yard.\nKill both. Bring their heads if you can carry them. When they are down, Kestrel takes the outer yard.
DIALOGUE_WATCH_SERGEANT_VARROTH_REWARD||Kestrel Watch Sergeant Moon-Bitten Cave reward|Varroth is dead? Good. A werewolf king near Rockmaw is too close to my sentries.\nTake the purse and this axe. We pulled it from Rockmaw stores.
DIALOGUE_WATCH_SERGEANT_VARROTH_REMINDER||Kestrel Watch Sergeant Moon-Bitten Cave reminder|Inconspicuous Cave, east of Highmark. Varroth holds the lower stone rooms. Kill him and report back to me at Camp Kestrel.
DIALOGUE_WATCH_SERGEANT_VARROTH_START||Kestrel Watch Sergeant Moon-Bitten Cave first offer|One more job now that Rockmaw holds. A werewolf pack has taken the lower rooms of Inconspicuous Cave, east of Highmark.\nVarroth, the Werewolf King, holds the clean stone below. Kill him and report back; I have coin and an axe from Rockmaw stores.
DIALOGUE_WATCH_SERGEANT_GRUMMOK_REWARD||Kestrel Watch Sergeant Grummok reward|Grummok is dead? Good. A troll king gathering fighters that close to camp was a siege waiting to happen.\nTake the purse and this armor from Rockmaw stores.
DIALOGUE_WATCH_SERGEANT_GRUMMOK_REMINDER||Kestrel Watch Sergeant Grummok reminder|Bloodied Cave, northeast of camp. Grummok holds the deepest chamber. Kill him and report back to me at Camp Kestrel.
DIALOGUE_WATCH_SERGEANT_GRUMMOK_START||Kestrel Watch Sergeant Grummok first offer|One more job now that Rockmaw holds. Trolls are gathering in Bloodied Cave, northeast of camp.\nGrummok calls himself their king. Kill him and report back; I have coin and armor from Rockmaw stores.
DIALOGUE_VAUST_ORDERS_HANDIN||Captain Vaust Orders for Kestrel hand-in|Good. West scouts need current routes, not guesses.\nTell the Lancers I heard the message. Take the carry pay.
DIALOGUE_VAUST_STONEWARD_GATE_BLOCKED||Captain Vaust Stoneward Gate blocked reminder|Dwarven runes below camp? My Lancers can hold a post, not read dwarf gate-craft. Take that to Throkk Flintvein in Stonecleft; if anyone knows old gate-craft, he does.
DIALOGUE_VAUST_NEEDS_WHITE_SEAL||Captain Vaust before White Seal rite completion|Camp Kestrel is not a shelter for unfinished relic work. Finish the White Seal's amulet business with Tharec, then come back.
DIALOGUE_VAUST_LIFT_NOT_READY||Captain Vaust before the Kestrel lift is opened from below|We can brace surface shafts, not open old Istarian roadwork from this side. If Blackglass Cavern drops you into our lift chamber below, secure it; then we can move supplies and wounded through it.
DIALOGUE_VAUST_BREACH_START||Captain Vaust after the Kestrel lift is opened from below|You found our lift chamber from below and got it working. Good. I am Captain Vaust Thane. My Lancers can hold this shortcut now; use it when you need camp, supplies, or a way back under the hill.\nThe old Istarian road keeps going below, and blackglass thickens the farther it runs. If stone, seal, or dragon-blood magic stops you, come back and tell me what stopped you.
DIALOGUE_EIRADHA_GHOSTWOOD_CONSULT||Envoy Eiradha Ghostwood consult for Ghostwood Smoke|The Ghostwood smoke has old ward work in it, not merely rot. Follow it to the tower if it still rises; when it quiets, return to the Kestrel Lancer.
DIALOGUE_EIRADHA_TELWYND_OPEN||Envoy Eiradha after Moonwell Reverie completion|You saw Telwynd through the Moonwell lens? Then you have the only directions that matter. Warden Sairveth Ilyr will receive you now.
DIALOGUE_EIRADHA_GLASSROOT_TURNIN||Envoy Eiradha Moonwell Reverie completion|You saw Telwynd through the Moonwell lens? Good. Then the forest has given you more trust than most strangers earn.\nGo there now. Warden Sairveth Ilyr will receive you.
DIALOGUE_EIRADHA_GLASSROOT_REMINDER||Envoy Eiradha Moonwell Reverie reminder|Glassroot Hollow first. Kill Mordraxis, take back the Moonwell lens, then set it in the frame at Moonwell Observatory. Through the lens you will see Telwynd clearly.
DIALOGUE_EIRADHA_GLASSROOT_START||Envoy Eiradha Moonwell Reverie first offer|Highmark does not usually send armed strangers to my door. Since you are here, I will be plain.\nTelwynd is hidden in the forest north of Moonwell Observatory. From the ground, common travelers do not see it clearly.\nThe observatory can show the town when its lens is in place. Mordraxis dragged that lens into Glassroot Hollow and nested on it like stolen gold.\nKill the drake. Take the lens to the observatory. Set it back in the frame. Through the lens you will see Telwynd clearly.
DIALOGUE_SAIRVETH_GLASSROOT_TURNIN||Sairveth Moonwell Reverie completion|You saw Telwynd from the observatory and still reached our trees. Good. The town can receive you properly.\nKeep to the streets and gardens while you are here. I can help with ordinary wardwork.
DIALOGUE_SAIRVETH_TELWYND_CLOSED||Sairveth Telwynd closed before Moonwell Reverie is complete|Telwynd is closed to guests until the Moonwell lens is back in the observatory. Kill Mordraxis in Glassroot Hollow, set the lens in the frame, then come north from the observatory.
DIALOGUE_SAIRVETH_MOONWELL_TURNIN||Sairveth Moonwell road completion|You opened the far exit? Good. The Moonwell Tunnels can carry wardens again.\nTake the ward pay and this ring. Highmark will have fewer excuses to close the tunnel route.
DIALOGUE_SAIRVETH_MOONWELL_REMINDER||Sairveth Moonwell road reminder|Moonwell Tunnels still need both moonstone dials set. Open the far exit, then return. Until then, I keep it off our patrol map.
DIALOGUE_SAIRVETH_MOONWELL_START||Sairveth Moonwell road first offer|The Moonwell Tunnels run below the high route, from the Moonwell site toward the southwest exit. Highmark leaves them closed; Telwynd needs another way through.\nSet both moonstone dials to open the far exit, then return to me. If you can open the route end to end, I can send wardens after you.
DIALOGUE_SAIRVETH_HIGHWIND_FOUND_CATACOMBS||Sairveth Buried Highwind completion after catacombs found|You found the Highwind Catacombs? Then the lower door still opens.\nTelwynd needed proof, and you brought it. Good work.
DIALOGUE_SAIRVETH_HIGHWIND_ASK_THERYN||Sairveth Buried Highwind after monastery inspection|The chapel wardwork is still sound, and it points below the monastery.\nOld Theryn Rusk knows the Highwind grounds. Ask him where the lower entrance opens.
DIALOGUE_SAIRVETH_HIGHWIND_MONASTERY_REMINDER||Sairveth Buried Highwind monastery reminder|Highwind Monastery first. Inspect the old chapel and return to me before you chase a lower door.
DIALOGUE_SAIRVETH_ELDERWYRM_TURNIN||Sairveth Elderwyrm Grove completion|Caerwyn is dead? Then Elderwyrm Grove can be held again.\nI will open the Telwynd gate and send wardworkers through. They go to hold the grove, not loot it.
DIALOGUE_SAIRVETH_VEILED_PATHS_OPEN||Sairveth opens elven passage below the dwarven gate|The sealed passage by the Ancient Dwarven Gate should answer now. Glassroot gave you enough standing with Telwynd.\nReturn below the gate and touch the elven wardwork. If it opens, stay on the main grove path.
DIALOGUE_SAIRVETH_HIGHWIND_START||Sairveth Buried Highwind first offer|Highwind Monastery has Telwynd wardwork under White Seal repairs, and there may be a lower door beneath the chapel.\nGo there, inspect the old chapel, then return. If the work is still sound, I will send you to the man who knows the lower entrance.
DIALOGUE_SAIRVETH_IDLE||Sairveth default wardwork chatter|Telwynd paths are not open to travelers. Bring me sealed doors, true shards, or broken wards before you test them.\nFor ordinary wardwork, speak plainly and I will see what can be done.
DIALOGUE_EIVYSS_BLACKGLASS_TABLE_LOCKED||Eivyss blackglass table locked before bloodline proof|No. Not yet. Sairveth has not vouched for your White Seal blood. Settle that with him first, then I will look at your shard.
DIALOGUE_EIVYSS_BLACKGLASS_TABLE_OPEN||Eivyss blackglass table unlocked|Sairveth vouched for you. Put true blackglass shards on the copper tray; I can set one into wards, staves, circlets, and Telwynd work.
DIALOGUE_EIVYSS_BLACKGLASS_TABLE_LIMITS||Eivyss blackglass table tier reminder|One shard, one finished piece. Stronger work waits until Sairveth opens more of the table.
DIALOGUE_EIVYSS_MOONWELL_ATTUNE_DONE||Eivyss Moonwell Alignment lens attunement complete|The lens is attuned. Take it to Moonwell Observatory and seat it in the frame. My table is done with it.
DIALOGUE_EIVYSS_MOONWELL_INSTALL||Eivyss Moonwell Alignment install reminder|The lens is tuned. Take it to Moonwell Observatory and seat it in the frame. My table is done with it.
DIALOGUE_EIVYSS_MOONWELL_RETURN_VEYDRAS||Eivyss Moonwell Alignment final handoff reminder|The lens is seated? Then Veydras needs the reading. Return to him in the White Seal building.
DIALOGUE_EIVYSS_CRYSTAL_TUNED||Eivyss tunes the White Vault crystal|This is White Seal glass, but the hurt in it is older than Highmark. I can tune the crystal; I cannot finish the work from this table.\nTake it to the lower ritual chamber beneath Moonwell Observatory. Touch it to the Moonwell Rite there. If something wakes, quiet it, then touch the crystal to the rite again.
DIALOGUE_EIVYSS_CRYSTAL_MISSING||Eivyss reminder when the tainted crystal is missing|Oryn sent you with a tainted White Vault crystal, yes? Bring it to me. I cannot tune a crystal from a polite description.
DIALOGUE_EIVYSS_CRYSTAL_RITE_REMINDER||Eivyss reminder to use the lower Moonwell rite|The crystal is tuned. Take it below Moonwell Observatory and touch it to the lower rite. If the chamber answers badly, answer worse.
DIALOGUE_EIVYSS_ELDERWYRM_START||Eivyss Elderwyrm Grove first offer|Elderwyrm Grove is no longer sleeping. Caerwyn has bent the old green wards around himself.\nReclaim the grove, or the path workers Sairveth sends there will go in with songs and come out as warnings.
DIALOGUE_AELTHIR_GROVE_TABLE_CLOSED||Aelthir grove table closed before reclamation|The grove table stays packed until Sairveth opens the gate. If Caerwyn still holds Elderwyrm Grove, go back to Telwynd and settle that first.
DIALOGUE_AELTHIR_GROVE_MAGIC_OPEN||Aelthir grove magic table open after reclamation|Gate open, crates tied down, ward line steady. Browse if you need grove work; step back if the old well flares.
DIALOGUE_SMUGGLER_DORUN_DONE||Disgruntled smuggler post-Dorun idle|Dorun paid. That is the end of it.
DIALOGUE_SMUGGLER_DORUN_HANDIN||Disgruntled smuggler Dorun hand-in|Dorun Varr is dead. Good. He crossed me, and now the price is paid. Take this.
DIALOGUE_SMUGGLER_DORUN_ROUTE||Disgruntled smuggler Dorun route reminder|Bandit Toll Camp. Dorun Varr. Kill him, then come back.
DIALOGUE_SMUGGLER_DORUN_OFFER||Disgruntled smuggler Dorun offer|Dorun Varr crossed me. He runs Bandit Toll Camp now. Go there, kill him, and come back when the price is paid.
DIALOGUE_SMUGGLER_LOCKBOX_DONE||Disgruntled smuggler post-lockbox idle|The lower cove is finished. If the watch asks, you saw wet crates and dead bandits. Leave my name out of it.
DIALOGUE_SMUGGLER_LOCKBOX_HANDIN||Disgruntled smuggler lockbox hand-in|Put it on the ground by the wall. Do not open it. The seal is still shut, and I pay for shut boxes.
DIALOGUE_SMUGGLER_LOCKBOX_PAY||Disgruntled smuggler lockbox payment|Good. Old Snapjaw is dead, the box is back, and I can move before the buyers come asking. Take the lockbox pay.
DIALOGUE_SMUGGLER_LOCKBOX_ROUTE||Disgruntled smuggler lockbox route reminder|Same grotto, lower cove, iron lockbox. The way down is a secret stair around the pond outside; search the wet stones and you will find it. Bring the box back shut.
DIALOGUE_SMUGGLER_SEAL_HANDIN||Disgruntled smuggler seal hand-in|That is my seal. You did the job clean, so I will pay what I promised.
DIALOGUE_SMUGGLER_LOCKBOX_AFTER_SEAL||Disgruntled smuggler lockbox offer after seal hand-in|There is one more thing in that grotto. The lower floor is hidden; search around the pond outside for a covered stair. My iron lockbox is in the lower cove. Bring it back shut and I will pay better coin.
DIALOGUE_SMUGGLER_LOCKBOX_OFFER_AFTER_SEAL||Disgruntled smuggler lockbox offer after badge quest complete|You brought the seal back clean. If you want the better pay, go back to the grotto and search the pond outside for a hidden stair. It drops to the lower cove where my iron lockbox is. Bring it back shut.
DIALOGUE_SMUGGLER_SEAL_ROUTE||Disgruntled smuggler seal route reminder|Take the east road from Havenford to King's Barrow, then turn south from the barrow road to Smuggler Grotto. Bring back my lead seal.
DIALOGUE_SMUGGLER_SEAL_START_PRESSURE||Disgruntled smuggler first meeting pressure|Keep your voice down. You are not Havenford watch, and the grotto crew will not know your face. Good.
DIALOGUE_SMUGGLER_SEAL_START_ROUTE||Disgruntled smuggler first meeting route and reward|Take the east road from Havenford toward King's Barrow, then turn south to Smuggler Grotto. Bring back my lead seal whole, and I pay.
DIALOGUE_SMUGGLER_RESPECTABLE_COMPANY||Smuggler's indirect response after the Havenford Watch route was selected|You've taken to respectable company, I hear. Best keep to it.
DIALOGUE_MERRIT_REPAIRED_SHOP_OPEN||Merrit repaired shop open chatter|The case is fixed. Shop's open.
DIALOGUE_MERRIT_TRAVEL_CASE_DAMAGE||Merrit travel case chatter before shop repair|The case took a hit on the road. Can't open it proper yet.
DIALOGUE_MERRIT_TRAVEL_CASE_STOCK||Merrit travel case stock note before shop repair|Once it's fixed, the stock will be worth a look.
DIALOGUE_THRUNNA_ORC_FORTRESS_DONE||Stonecleft gate warden post Orc Fortress completion|No new raids from the Orc Fortress. Gorvuk's warband is broken.
DIALOGUE_THRUNNA_ORC_FORTRESS_TURNIN||Stonecleft gate warden Orc Fortress turn-in|Gorvuk is dead? Good. That should break the fortress command.
DIALOGUE_THRUNNA_ORC_FORTRESS_REWARD||Stonecleft gate warden Orc Fortress reward|Take this hammer and the road pay. Stonecleft pays for cleared roads.
DIALOGUE_THRUNNA_ORC_FORTRESS_REMINDER_ROUTE||Stonecleft gate warden Orc Fortress route reminder|Orc Fortress is southwest of Stonecleft. Kill Gorvuk and report back.
DIALOGUE_THRUNNA_NEEDS_FORTRESS_SKETCH||Thrunna general chatter before Orc Fortress sketch|Gatehouse is barely safe these days with all the monsters around.
DIALOGUE_THRUNNA_GATE_WARDEN_IDLE||Thrunna gate warden chatter after the fortress sketch chain is removed|Gatehouse is barely safe these days with all the monsters around.
DIALOGUE_THRUNNA_HALF_ORC_REFUSAL||Thrunna refuses half-orc player for Orc Fortress work|Keep the sketch. I will not send a half-orc under Stonecleft colors against an orc palisade. That would get you killed before you reached the gate.
DIALOGUE_THRUNNA_ORC_FORTRESS_TOO_GREEN||Thrunna Orc Fortress level gate|Not yet. That fortress is too much for you right now. Come back stronger.
DIALOGUE_THRUNNA_ORC_FORTRESS_MAP_HANDIN_READ||Stonecleft gate warden Orc Fortress map hand-in read|This is an orc fortress, not a camp. Watch posts, dug rooms, and Gorvuk's mark.
DIALOGUE_THRUNNA_ORC_FORTRESS_MAP_HANDIN_ASK||Stonecleft gate warden Orc Fortress map hand-in ask|I am keeping the sketch. Break the warband, kill Gorvuk, and report back. Hammer and coin if you return.
DIALOGUE_BOREK_ORC_FORTRESS_DONE||Stonecleft scout post Orc Fortress completion|No fresh cuts on the western track. Looks like Gorvuk's crew stopped dragging timber across the road.
DIALOGUE_BOREK_SKETCH_TO_THRUNNA||Stonecleft scout reminder after the orc fortress sketch has been found or delivered|The western track is quiet for now. Thrunna decides the rest.
DIALOGUE_BOREK_TOO_GREEN||Stonecleft scout level gate|Not yet. That fort is gate business now, and Thrunna will want the sketch intact.
DIALOGUE_BOREK_SKETCH_DELIVERY||Traveller's Rest innkeeper follow-up after Old Cave, giving Orc Fortress sketch|A trader left this after hearing you came back from Old Cave. It shows an orc palisade west of Stonecleft. Take it to the gate warden; she will know if it matches scout reports.
DIALOGUE_BORRI_RESCUED_REPEAT||Borri repeat after rescue|I can make Stonecleft from here. Finish what you came for; I will not slow you down.
DIALOGUE_BORRI_RESCUE||Borri first rescue in Orc Fortress|By the forge, I thought those orcs had me. This is not the last of them—I heard talk of war camps farther north. I am going back to Stonecleft. You have my thanks.
DIALOGUE_BORRI_HELM_REWARD||Borri helm reward at Stonecleft after rescue|I made it back. This helm is yours now, and better in your hands than locked in a dwarf chest.
DIALOGUE_BORRI_ORC_FORTRESS_REPORT||Borri receives the Orc Fortress report and reveals the Warrens route|Gorvuk kept a rough map of tunnels farther north. The survivors call them warrens. Take this hammer; if you follow them, make certain none come back.
DIALOGUE_BORRI_ORC_WARRENS_REMINDER||Borri reminds the player about the Orc Warrens|The warrens are farther north, cut into the hills. Cramped ground favors a short weapon and a steady shield.
DIALOGUE_BORRI_ORC_WARRENS_TURNIN||Borri receives the final Orc Warrens report|Their chief is dead? Then the tunnels can rot around the rest. This armor was made for a harder road than mine. Take it.
DIALOGUE_BORRI_ORC_CAMPAIGN_DONE||Borri after the Orc Warrens campaign|No new bands have come south from those hills. You ended more than one raid in those tunnels.
DIALOGUE_BORRI_ORC_CALDUS_ROUTE_ACK||Borri acknowledges that another report already set the route|Word reached the gatehall before you did. The north road will tell the rest.
DIALOGUE_MAVETH_FARMER_THOM_HOME||Farmer Maveth after missing husband quest complete|Thom is home, breathing, and stubborn enough to complain about the fence again. I will take that miracle. Our family is in your debt.
DIALOGUE_MAVETH_FARMER_THOM_RETURNED||Farmer Maveth after Thom returns before reward|Thom is back. Shaken half out of his skin, but back. Thank you. I had started counting which neighbors could help me dig.
DIALOGUE_MAVETH_FARMER_REMINDER_SHRINE||Farmer Maveth Roadside Shrine reminder|Have you found any sign of Thom? Every hour makes it harder to pretend he only lost the path.
DIALOGUE_MAVETH_FARMER_REMINDER_GOBLIN||Farmer Maveth Goblin Cave reminder|Have you found any sign of Thom? Every hour makes it harder to pretend he only lost the path.
DIALOGUE_MAVETH_FARMER_START_PRESSURE||Farmer Maveth first meeting pressure|My husband Thom has been gone too long. The chores still wait for him, his cup still sits by the hearth, and I am near out of lies to tell myself.
DIALOGUE_MAVETH_FARMER_START_SHRINE||Farmer Maveth Roadside Shrine offer|Thom followed tracks out past the north fence and never came home. I do not know where the trail carried him. Please find him if he is alive, or bring me the truth if he is not.
DIALOGUE_MAVETH_FARMER_START_GOBLIN||Farmer Maveth Goblin Cave offer|Thom followed tracks out past the north fence and never came home. I do not know where the trail carried him. Please find him if he is alive, or bring me the truth if he is not.
DIALOGUE_THOM_LOST_REPEAT||Thom lost farmer repeat after rescue flag|I owe you twice over. Once for finding me, once for not leaving me there.
DIALOGUE_THOM_LOST_RESCUE||Thom lost farmer first rescue|You... by all the saints, you came. I thought I was dead and only waiting for the dark to notice. Get me out of here.
DIALOGUE_THOM_WOLD_REWARD||Farmer Thom reward after rescue|This charm has seen me through bad weather and worse choices. Take it. It did its work for me.
DIALOGUE_THOM_WOLD_HOME_IDLE||Farmer Thom post-reward home chatter|I am home with Maveth, the hearth is warm, and I am done chasing tracks for a while.
DIALOGUE_NOTHAS_THOM_FOUND||Porter Nothas after Thom is found|You found my brother? The gods smile on you.
DIALOGUE_NOTHAS_THOM_MISSING_HINT||Porter Nothas before Thom is found|Thom's missing. Maveth in Havenford is sick with worry. If you can find him, the family would be in your debt.
DIALOGUE_HARREN_TUTORIAL_START||NPC dialogue in talk_harren before Harren starts the note delivery quest|You're awake. Good. Harren, old friend of your father's, and the fool who brought you this close to Brindle Quay. I go no farther. That amulet has started pulling again, and I know enough old family stories to be afraid of it. Take this note to Dockmaster Garran at the quay. Grab what you can from the crate, follow the east path, and keep moving.
DIALOGUE_HARREN_TUTORIAL_REMINDER||NPC dialogue in talk_harren after Harren starts the note delivery quest|East path to Brindle Quay. Put my note in Garran's hand, not in a ditch.
DIALOGUE_GARRAN_NO_NOTE||Dockmaster Garran no-note refusal before Harren's delivery quest|Harren said he would send a note. Bring it here before you ask me for passage.
DIALOGUE_GARRAN_NOTE_HANDIN||Dockmaster Garran Harren note hand-in|Harren's hand, sure enough. He says the amulet is stirring and that means more than I like. The Reedwater boat needs the night before it can sail; no captain takes strange water tired. Get a room at Orrin's inn north of the quay and be back at first light.
DIALOGUE_GARRAN_SLEEP_AT_INN||Dockmaster Garran starts sleep-at-inn objective|Orrin's inn is north of here. Tell him I sent you for the spare room, then sleep while the crew readies the boat.
DIALOGUE_GARRAN_SLEEP_REMINDER||Dockmaster Garran sleep-at-inn reminder|No half-rested passenger on my quay at dawn. Sleep at Orrin's inn and come back when the light is up.
DIALOGUE_GARRAN_READY_TO_SAIL||Dockmaster Garran post-rest travel handoff|Rested? Good. Captain Thauld is ready for Reedwater Docks. The water has grown mean and the inland roads are worse, so once you are ashore, follow the north road toward Havenford.
DIALOGUE_CORREN_STOCK||NPC dialogue in talk_corren for tutorial provisioner stock|Need supplies before the crossing? Rations, bandages, rope, and rain-stubborn kits are on the shelves. Buy dull things now; dull things save lives.
DIALOGUE_BRECK_START_CHECK||Guard Breck starts class-action tutorial quest|New blood on the quay. Before the road tests you, I will. Open with your class technique when the bout starts.
DIALOGUE_BRECK_START_INPUT||Guard Breck class-action tutorial input instruction|When your turn comes, use {class_actions}. Learn the motion here, where mistakes only bruise.
DIALOGUE_BRECK_ACTION_USED||Guard Breck after class action is used before road fight|There it is. Now finish the bout and remember that edge when the road stops being polite.
DIALOGUE_BRECK_FIGHT_DONE||Guard Breck after tutorial fight is complete|Good enough. The Dragonwake will hit harder than I did.
DIALOGUE_ORRIN_ROOM_NOT_READY||Innkeeper Orrin before dockmaster sends player to sleep|No room held until Garran clears it. Dockmasters make poor friends, but good paperwork.
DIALOGUE_ORRIN_ROOM_READY||Innkeeper Orrin sleep-at-inn support line|Garran sent word. The back room is yours, clean enough and quiet enough. Rest while the boat is made ready.
DIALOGUE_TUTORIAL_INN_REST_TITLE|32|tutorial dialogue title after resting at Orrin's inn|Innkeeper Orrin
DIALOGUE_TUTORIAL_INN_REST_MORNING||Innkeeper Orrin after first inn rest, before giving camping kit|Light is up, and Garran hates waiting. See him or the captain before the tide turns.
DIALOGUE_TUTORIAL_INN_REST_CAMP_KIT||Innkeeper Orrin gives camping kit after first inn rest|Take this camping kit for the road north. Inns get scarce fast once the roofs thin out.
DIALOGUE_TUTORIAL_GUIDE_LAYOUT||NPC dialogue in talk_tutorial_guide about Brindle Quay layout|Brindle Quay is small enough to learn in one look. Docks and boat landing south, road east to the crossing, then north toward Reedwater and Havenford. {guide_help_menu}
DIALOGUE_TUTORIAL_GUIDE_MARKED_NPCS||NPC dialogue in talk_tutorial_guide about marked NPCs|Folk with business stand out if you look for them. Garran handles passage, Corren sells supplies, and Breck trains anyone brave enough to ask. For Breck's drill, {guide_class_actions}
DIALOGUE_TUTORIAL_GUIDE_SURVIVAL||NPC dialogue in talk_tutorial_guide about survival guidance|The Dragonwake has made road and water less forgiving. Rest at inns or safe camps, keep bandages close, and eat before hunger makes the choice for you. {guide_inventory}
DIALOGUE_TUTORIAL_GUIDE_BOAT_ROUTE||NPC dialogue in talk_tutorial_guide about the boat route|Once Garran clears you, the boat runs to Reedwater Docks. From there, follow the north road toward Havenford until you know the country.

STORY_NPC_DETAIL_ALDREN_COMPLETE||NPC inspect detail for Aldren after cave chief quest completion|He looks worn but steadier, already spending the victory on repairs and patrols.
STORY_NPC_DETAIL_ALDREN_OPEN||NPC inspect detail for Aldren before cave chief quest completion|He looks sleepless, with gate tools, torn straps, and guard names close at hand.
STORY_NPC_DETAIL_THAULD||NPC inspect detail for Thauld|He keeps checking the cracked hull ribs, stern rope, and Reedwater dock cleats.
STORY_NPC_DETAIL_VOSK||NPC inspect detail for Vosk|He keeps glancing from the line to the south channel, waiting for Captain Veysha's mark.
STORY_NPC_DETAIL_QUADE||NPC inspect detail for Quade|He keeps close to the skiff, ready to untie it the moment a passenger pays.
STORY_NPC_DETAIL_VEYSHA||NPC inspect detail for Veysha|She watches the water, the skiff, and every traveler standing too close to the edge.
STORY_NPC_DETAIL_MIRA||NPC inspect detail for Mira|She keeps the lamp flasks corked tight before dusk.
STORY_NPC_DETAIL_KETHRA||NPC inspect detail for Kethra|She checks each spear by flex, balance, and how the grip sits in wet hands.
STORY_NPC_DETAIL_NESKA||NPC inspect detail for Neska|She keeps one hand on the mug shelf and one eye on the tavern door.
STORY_NPC_DETAIL_BRAN||NPC inspect detail for Bran|He keeps one boot pinning a net while both hands work the torn edge.
STORY_NPC_DETAIL_BRANNA||NPC inspect detail for Travellers' Rest innkeeper|She keeps the room keys near her hand and counts cups before anyone leaves.
STORY_NPC_DETAIL_ORRICK||NPC inspect detail for Travellers' Rest shopkeeper|He keeps the better stock close enough to cover with one hand.
STORY_NPC_DETAIL_VELRA||NPC inspect detail for Travellers' Rest arcane peddler|Her case is packed with sealed scrolls, capped wands, and small warded boxes.
STORY_NPC_DETAIL_CALDUS||NPC inspect detail for Travellers' Rest warrior|He sits straight-backed even at rest, with an old blade close to hand and one eye on the inn doors.
STORY_NPC_DETAIL_CAEL||NPC inspect detail for Travellers' Rest researcher|He keeps road rubbings, glass notes, and star-glass sketches clipped under a slate weight.
STORY_NPC_DETAIL_NOLL||NPC inspect detail for shady Travellers' Rest patron|He keeps a folded wagon tally under his cup and sits facing both doors.
STORY_NPC_DETAIL_MERRIT_REPAIRED||NPC inspect detail for Merrit after shop repair|He keeps the repaired shop neat, locked, and ready for buyers with coin for rings and charms.
STORY_NPC_DETAIL_MERRIT_BURNED||NPC inspect detail for Merrit before shop repair|He keeps one travel case close and checks the latch whenever a customer comes near.
STORY_NPC_DETAIL_TIDEHOOK_NETMENDER||NPC inspect detail for Tidehook netmender|She works fast, cutting bad knots instead of pretending they can be saved.
STORY_NPC_DETAIL_SARN||NPC inspect detail for Highmark market merchant|He keeps the coin bowl behind the sacks and checks each cart mark before he prices a bundle.
STORY_NPC_DETAIL_DARRON||NPC inspect detail for Highmark armorer|He keeps lance-pattern mail on the upper hooks and traveller pieces below.
STORY_NPC_DETAIL_BRETHRA||NPC inspect detail for Highmark provisioner|She keeps field kits near the counter and oil flasks sealed under waxed cloth.
STORY_NPC_DETAIL_MAVETH_APOTHECARY||NPC inspect detail for Highmark apothecary|She keeps the glowing bottles behind the counter and marks uncorking dates on a slate.
STORY_NPC_DETAIL_JAETH||NPC inspect detail for Highmark fletcher|He flexes each bowstave once, checks the grain, and sets warped shafts in a reject barrel.
STORY_NPC_DETAIL_OSKARN||NPC inspect detail for Highmark jeweler|He keeps loose stones in felt trays and locks each ring case after showing one piece.
STORY_NPC_DETAIL_TESSA||NPC inspect detail for Tessa|She looks light on her feet, weathered by the road, and alert to movement at the edge of town.
STORY_NPC_DETAIL_MAELIN||NPC inspect detail for Maelin|She looks tired but composed, like a shrine-keeper used to calming fear before it turns to panic.
STORY_NPC_DETAIL_BRANNOC||NPC inspect detail for Brannoc|He looks strong enough to work the forge all day and still swing a hammer if the door breaks.
STORY_NPC_DETAIL_GARRICK||NPC inspect detail for Garrick|He patrols between the shrine road and the commons, checking carts, strangers, and the lanes leading back to Thavoss's hall.
STORY_NPC_DETAIL_VETHRIN||NPC inspect detail for Vethrin|He keeps stopping to compare chips in the stone with notes on a folded scrap.
STORY_NPC_DETAIL_THERYN||NPC inspect detail for Theryn|He looks frail, sharp-eyed, and fully awake despite the late hour.
STORY_NPC_DETAIL_THROKK||NPC inspect detail for Throkk|He keeps his hammers, stone gauges, and forge notes within easy reach.
STORY_NPC_DETAIL_THAREC||NPC inspect detail for High Canon|He looks composed, deliberate, and used to dangerous relics arriving with missing labels and burnt wrappings.
STORY_NPC_DETAIL_TOVAN||NPC inspect detail for White Seal antiquities seller|He keeps the case locked, sorted, and close enough to shut with one hand.
STORY_NPC_DETAIL_ORYN||NPC inspect detail for White Vault sacristan|He looks steady enough to open a sealed door, and careful enough to resent being rushed.
STORY_NPC_DETAIL_VAUST||NPC inspect detail for Kestrel commander|He watches the breach road, the gate horns, and the wounded line without sitting down.
STORY_NPC_DETAIL_SERRIN||NPC inspect detail for Kestrel field supplier|He keeps spare spearheads, field packs, patched mail, and ration sacks close to hand.
STORY_NPC_DETAIL_KESTREL_GUARD||NPC inspect detail for Kestrel guards and scouts|The Lancer looks tired from smoke, disciplined, and one horn call away from the wall.
STORY_NPC_DETAIL_KESTREL_SAPPER||NPC inspect detail for Kestrel sapper|The Lancer looks blast-smudged, steady-handed, and more comfortable near broken stone than open ground.
STORY_NPC_DETAIL_KESTREL_CAMP_WORKER||NPC inspect detail for Kestrel camp workers|The smith looks worn thin by field work, but not close to stopping.
STORY_NPC_DETAIL_EIRADHA||NPC inspect detail for elf contact|She looks poised, guarded, and perfectly aware of every nearby exit.
STORY_NPC_DETAIL_SAIRVETH||NPC inspect detail for Telwynd keeper|She stands calm beside cut ward glass, sealed tools, and a covered blackglass table.
STORY_NPC_DETAIL_AELRION||NPC inspect detail for Telwynd bowyer|He checks each bow by flex, grain, and how cleanly the string settles.
STORY_NPC_DETAIL_AELTHIR||NPC inspect detail for Elderwyrm Grove enchanter|He keeps high wardwork close, wrapped, and ready to cover if the grove alarms ring.
STORY_NPC_DETAIL_FISHERMAN||NPC inspect detail for generic fishermen|He keeps a line spool under one foot and checks the river before answering.
STORY_NPC_DETAIL_PEASANT||NPC inspect detail for generic town resident|The town resident keeps half a step from the road traffic, ready to get back to work.
STORY_NPC_DETAIL_TRAVELLERS_REST_TRAVELLER||NPC inspect detail for Travellers' Rest traveler|The traveler's boots are unlaced under the bench, but the bedroll stays tied.
STORY_NPC_DETAIL_PORTER||NPC inspect detail for porter|The shoulder strap has been patched twice, and one parcel is tied with a White Seal shrine tag.
STORY_NPC_DETAIL_LABORER||NPC inspect detail for laborer|The laborer's cuffs are caked with lime dust, and a crate hook at the belt has a bent tooth.
STORY_NPC_DETAIL_EDRAN||NPC inspect detail for King's Barrow pilgrim|His thumb stays on the manuscript case's knot, checking that the wax seal has not cracked.
STORY_NPC_DETAIL_PILGRIM||NPC inspect detail for generic pilgrim|Mud cakes both sandals, and the shrine token is wrapped in oiled cloth against the rain.
STORY_NPC_DETAIL_STABLEHAND||NPC inspect detail for stablehand|The stablehand keeps one eye on the hitching rail and one hand on a currycomb with a cracked handle.
STORY_NPC_DETAIL_DEFAULT||NPC inspect detail fallback for known story NPCs|This person looks wary but unhurt.
