MONSTER_ORC_THROWER_NAME|orc thrower
MONSTER_ORC_THROWER_DESC|A wiry orc skirmisher with a hand axe in one fist and more axes hanging from a rope belt. It softens targets at range, then closes when the line breaks.
MONSTER_ORC_WARLOCK_NAME|orc warlock
MONSTER_ORC_WARLOCK_DESC|A scarred orc fire-caller in a singed robe, gripping a mace with blackened iron bands. It hangs behind heavier orcs and throws destructive magic into crowded fights.
MONSTER_BANDIT_MARKSMAN_NAME|bandit marksman
MONSTER_BANDIT_MARKSMAN_DESC|A hard-eyed human archer in leather armor, carrying a longbow and a short blade. It keeps lanes open and punishes anyone who tries to cross exposed ground.
MONSTER_BANDIT_MAGE_NAME|bandit mage
MONSTER_BANDIT_MAGE_DESC|A nervous outlaw spellcaster in a travel robe, carrying a dagger and stolen spell scraps. It uses simple arcane tricks to escape pressure and keep stronger bandits alive.
MONSTER_ASSASSIN_NAME|assassin
MONSTER_ASSASSIN_DESC|A quiet killer in close dark leathers, carrying a narrow dagger and moving with no wasted steps. It waits for a clean angle, then lets poison do part of the work.
MONSTER_ASSASSIN_ARCHER_NAME|assassin archer
MONSTER_ASSASSIN_ARCHER_DESC|A lean killer with a blackened shortbow, light armor, and a poisoned knife at the belt. It keeps distance and relies on one sharp opening rather than endurance.
MONSTER_LESSER_WATER_ELEMENTAL_NAME|lesser water elemental
MONSTER_LESSER_WATER_ELEMENTAL_DESC|A knee-high wave of animated water with a faint torso shape and grasping spray for hands. It surges from flooded stone and batters with cold, heavy water.
COMBAT_MONSTER_NET_MISS|The {0} throws a net, but you slip clear.
COMBAT_MONSTER_NET_HIT|The {0} throws a net over you.
COMBAT_MONSTER_ACTION_HEAVY_BOLT|fires a heavy bolt
COMBAT_MONSTER_ACTION_ACID_SPRAY|sprays acid vapor
MONSTER_BOMBARDIER_BEETLE_NAME|bombardier beetle
MONSTER_BOMBARDIER_BEETLE_DESC|A dog-sized beetle with a mottled shell and hot chemical sacs under its abdomen. It turns its rear toward threats and sprays burning acid vapor before closing with its jaws.
MONSTER_HOBGOBLIN_ARBALESTER_NAME|hobgoblin arbalester
MONSTER_HOBGOBLIN_ARBALESTER_DESC|A tall hobgoblin crossbowman in quilted armor, carrying a crank-bowed arbalest and a short blade. It waits behind the line and fires heavy bolts down clear corridors.
MONSTER_PHASE_SPIDER_NAME|phase spider
MONSTER_PHASE_SPIDER_DESC|A large gray spider with translucent legs and a body that flickers out of line with the room. It vanishes between lunges, then returns close enough to web or bite.
MONSTER_SWORD_SPIDER_NAME|sword spider
MONSTER_SWORD_SPIDER_DESC|A hard-shelled spider with long blade-like legs and a narrow cutting abdomen. It scuttles into reach and carves with several slashing limbs at once.
MONSTER_DISPLACER_BEAST_NAME|displacer beast
MONSTER_DISPLACER_BEAST_DESC|A panther-like magical beast with six legs and two lashing tentacles over its shoulders. Its outline slides away from its true body, making direct charges unreliable.
MONSTER_EVIL_MAGIC_USER_NAME|evil magic-user
MONSTER_EVIL_MAGIC_USER_DESC|A hostile spellcaster in a patched robe, clutching a dagger and a bundle of stolen notes. It stays behind stronger bodies and uses simple arcane magic to break a straight approach.
MONSTER_EVIL_MAGE_NAME|evil mage
MONSTER_EVIL_MAGE_DESC|A practiced enemy mage in a scorched robe, carrying a wand case and a narrow knife. It casts battlefield spells freely enough that open ground becomes dangerous.
MONSTER_EVIL_ARCHMAGE_NAME|evil archmage
MONSTER_EVIL_ARCHMAGE_DESC|A dangerous archmage in a travel-stained robe, calm-eyed and guarded by layered magic. It turns corridors and crowds against intruders with high arcane spells.
MONSTER_SKELETON_ARCHER_NAME|skeleton archer
MONSTER_SKELETON_ARCHER_DESC|A human skeleton with a cracked shortbow, a knife, and old arrow shafts rattling in its ribs. It holds the back of a crypt passage and looses brittle arrows at anything living.
MONSTER_GHAST_NAME|ghast
MONSTER_GHAST_DESC|A taller ghoul with tight gray skin, black claws, and a fixed hungry stare. Its touch can lock muscles long enough for the dead thing to tear in close.
MONSTER_GIANT_SCORPION_NAME|giant scorpion
MONSTER_GIANT_SCORPION_DESC|A heavy cave scorpion with dark plates, wide claws, and a raised venomous tail. It holds ground with its pincers while looking for a clean sting.
MONSTER_GIANT_WASP_NAME|giant wasp
MONSTER_GIANT_WASP_DESC|A dog-sized wasp with glassy wings, a narrow striped body, and a long stinger. It darts in and backs away before its prey can settle into a stance.
MONSTER_GIANT_SLUG_NAME|giant slug
MONSTER_GIANT_SLUG_DESC|A massive gray slug with a wet ridged body, rasping mouthparts, and acidic slime pooling under it. It moves slowly but spits burning acid when prey stays out of reach.
MONSTER_DOPPELGANGER_NAME|doppelganger
MONSTER_DOPPELGANGER_DESC|A smooth-faced mimic of a person, wearing a borrowed shape with unsettling precision. It steps like an adventurer and uses that familiarity to break focus at close range.
MONSTER_BEHOLDER_NAME|beholder
MONSTER_BEHOLDER_DESC|A floating orb of flesh with one central eye, a wide mouth, and smaller eyestalks turning in several directions at once. It dominates open space with cruel rays instead of chasing prey.
STORY_MSG_REACHED_CAMP_KESTREL|Camp Kestrel sprawls near the Great Scar in canvas, ash, and hammer-noise from fresh breachworks.
CATALOG_LOCATION_CAMP_KESTREL_SUMMARY|Camp Kestrel is a forward Silver Lance camp near the Great Scar.
STORY_MSG_QUEST_UPDATE_RETURN_ORYN_BEACON|Quest updated: return to High Canon Tharec with the Beacon Prism.
STORY_MSG_QUEST_UPDATE_CLEANSING_TAKE_EIVYSS|Quest updated: take the Tainted White Vault Crystal to Eivyss Glass-Singer in Telwynd.
STORY_MSG_QUEST_UPDATE_CLEANSING_MOONWELL_RITE|Quest updated: take the Resonant White Vault Crystal to the lower ritual chamber beneath Moonwell Observatory.
STORY_MSG_QUEST_UPDATE_CLEANSING_DEFEAT_ECHO|Quest updated: defeat the Moonwell Echo.
STORY_MSG_QUEST_UPDATE_CLEANSING_FINISH_RITE|Quest updated: touch the Resonant White Vault Crystal to the Moonwell Rite again.
STORY_MSG_QUEST_UPDATE_CLEANSING_RETURN_ORYN|Quest updated: return to Sacristan Oryn in Highmark.
STORY_MSG_CLEANSING_PLINTH_CLEANSED|The White Vault plinth holds steady. The old pressure is gone.
STORY_MSG_CLEANSING_PLINTH_DIM|The White Vault plinth is dim and cold. Taint still clings to the lower chamber.
STORY_MSG_MOONWELL_RITE_INERT|The lower Moonwell Rite hums under the old stone, but nothing answers.
STORY_MSG_MOONWELL_RITE_NEEDS_RESONANT_CRYSTAL|The rite is too quiet. Eivyss must tune the White Vault crystal before it can answer here.
STORY_MSG_MOONWELL_RITE_CRYSTAL_MISSING|The rite reaches for the Resonant White Vault Crystal, but it is not in your pack.
STORY_MSG_MOONWELL_RITE_STIRS|The rite stirs, then falls silent. Something blocks the chamber.
STORY_MSG_MOONWELL_RITE_ECHO_SUMMONED|The crystal rings against the Moonwell Rite. Pale light rises from the water and folds into a dragon-shaped ghost.
STORY_MSG_MOONWELL_RITE_ECHO_ALIVE|The Moonwell Echo holds the rite in a hard, cold grip.
STORY_MSG_MOONWELL_RITE_COMPLETED|The crystal clears in your hand, then dissolves into pale sparks. Far away, the White Vault's pressure breaks.
STORY_MSG_MOONWELL_RITE_SETTLED|The lower Moonwell Rite is quiet now.
STORY_MSG_BOSS_MOONWELL_ECHO_SLAIN|The Moonwell Echo breaks into pale rings of light. The lower rite steadies.
STORY_XP_BOSS_MOONWELL_ECHO_SLAIN|The Moonwell Echo is slain
NAMED_MONSTER_MOONWELL_ECHO_NAME|Moonwell Echo
BOSS_INTRO_MOONWELL_ECHO_THE_LIGHTGLASS_GHOST|A pale dragon-shape rises inside the ghost. It opens a mouth of cold light, and the Moonwell water trembles.
QUEST_LOG_CLEANSING_VAULT_RETURN_ORYN_OBJECTIVE|Return to Sacristan Oryn.
QUEST_LOG_CLEANSING_VAULT_RETURN_ORYN_DETAIL|Oryn says the White Vault is open but still fouled. He should know if the tainted crystal is missing.
QUEST_LOG_CLEANSING_VAULT_TAKE_EIVYSS_OBJECTIVE|Take the Tainted White Vault Crystal to Eivyss Glass-Singer.
QUEST_LOG_CLEANSING_VAULT_TAKE_EIVYSS_DETAIL|Oryn gave me a tainted crystal from the White Vault. Eivyss Glass-Singer in Telwynd may know how to tune it for a cleaner rite.
QUEST_LOG_CLEANSING_VAULT_RECOVER_TAINTED_OBJECTIVE|Recover the Tainted White Vault Crystal.
QUEST_LOG_CLEANSING_VAULT_RECOVER_TAINTED_DETAIL|The tainted White Vault crystal is missing. Eivyss cannot tune what I am not carrying.
QUEST_LOG_CLEANSING_VAULT_MOONWELL_RITE_OBJECTIVE|Take the Resonant White Vault Crystal to the lower Moonwell rite.
QUEST_LOG_CLEANSING_VAULT_MOONWELL_RITE_DETAIL|Eivyss tuned the crystal. I should take it to the lower ritual chamber beneath Moonwell Observatory and touch it to the Moonwell Rite.
QUEST_LOG_CLEANSING_VAULT_RECOVER_RESONANT_OBJECTIVE|Recover the Resonant White Vault Crystal.
QUEST_LOG_CLEANSING_VAULT_RECOVER_RESONANT_DETAIL|The resonant White Vault crystal is missing. The lower Moonwell rite needs it.
QUEST_LOG_CLEANSING_VAULT_DEFEAT_ECHO_OBJECTIVE|Defeat the Moonwell Echo.
QUEST_LOG_CLEANSING_VAULT_DEFEAT_ECHO_DETAIL|The Moonwell Rite woke a pale echo in the lower chamber. The rite will not finish while it holds the crystal's light.
QUEST_LOG_CLEANSING_VAULT_FINISH_RITE_OBJECTIVE|Touch the crystal to the Moonwell Rite again.
QUEST_LOG_CLEANSING_VAULT_FINISH_RITE_DETAIL|The Moonwell Echo is gone. The lower rite should be able to send the crystal's clean resonance back to the White Vault.
QUEST_LOG_CLEANSING_VAULT_RETURN_FINAL_OBJECTIVE|Return to Sacristan Oryn.
QUEST_LOG_CLEANSING_VAULT_RETURN_FINAL_DETAIL|The lower Moonwell rite answered, and the White Vault's pressure broke from far away. Oryn should know the chamber has settled.
DIALOGUE_ORYN_CLEANSING_START|The vault beast is dead, but the lower chamber still feels wrong. I drew this tainted crystal from the White Vault before the stair sealed again.\nTake it to Eivyss Glass-Singer in Telwynd. If Telwynd can tune it clean, the lower Moonwell rite may carry that work back here while we make the vault fit for people again.
DIALOGUE_ORYN_CLEANSING_CRYSTAL_MISSING|The White Vault crystal is not with you. Find it, then take it to Eivyss Glass-Singer in Telwynd.
DIALOGUE_ORYN_CLEANSING_TELWYND_REMINDER|Take the Tainted White Vault Crystal to Eivyss Glass-Singer in Telwynd. If anyone can tune White Seal glass without cracking it, he can.
DIALOGUE_ORYN_CLEANSING_MOONWELL_REMINDER|Eivyss tuned the crystal? Then take it below Moonwell Observatory. The lower ritual chamber is old enough to answer this kind of work.
DIALOGUE_EIVYSS_CRYSTAL_TUNED|This is White Seal glass, but the hurt in it is older than Highmark. I can tune the crystal; I cannot finish the work from this table.\nTake it to the lower ritual chamber beneath Moonwell Observatory. Touch it to the Moonwell Rite there. If something wakes, quiet it, then touch the crystal to the rite again.
DIALOGUE_EIVYSS_CRYSTAL_MISSING|Oryn sent you with a tainted White Vault crystal, yes? Bring it to me. I cannot tune a crystal from a polite description.
DIALOGUE_EIVYSS_CRYSTAL_RITE_REMINDER|The crystal is tuned. Take it below Moonwell Observatory and touch it to the lower rite. If the chamber answers badly, answer worse.
ITEM_TAINTED_WHITE_VAULT_CRYSTAL_NAME|Tainted White Vault Crystal
ITEM_TAINTED_WHITE_VAULT_CRYSTAL_DESC|A pale crystal from the White Vault, dimmed by old vault-taint.
ITEM_RESONANT_WHITE_VAULT_CRYSTAL_NAME|Resonant White Vault Crystal
ITEM_RESONANT_WHITE_VAULT_CRYSTAL_DESC|A White Vault crystal tuned by Telwynd glass-singing and ready for the lower Moonwell rite.
STORY_MSG_QUEST_UPDATE_SPEAK_ORYN_BEACON|Quest updated: speak with High Canon Tharec about the Beacon Prism.
STORY_MSG_QUEST_UPDATE_RECOVER_BEACON_PRISM|Quest updated: recover the Beacon Prism from the White Seal Tower far down the east road and return to Tharec.
STORY_NAME_ORYN|Oryn
STORY_MSG_WHITE_SEAL_TOWER_AID|Tharec gives you {0} for the road to the tower.
QUEST_LOG_BEACON_PRISM_TALK_THAREC_DETAIL|Highmark is reached. High Canon Tharec can explain what the White Seal knows about the star, the bloodline, and the dragons stirring below.
QUEST_LOG_BEACON_PRISM_TALK_ORYN_OBJECTIVE|Speak with High Canon Tharec in Highmark.
QUEST_LOG_BEACON_PRISM_TALK_ORYN_DETAIL|Tharec handles the Beacon Prism rite. I should recover the prism and bring it back to him.
QUEST_LOG_BEACON_PRISM_RETURN_OBJECTIVE|Return the Beacon Prism to High Canon Tharec.
QUEST_LOG_BEACON_PRISM_RETURN_DETAIL|The Beacon Prism is recovered. Tharec can set the prism and use my blood to turn the star to Lightglass.
QUEST_LOG_BEACON_PRISM_RECOVER_CLAIMED_OBJECTIVE|Recover the Beacon Prism and return to High Canon Tharec.
QUEST_LOG_BEACON_PRISM_RECOVER_CLAIMED_DETAIL|The prism was claimed from the White Seal Tower, but it is not in my pack. Tharec still needs it in Highmark.
QUEST_LOG_BEACON_PRISM_CLAIM_OBJECTIVE|Claim the Beacon Prism from the White Seal Tower.
QUEST_LOG_BEACON_PRISM_CLAIM_DETAIL|The dragon fell at the beacon. The Beacon Prism still glows above the chamber.
QUEST_LOG_BEACON_PRISM_OBJECTIVE|Recover the Beacon Prism from the White Seal Tower far down the east road.
QUEST_LOG_BEACON_PRISM_DETAIL|Tharec says the Beacon Prism is in the Tower of the White Seal far down the east road from Highmark. A dragon holds the tower. Recover the prism and bring it back to him.
QUEST_LOG_BEACON_PRISM_PREPARE_VAULT_OBJECTIVE|Return to High Canon Tharec.
QUEST_LOG_BEACON_PRISM_PREPARE_VAULT_DETAIL|The star should be Lightglass now, but Tharec still needs to settle the Beacon Prism rite.
QUEST_LOG_WHITE_VAULT_OPEN_OBJECTIVE|Open the White Vault.
QUEST_LOG_WHITE_VAULT_OPEN_DETAIL|The prism is set. Sacristan Oryn waits beside the vault stair in Highmark's White Seal hall. Something draconic waits below.
QUEST_LOG_WHITE_VAULT_RETURN_OBJECTIVE|Return to Sacristan Oryn.
QUEST_LOG_WHITE_VAULT_RETURN_DETAIL|The greater drake fell in the inner chamber. The White Vault is quiet enough for Oryn to inspect.
QUEST_LOG_WHITE_VAULT_RETURN_FINAL_OBJECTIVE|Return to Sacristan Oryn.
QUEST_LOG_WHITE_VAULT_RETURN_FINAL_DETAIL|The vault beast is slain. The White Vault is quiet enough for Oryn to inspect.
QUEST_LOG_WHITE_VAULT_OBJECTIVE|Slay the beast in the White Vault.
QUEST_LOG_WHITE_VAULT_DETAIL|Oryn opened the White Vault stair. Something draconic waits in the lower chamber. Kill it, then return to him.
DIALOGUE_THAREC_LIGHTGLASS_SHARD_REFERRAL|That is a pure blackglass shard, not a keepsake. Veydras can set it into the White Seal pattern and make a Lightglass fragment of it. Do not carry it longer than need requires.
DIALOGUE_THAREC_LIGHTGLASS_STAR_BLACKGLASS_LEAD|Your inherited star is Lightglass now: blackglass given law by your blood and our oldest patterns. With this Lightglass and your bloodline, the Scar may be closed. Blackglass Cavern is the clearest source we can still reach. Go down there and end what is feeding it. If you find blackglass shards, bring them to Veydras; he can judge what the White Seal can make of them.
DIALOGUE_THAREC_VAULT_ALREADY_PURIFIED|The star is already Lightglass, and that is the proof I needed. Keep it close; the lower seals will know that instrument when the road reaches them.
DIALOGUE_THAREC_WHITE_VAULT_TURNIN|The vault beast is dead. Good. Oryn can finish the chamber work from here. Your path leads deeper now: Blackglass Cavern is where the pressure is strongest.
DIALOGUE_THAREC_WHITE_VAULT_REMINDER|Oryn opened the White Vault stair. If you mean to reclaim that chamber, kill what waits below and return to him.
DIALOGUE_THAREC_BEACON_RETURN_TO_ORYN|Set the Beacon Prism here. When it is lit, press your blood to the star. The blackglass takes order: the star is Lightglass now. With that light and your bloodline, the Scar may still be closed. Blackglass Cavern is the strongest source we can reach; go down and end what is feeding it. If you choose to clear the White Vault, Oryn can open the lower ward.
DIALOGUE_ORYN_BEACON_HANDIN|The Beacon Prism belongs with Tharec's rite. Take it to him; my work begins when the lower ward opens.
DIALOGUE_ORYN_BEACON_SET|Tharec must settle the star before I risk the White Vault stair. Bring the prism to him.
DIALOGUE_ORYN_BEACON_SET_HALF_ORC|Tharec must settle the star before I risk the White Vault stair. Bring the prism to him.
DIALOGUE_THAREC_BEACON_READY|The star is Lightglass now. With that light and your bloodline, the Scar may still be closed. Blackglass Cavern is the strongest source we can reach; go down and end what is feeding it.
DIALOGUE_THAREC_BEACON_REMINDER|The Beacon Prism remains in the Tower of the White Seal, far down the east road. Kill the dragon, recover the prism, and bring it back to me.
DIALOGUE_THAREC_BEACON_ORYN_REMINDER|The Beacon Prism remains in the Tower of the White Seal, far down the east road. Kill the dragon, recover the prism, and bring it back to me.
DIALOGUE_THAREC_NEEDS_PROOF|You ask for sealed work on old blood and bare claims. Bring proof I can test, then we will speak.
DIALOGUE_THAREC_BEACON_START|That heirloom at your throat is not ornament. It is a blackglass star keyed to seal-priest blood. The old Istarian seals were built for bloodlines, and the dragons stirring below are answering that same broken pressure.\nThe Beacon Prism in the Tower of the White Seal can turn blackglass toward Lightglass when it is lit with a living sample. The tower lies far down the east road from Highmark. Kill the dragon there, recover the prism, and bring it back to me.
DIALOGUE_ORYN_BEACON_START|Tharec handles the Beacon Prism rite. Recover the prism from the Tower of the White Seal, then bring it back to him.
DIALOGUE_ORYN_BEACON_REMINDER|The Beacon Prism belongs with Tharec. Bring it to him when it is recovered.
DIALOGUE_ORYN_CLEANSING_COMPLETE_RITE|The vault is quiet. Not empty, never that, but quiet enough that I can trust the stair again.
DIALOGUE_ORYN_CLEANSING_COMPLETE_REWARD|You have done the White Seal a rare service. Take this reward and a Lightglass fragment. Use both with care.
FEATURE_VAULT_FOCUS_PLINTH_NAME|Vault Keystone Plinth
ITEM_RADIANT_LIGHTGLASS_STAR_AMULET_DESC|The radiant form of the old blackglass star. The cleansed White Vault keystone steadies its lightglass, and it grants +3 to all attributes.
DIALOGUE_LANCER_ORDERS_START|You there, traveler. Highmark has no runner to spare, and Camp Kestrel needs to know which west roads are open.\nIf you are heading to Camp Kestrel, carry that message to Captain Vaust Thane. He pays when it reaches his hand.
QUEST_LOG_ORDERS_FOR_KESTREL_DETAIL|A Silver Lancer says Camp Kestrel needs to know which west roads are open. I should carry the message to the camp and put it in the commander's hand.
QUEST_LOG_DEPTHS_OF_STARFALL_I_OBJECTIVE|Enter Blackglass Cavern.
NPC_LINE_TRAVELLERS_REST_SHADY_4|What fits in a cloak pocket travels well. What whispers stays buried.
STORY_MSG_QUEST_UPDATE_DESCEND_ISTARIAN|Quest updated: follow the lower descent into the Istarian Tunnels.
STORY_MSG_QUEST_UPDATE_ASK_THROKK_STONEWARD|Quest updated: ask in Stonecleft about the Stoneward Gate's dwarven runes.
STORY_MSG_REACHED_ISTARIAN_TUNNELS|You enter the Istarian Tunnels, old imperial stoneworks below the Blackglass descent.
DIALOGUE_THROKK_STONEWARD_BREAKER|You saw the Stoneward Gate and lived to complain about it? Good. Dwarven hands built that gate, and I know the release for that old lock. Go back below Camp Kestrel; it should open now.
QUEST_LOG_FINAL_DESCENT_II_DETAIL|The Lightglass star answers in the Starfall Core. The primordial dragon waits where the deep rumble becomes a voice.
QUEST_LOG_FINAL_DESCENT_I_DETAIL|The final blood seal is open. A core rift waits below it, bright with blackglass glare, leading into the Starfall Core.
QUEST_LOG_BLOOD_OF_THE_ANCIENTS_III_DETAIL|Theryn's words are in hand. At the final blood seal, the Lightglass star, the old phrase, and my blood should open the way.
QUEST_LOG_BLOOD_OF_THE_ANCIENTS_II_DETAIL|The final blood seal answers the Lightglass star, but it needs old words I do not know. Theryn Rusk in Havenford may remember them.
QUEST_LOG_BLOOD_OF_THE_ANCIENTS_I_DETAIL|The Stoneward Gate is open, and the route drops past it into deeper blackglass. Somewhere in the Sundering Depths, the final blood seal is waiting.
QUEST_LOG_DEPTHS_OF_STARFALL_III_DETAIL|The lower Istarian route should lead through the Stoneward Gate. I need to find it and work out what keeps it shut.
QUEST_LOG_DEPTHS_OF_STARFALL_II_DETAIL|Vharox is dead, and the lower Blackglass descent opens into old Istarian tunnels. I should follow that road and find what is feeding the blackglass.
DIALOGUE_VAUST_STONEWARD_GATE_BLOCKED|Dwarven runes below camp? My sappers are out of their depth. Take that to Throkk Flintvein in Stonecleft; if anyone knows old gate-craft, he does.
DIALOGUE_VAUST_LIFT_NOT_READY|My sappers can brace surface shafts, not open old Istarian roadwork from this side. If Blackglass Cavern drops you into our lift chamber below, secure it; then we can move supplies and wounded through it.
DIALOGUE_VAUST_BREACH_START|You found our lift chamber from below and got it working. Good. I am Captain Vaust Thane. My sappers can hold this shortcut now; use it when you need camp, supplies, or a way back under the hill.\nThe old Istarian road keeps going below, and blackglass thickens the farther it runs. If stone, seal, or dragon-blood magic stops you, come back alive enough to name it.

# English fallback for flesh golem shock-berserk status.
UI_STATUS_BERSERK|Berserk
UI_STATUS_BERSERK_COMPACT|Bsk
UI_INSPECT_MONSTER_STATUS_BERSERK|Berserk: +1 melee attack and +2 damage, but -2 ATK and DEF.
COMBAT_MONSTER_SHOCK_BERSERK|Lightning drives {0} into a berserk surge.
COMBAT_MONSTER_DAMAGE_BERSERK|The {0} surges into a berserk fury.
